/* Lecture 6 video lecture data: chapters, slide start times, timed bilingual transcript (generated). */
window.LEC = {"num":6,"videoBase":"https://wabyking.github.io/nlp2026-videos-2/lecture06/","parts":[{"n":1,"title":"How LLMs Are Trained: Pre-Training, Mid-Training and SFT","blurb":"The three stages of modern LLM training, how SFT differs from pre-training, back-translation for making SFT data, and what imitation alone cannot achieve.","file":"lecture06_part1.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part1.jpg","duration":537.5,"first":1,"last":9,"slides":[{"n":1,"title":"Title: Lecture 6","t":0.8},{"n":2,"title":"Contents","t":69.9},{"n":3,"title":"1 How Are LLMs Trained?","t":146.42},{"n":4,"title":"Three Stages of Modern LLM Training","t":166.02},{"n":5,"title":"Mid-Training in Practice","t":235.19},{"n":6,"title":"Pre-Training vs. SFT","t":310.04},{"n":7,"title":"Back-Translation: Turning Pre-Training Data into SFT Data","t":367.85},{"n":8,"title":"Back-Translation: Turning Pre-Training Data into SFT Data","t":425.91},{"n":9,"title":"From Imitation to Alignment: What SFT Cannot Do","t":473.25}],"sents":[[0.8,3.72,1,"Hello everyone, and welcome to Lecture six.","大家好，欢迎来到第六讲。"],[4.07,8.93,1,"Last time, in Lecture five, we looked at large language models themselves.","上一次，在第五讲，我们研究了大语言模型本身。"],[9.28,17.92,1,"We saw how pre-training on next-token prediction, at enormous scale, gives us a base model that knows a lot about language and about the world.","我们看到，在超大规模上做下一个词预测的预训练，会得到一个对语言和世界都了解很多的基座模型。"],[18.27,21.14,1,"But a base model is not an assistant.","但基座模型并不是一个助手。"],[21.49,32.02,1,"It doesn't reliably follow instructions, it doesn't know when to refuse, and it certainly doesn't sit and think carefully through an olympiad problem.","它不能可靠地遵循指令，不知道什么时候该拒绝，更不会静下心来仔细思考一道奥赛题。"],[32.37,37.85,1,"Today is about the step that closes that gap: post-training with reinforcement learning.","今天讲的就是弥补这一差距的那一步：用强化学习做后训练。"],[38.2,40.82,1,"We'll follow one thread through the whole lecture.","我们会用一条主线贯穿整堂课。"],[41.17,48.56,1,"RL was first used to align models with human preferences, and that's what turned GPT-3 into ChatGPT.","强化学习最早被用来让模型对齐人类偏好，正是它把 GPT-3 变成了 ChatGPT。"],[48.91,59.36,1,"Then the same tool, with rewards coming from automatic checkers instead of people, gave us reasoning models like o1 and DeepSeek-R1.","后来，同样的工具，把奖励来源从人换成自动检查器，就带来了 o1 和 DeepSeek-R1 这样的推理模型。"],[59.71,63.23,1,"And now it's being pushed toward agents that act in the world.","而现在，它正被推向在真实世界中行动的智能体。"],[63.58,68.5,1,"If you want to understand where today's frontier models come from, this is the lecture.","如果你想理解当今最前沿的模型从何而来，这一讲就是答案。"],[69.75,71.29,2,"Here's the roadmap.","这是我们的路线图。"],[71.64,74.58,2,"There are seven parts, grouped into three acts.","一共七个部分，分为三幕。"],[74.93,80.32,2,"The first act is alignment: making the model helpful, honest and harmless.","第一幕是对齐：让模型有用、诚实、无害。"],[80.67,86.02,2,"We start with how LLMs are trained, and why supervised fine-tuning alone isn't enough.","我们先讲大模型是怎么训练的，以及为什么仅靠监督微调还不够。"],[86.37,89.29,2,"Then we build up RLHF and DPO.","然后我们一步步搭建 RLHF 和 DPO。"],[89.64,96.04,2,"And then we open the box of RL algorithms, from PPO all the way to GRPO and DAPO.","接着我们打开强化学习算法这个黑箱，从 PPO 一路讲到 GRPO 和 DAPO。"],[96.39,99.31,2,"The second act is reasoning: making the model think.","第二幕是推理：让模型学会思考。"],[99.66,103.54,2,"We'll look at what large reasoning models like o1 actually do.","我们会看看像 o1 这样的大型推理模型到底在做什么。"],[103.89,110.33,2,"Then the different paths people tried to get there, with DeepSeek-R1 as the turning point.","然后是人们为此尝试过的不同路径，其中 DeepSeek-R1 是转折点。"],[110.68,115.65,2,"And then some of our own work, taking RL beyond math, into medicine and video.","再介绍我们自己的一些工作：把强化学习从数学拓展到医学和视频。"],[116.0,119.37,2,"The third act is agentic RL: making the model act.","第三幕是智能体强化学习：让模型去行动。"],[119.72,124.93,2,"Look at the box on the right, because it's the one idea I want you to carry through the whole lecture.","请看右边这个框，这是我希望你们贯穿整堂课记住的一个核心思想。"],[125.28,129.0,2,"The tool barely changes. It's RL all the way down.","工具几乎不变，自始至终都是强化学习。"],[129.35,132.71,2,"What changes is where the reward comes from.","变化的是奖励从哪里来。"],[133.06,139.8,2,"First from human preferences, then from verifiers, then from tools and environments.","先是来自人类偏好，然后来自验证器，再然后来自工具和环境。"],[140.15,145.02,2,"So keep asking yourself, on every slide: where is the reward coming from?","所以在每一页上，都请不断问自己：奖励是从哪里来的？"],[146.27,147.92,3,"Let's start with part one.","我们从第一部分开始。"],[148.27,152.83,3,"Before we talk about aligning a model, we need a clear picture of the training pipeline.","在讨论如何对齐模型之前，我们需要先清楚地了解整个训练流程。"],[153.18,157.53,3,"What do pre-training, mid-training and supervised fine-tuning already give us?","预训练、中期训练和监督微调已经给了我们什么？"],[157.88,160.99,3,"And where does pure imitation run out of steam?","纯粹的模仿又在哪里后劲不足？"],[161.34,164.62,3,"That gap is exactly where RL enters.","这个缺口，正是强化学习登场的地方。"],[165.87,171.76,4,"Modern LLM training happens in three stages, and it helps to read this table from left to right.","现代大模型的训练分为三个阶段，这张表最好从左往右读。"],[172.11,174.93,4,"Pre-training is where the model gets broad knowledge.","预训练阶段，模型获得广泛的知识。"],[175.28,185.56,4,"It sees trillions of tokens of web, books and code, with Qwen3 at around thirty-six trillion, all with plain next-token prediction.","它会看到数万亿个来自网页、书籍和代码的 token，Qwen3 大约用了三十六万亿，全部用最朴素的下一个词预测。"],[185.91,188.36,4,"This is where almost all the compute goes.","几乎所有的算力都花在这里。"],[188.71,191.82,4,"Mid-training is a newer, more explicit stage.","中期训练是一个较新的、更明确的阶段。"],[192.17,201.36,4,"It's still next-token prediction, but on smaller, curated data: math, code, synthetic chains of thought, long documents, even agent trajectories.","它仍然是下一个词预测，但用的是更小、更精选的数据：数学、代码、合成的思维链、长文档，甚至智能体轨迹。"],[201.71,207.36,4,"Its job is to sharpen the abilities we'll later want to unlock, and to stretch the context window.","它的任务是打磨我们之后想要释放的能力，并拉长上下文窗口。"],[207.71,214.68,4,"Post-training is where the model learns to behave: follow instructions, align, reason, act.","后训练阶段，模型学会该怎么做：遵循指令、对齐、推理、行动。"],[215.03,220.68,4,"It's small in tokens, but RL compute here is growing fast, and that's today's topic.","它用的 token 很少，但这里的强化学习算力增长很快，这正是今天的主题。"],[221.03,223.36,4,"The line at the bottom sums it up.","底部这一行做了总结。"],[223.71,233.79,4,"As we move right, the data gets smaller, cleaner and more task-specific, and the model moves from knowing things to doing things.","越往右，数据越少、越干净、越针对具体任务，模型也从“知道”走向“做到”。"],[235.04,238.98,5,"Why bother with a separate mid-training stage?","为什么要专门设一个中期训练阶段？"],[239.33,245.91,5,"Because it's much cheaper than pre-training, and yet it largely decides what post-training can unlock.","因为它比预训练便宜得多，却在很大程度上决定了后训练能释放出什么。"],[246.26,252.51,5,"Here's a theme you'll hear again later today: RL mostly amplifies abilities the base model already has.","这里有一个今天稍后还会反复出现的主题：强化学习主要是放大基座模型本来就有的能力。"],[252.86,258.83,5,"If the base model has never seen good reasoning or long documents, RL has very little to amplify.","如果基座模型从没见过好的推理或长文档，强化学习就没什么可放大的。"],[259.18,263.88,5,"Look at the right side. Almost every major lab now does something like this.","看右边。现在几乎每个大实验室都在做类似的事情。"],[264.23,273.4,5,"Llama 3 anneals on high-quality code and math at the end of pre-training, and then extends context to one hundred twenty-eight K.","Llama 3 在预训练末期用高质量代码和数学数据做退火，然后把上下文扩展到 128K。"],[273.75,277.04,5,"OLMo 2 names it explicitly as mid-training.","OLMo 2 明确地把它称为中期训练。"],[277.39,281.08,5,"DeepSeek-V3 does staged context extension.","DeepSeek-V3 做分阶段的上下文扩展。"],[281.43,287.07,5,"Qwen3 has a whole stage of about five trillion STEM and reasoning tokens.","Qwen3 有一整个阶段，使用约五万亿 STEM 和推理类 token。"],[287.42,293.96,5,"And GLM-4.5 adds agent trajectories.","GLM-4.5 则加入了智能体轨迹。"],[294.31,304.06,5,"Continued pre-training for a domain, like what we did for HuatuoGPT in medicine or AceGPT for Arabic, is really one form of mid-training too.","面向某个领域的继续预训练，比如我们在医学上做的 HuatuoGPT、在阿拉伯语上做的 AceGPT，其实也是中期训练的一种形式。"],[304.41,308.64,5,"Same idea: prepare the base for the job you want it to do.","思路是一样的：让基座模型为你希望它完成的工作做好准备。"],[309.89,317.06,6,"Now let's zoom into the first step of post-training, supervised fine-tuning, and compare it with pre-training.","现在我们聚焦后训练的第一步，监督微调，并把它和预训练做个比较。"],[317.41,321.12,6,"The objective is the same: predicting the next token.","目标是一样的：预测下一个词。"],[321.47,325.22,6,"What changes is the data, and where you put the loss.","变化的是数据，以及损失计算在哪里。"],[325.57,328.58,6,"In pre-training, every token in the corpus counts.","在预训练中，语料里的每个 token 都要算损失。"],[328.93,337.49,6,"In SFT, the data is structured as instruction, input and output, and we only compute the loss on the output tokens.","在 SFT 中，数据被组织成指令、输入、输出三元组，我们只在输出 token 上计算损失。"],[337.84,345.31,6,"We don't want the model to learn to write instructions. We want it to learn to answer them, conditioned on the instruction.","我们不希望模型学会写指令，而是希望它在给定指令的条件下学会回答。"],[345.66,347.14,6,"The other difference is scale.","另一个区别是规模。"],[347.49,354.35,6,"Pre-training uses trillions of tokens, while SFT typically uses thousands to millions of examples.","预训练用的是数万亿 token，而 SFT 通常只用几千到几百万个样本。"],[354.7,358.41,6,"That's a big hint: SFT isn't teaching much new knowledge.","这是一个很重要的提示：SFT 并没有教给模型多少新知识。"],[358.76,366.45,6,"It mostly teaches the model the format and style of being an assistant, on top of what it already knows.","它主要是在模型已有知识的基础上，教会它当一个助手的格式和风格。"],[367.7,372.64,7,"Here's a practical trick that blurs the line between the two stages: back-translation.","这里有一个模糊两个阶段界限的实用技巧：反向翻译。"],[372.99,379.75,7,"The idea, from instruction back-translation, is that any piece of good text is the answer to some question.","这个想法来自指令反向翻译：任何一段好的文本，都是某个问题的答案。"],[380.1,384.92,7,"So you take a document, and ask an LLM to write the question it answers.","所以你拿来一篇文档，让大模型写出它所回答的那个问题。"],[385.27,388.78,7,"This figure is from our HuatuoGPT-II work.","这张图来自我们的 HuatuoGPT-II 工作。"],[389.13,398.14,7,"On the top path, we took about five point two million Chinese and English documents: books, web pages, encyclopedias and medical literature.","在上面这条路径上，我们收集了约五百二十万篇中英文文档：书籍、网页、百科和医学文献。"],[398.49,403.43,7,"We used an LLM to turn each one into an instruction and answer pair.","我们用大模型把每一篇都转成一个指令和答案对。"],[403.78,410.03,7,"On the bottom path, real medical questions were answered with GPT-4 to make fine-tuning data.","在下面这条路径上，真实的医学问题由 GPT-4 作答，构成微调数据。"],[410.38,414.17,7,"Then both streams were mixed in a single stage of training.","然后两路数据混合在一起，进行单阶段训练。"],[414.52,419.9,7,"The point is that pre-training data and SFT data don't have to live in separate worlds.","关键在于，预训练数据和 SFT 数据不必分属两个世界。"],[420.25,424.51,7,"You can transform one into the other, and train in one go.","你可以把一种转换成另一种，一次性完成训练。"],[425.76,428.64,8,"Here's what one of those transformed examples looks like.","这是其中一个转换后样本的样子。"],[428.99,434.73,8,"The raw data is a passage from an English medical textbook about Alzheimer's disease.","原始数据是一段英文医学教科书中关于阿尔茨海默病的文字。"],[435.08,442.97,8,"After data unification, it becomes a Chinese question: what are the main clinical and pathological features of Alzheimer's disease?","经过数据统一之后，它变成了一个中文问题：阿尔茨海默病的主要临床和病理特征是什么？"],[443.32,448.3,8,"And a Chinese answer that carries the same knowledge as the original passage.","以及一个中文答案，承载着与原文相同的知识。"],[448.65,455.72,8,"Notice what happened. The knowledge came from the textbook, not from a model's imagination, so it's grounded.","注意这里发生了什么：知识来自教科书，而不是模型的想象，所以它是有依据的。"],[456.07,460.39,8,"And the format is now question and answer, which matches how the model will be used.","而且格式变成了问答，和模型实际的使用方式一致。"],[460.74,464.6,8,"That's why the slide says learning becomes more knowledge-intensive.","这就是为什么这页说，学习变得更加知识密集。"],[464.95,471.85,8,"So SFT is powerful and flexible. But it still has a ceiling, and that's what comes next.","所以 SFT 强大又灵活，但它仍然有天花板，这就是接下来要讲的。"],[473.1,478.54,9,"Here are four things SFT fundamentally can't do, and each one points toward RL.","SFT 有四件事从根本上做不到，而每一件都指向强化学习。"],[478.89,482.0,9,"First, it only sees positive examples.","第一，它只看到正例。"],[482.35,488.62,9,"It's told what to say, never what not to say, so it has no idea that one answer is worse than another.","它只被告知该说什么，从不被告知不该说什么，所以它不知道一个答案比另一个更差。"],[488.97,491.82,9,"Second, it's bounded by the demonstrator.","第二，它受限于示范者。"],[492.17,498.17,9,"Imitate a teacher, and you copy their errors and biases, and it's hard to surpass them.","模仿一位老师，你就会复制他的错误和偏见，而且很难超越他。"],[498.52,501.61,9,"Third, writing ideal answers is expensive.","第三，写出理想答案的成本很高。"],[501.96,509.72,9,"Experts take ages to write a perfect response, but anyone can quickly say which of two responses is better.","专家要花很长时间才能写出完美的回答，但任何人都能很快判断两个回答哪个更好。"],[510.07,512.52,9,"Fourth, there's an objective mismatch.","第四，目标不匹配。"],[512.87,520.65,9,"Token-level likelihood isn't what we actually want. We want answers that are helpful, honest and harmless.","token 级别的似然并不是我们真正想要的。我们想要的是有用、诚实、无害的回答。"],[521.0,527.45,9,"So the fix is on the right: stop imitating, and optimize directly for what humans prefer.","所以解决办法在右边：不再模仿，而是直接针对人类的偏好去优化。"],[527.8,531.04,9,"Humans only have to compare, not write.","人类只需要比较，而不需要撰写。"],[531.39,535.7,9,"That's reinforcement learning from human feedback, and it's part two.","这就是基于人类反馈的强化学习，也就是第二部分。"]]},{"n":2,"title":"Alignment via RLHF: From Summaries to ChatGPT","blurb":"Helpful, honest and harmless as alignment goals, why comparisons beat scores, the three-step RLHF recipe, and how InstructGPT and ChatGPT scaled it up.","file":"lecture06_part2.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part2.jpg","duration":1045.3,"first":10,"last":29,"slides":[{"n":10,"title":"2 Alignment via RLHF","t":0.8},{"n":11,"title":"Motivation: Alignment — the Three H's of Model Desiderata","t":28.47},{"n":12,"title":"Helpful: Solve the User's Actual Task","t":74.66},{"n":13,"title":"Honest: Be Truthful and Calibrated","t":128.86},{"n":14,"title":"Harmless: Avoid Harm — Without Over-Refusing","t":192.54},{"n":15,"title":"Benefits of RLHF","t":246.73},{"n":16,"title":"RLHF in Practice: Example Responses","t":304.6},{"n":17,"title":"2.2 The RLHF Recipe","t":359.81},{"n":18,"title":"RLHF: Learning to Summarize from Human Feedback","t":383.44},{"n":19,"title":"Optimizing for Human Preferences","t":430.56},{"n":20,"title":"Reinforcement Learning to the Rescue","t":498.13},{"n":21,"title":"Modeling Human Preferences (1): Humans Are Expensive","t":554.79},{"n":22,"title":"Modeling Human Preferences (2): Scores Are Noisy, Comparisons Are Not","t":606.04},{"n":23,"title":"An Overall Picture of RLHF","t":662.06},{"n":24,"title":"RLHF in Three Steps","t":714.87},{"n":25,"title":"RLHF Provides Gains over Pre-Training + Fine-Tuning","t":781.89},{"n":26,"title":"InstructGPT: Scaling Up RLHF to Tens of Thousands of Tasks","t":840.69},{"n":27,"title":"InstructGPT: Where Do the Prompts Come From?","t":891.99},{"n":28,"title":"ChatGPT: Instruction Fine-Tuning + RLHF for Dialog Agents","t":949.91},{"n":29,"title":"ChatGPT: Instruction Fine-Tuning + RLHF for Dialog Agents","t":993.57}],"sents":[[0.8,9.68,10,"So, to close part one: SFT gives the model the format of an assistant, but not a sense of which answers are actually better.","那么，第一部分小结一下：SFT 给了模型助手的格式，却没有让它知道哪些回答真正更好。"],[10.03,17.98,10,"A pre-trained model just continues text. An assistant has to be helpful, honest and harmless.","预训练模型只会续写文本，而助手必须有用、诚实、无害。"],[18.33,23.55,10,"Part two asks how we specify that goal through human feedback, and how we train toward it.","第二部分要问的是：我们如何通过人类反馈来定义这个目标，以及如何朝它训练。"],[23.9,27.07,10,"And then, where that feedback falls short.","然后再看，这种反馈在哪些地方力有不逮。"],[28.32,33.05,11,"Let's begin with the goal itself: what does it mean for a model to be aligned?","我们从目标本身说起：一个模型“对齐”了，到底意味着什么？"],[33.4,39.17,11,"The most common answer is the three H's, from Askell and colleagues at Anthropic.","最常见的答案是“三个 H”，出自 Anthropic 的 Askell 等人。"],[39.52,42.55,11,"Helpful means actually solving the user's task.","有用，意味着真正解决用户的任务。"],[42.9,49.85,11,"Honest means giving accurate information, and saying when you don't know, instead of making something up.","诚实，意味着给出准确的信息，不知道时就说不知道，而不是编造。"],[50.2,54.9,11,"Harmless means not causing physical, psychological or social harm.","无害，意味着不造成身体、心理或社会层面的伤害。"],[55.25,60.51,11,"These sound obvious, but notice that none of them is something you can write down as a loss function.","这些听起来显而易见，但请注意，没有一条能写成损失函数。"],[60.86,62.98,11,"There's no formula for helpfulness.","“有用”是没有公式的。"],[63.33,68.13,11,"That's precisely why we'll end up needing human judgments to define the target.","这正是为什么我们最终需要用人类的判断来定义目标。"],[68.48,73.26,11,"Over the next three slides, let's make each H concrete with examples.","接下来三页，我们用例子把每个 H 讲具体。"],[74.51,78.72,12,"Start with helpful. The top example is a classic.","先看“有用”。上面这个例子很经典。"],[79.07,86.09,12,"Ask the original GPT-3 to explain the moon landing to a six-year-old, and it just continues the pattern.","让最初的 GPT-3 给六岁小孩解释登月，它只会顺着模式往下续写。"],[86.44,93.31,12,"It produces more prompts like it: explain gravity to a six-year-old, explain relativity.","它生成了更多类似的提示：给六岁小孩解释引力，解释相对论。"],[93.66,96.76,12,"It's a document completer, not an assistant.","它是一个文档补全器，而不是助手。"],[97.11,103.58,12,"InstructGPT, after SFT and RLHF, actually answers the question in simple words.","而经过 SFT 和 RLHF 的 InstructGPT，真的用简单的话回答了这个问题。"],[103.93,105.82,12,"The second example is subtler.","第二个例子更微妙。"],[106.17,113.49,12,"Both answers to the KeyError question are true, but the first one is useless. It just defines the error.","关于 KeyError 的两个回答都是对的，但第一个毫无用处，它只是给这个错误下了个定义。"],[113.84,118.97,12,"The helpful one diagnoses the problem, gives concrete fixes, and invites a follow-up.","有用的那个回答诊断了问题、给出具体的修复办法，还邀请用户继续追问。"],[119.32,121.57,12,"So helpfulness isn't just correctness.","所以，有用不仅仅是正确。"],[121.92,127.46,12,"It means understanding the intent behind the request, and giving something you can actually act on.","它意味着理解请求背后的意图，并给出能真正付诸行动的内容。"],[128.71,132.1,13,"Next, honest. There are two failure modes here.","接下来是“诚实”。这里有两种失败模式。"],[132.45,137.25,13,"In the first example, the question has a false premise: nobody has walked on Mars.","第一个例子里，问题本身有一个错误前提：没有人在火星上行走过。"],[137.6,143.42,13,"A model that just wants to sound fluent happily invents an answer about Neil Armstrong on Mars.","一个只想显得流畅的模型，会兴致勃勃地编出阿姆斯特朗登上火星的答案。"],[143.77,146.01,13,"The honest answer corrects the premise.","诚实的回答会纠正这个前提。"],[146.36,151.1,13,"The second one is even more dangerous: fabricated citations.","第二个更危险：伪造的引用。"],[151.45,159.07,13,"The bad answer gives two references that look perfectly real, with authors, venues and years, and are completely made up.","糟糕的回答给出两篇看起来完全真实的参考文献，有作者、会议和年份，却完全是编造的。"],[159.42,162.1,13,"They're deliberately fake on this slide.","这页上的这两条引用是故意伪造的。"],[162.45,170.78,13,"The good answer says what it actually knows, gives the one real number it can stand behind, and asks you to verify citations.","好的回答只说它真正知道的，给出它能负责的那一个真实数据，并提醒你去核实引用。"],[171.13,178.92,13,"That real number is from InstructGPT: fewer hallucinations on closed-domain tasks, twenty-one versus forty-one percent.","这个真实数据来自 InstructGPT：在封闭领域任务上幻觉更少，百分之二十一对百分之四十一。"],[179.27,181.77,13,"Keep this fake-reference example in mind.","请记住这个伪造引用的例子。"],[182.12,191.14,13,"A bit later we'll see that fake references don't just mislead users. They also fool the judges we use to train reward models.","稍后我们会看到，伪造的引用不仅会误导用户，还会骗过我们用来训练奖励模型的评判者。"],[192.39,194.51,14,"And the third H, harmless.","然后是第三个 H，无害。"],[194.86,199.7,14,"The first example is clear: helping someone break into their neighbour's Wi-Fi is harmful.","第一个例子很清楚：帮人侵入邻居的 Wi-Fi 是有害的。"],[200.05,204.17,14,"A good answer declines, and offers a legal alternative.","好的回答会拒绝，并提供一个合法的替代方案。"],[204.52,208.83,14,"But look at the second example, because it's the other side of the coin.","但请看第二个例子，因为它是硬币的另一面。"],[209.18,213.23,14,"Killing a stuck Python process is a completely normal request.","结束一个卡住的 Python 进程，是一个完全正常的请求。"],[213.58,219.52,14,"A model that refuses because it sees the word kill is safe, but useless.","一个因为看到 kill 这个词就拒绝的模型，是安全的，但毫无用处。"],[219.87,223.37,14,"That's over-refusal, and users find it really annoying.","这叫过度拒绝，用户会觉得非常烦人。"],[223.72,227.42,14,"So the three H's pull against each other.","所以这三个 H 之间是相互拉扯的。"],[227.77,233.29,14,"Be too cautious and you're unhelpful. Be too compliant and you're harmful.","太谨慎就没用，太顺从就有害。"],[233.64,236.27,14,"There's no simple rule that draws this line correctly.","没有哪条简单的规则能正确地划出这条线。"],[236.62,245.33,14,"And that's the key motivation for RLHF: we let the model learn where the line is from many human comparisons, rather than hand-writing rules.","这正是 RLHF 的关键动机：让模型从大量人类比较中学会这条线在哪里，而不是手写规则。"],[246.58,252.6,15,"Here's what this looked like in practice when ChatGPT came out, compared with the earlier InstructGPT model.","这是 ChatGPT 刚推出时的实际表现，与更早的 InstructGPT 模型做的对比。"],[252.95,257.83,15,"Read the first row: ask about Christopher Columbus coming to the US in two thousand fifteen.","看第一行：问的是哥伦布在 2015 年来到美国的事。"],[258.18,263.38,15,"InstructGPT just goes along with it, saying he was very excited to be here.","InstructGPT 直接顺着说，说他来到这里非常兴奋。"],[263.73,270.84,15,"ChatGPT points out the false premise, since Columbus died in fifteen oh six, and then plays along with the hypothetical.","ChatGPT 指出了错误前提，因为哥伦布死于 1506 年，然后再配合这个假设往下讲。"],[271.19,272.13,15,"That's honesty.","这就是诚实。"],[272.48,275.89,15,"The second and third rows are about harmlessness.","第二行和第三行是关于无害性的。"],[276.24,283.1,15,"Asked for a gory story glorifying pain, or how to bully someone, InstructGPT simply complies.","被要求写一个美化痛苦的血腥故事，或者问如何欺负别人，InstructGPT 直接照做。"],[283.45,286.83,15,"ChatGPT declines, and explains why.","ChatGPT 则拒绝了，并解释了原因。"],[287.18,296.77,15,"The underlying recipe is the same family, SFT plus RLHF, but with more and better preference data the behaviour shifts noticeably.","底层方法属于同一家族，也就是 SFT 加 RLHF，但有了更多更好的偏好数据，行为就有了明显改变。"],[297.12,303.2,15,"These are OpenAI's own examples, so take them as illustrations rather than a benchmark.","这些是 OpenAI 自己挑的例子，所以把它们当作示例，而不是基准测试。"],[304.45,310.16,16,"And here's a vivid example from twenty twenty-three chat assistants, in Chinese.","这里还有一个来自 2023 年聊天助手的生动中文例子。"],[310.51,317.64,16,"The user asks for a letter to their daughter, who has bad grades, with the title: you are truly worthless.","用户要求给成绩不好的女儿写一封信，标题是《你真的毫无价值》。"],[317.99,324.51,16,"On the left, the assistant follows the instruction literally, and writes a genuinely hurtful letter to a child.","左边的助手逐字照办，写了一封真正伤害孩子的信。"],[324.86,332.41,16,"On the right, the GPT-4 response recognises that this could cause real psychological harm, and gently pushes back.","右边，GPT-4 的回答意识到这可能造成真正的心理伤害，于是温和地提出异议。"],[332.76,337.18,16,"It offers a letter with a different title, roughly: believe in your potential.","它提供了一封换了标题的信，大意是《相信你的潜力》。"],[337.53,341.26,16,"This is a nice illustration of why alignment is hard.","这很好地说明了为什么对齐很难。"],[341.61,349.19,16,"The left response is, in a narrow sense, very instruction-following. But it fails on harmlessness.","左边的回答在狭义上非常遵循指令，但它在无害性上失败了。"],[349.54,353.36,16,"Getting this right needs judgment about the person behind the request.","要做对这件事，需要对请求背后的那个人有所判断。"],[353.71,358.41,16,"And that kind of judgment is what human feedback is meant to teach.","而这种判断，正是人类反馈想要教会模型的。"],[359.66,364.86,17,"We now know what we want. The question for this subsection is how to train for it.","现在我们知道想要什么了。这一小节的问题是：怎么朝这个目标训练。"],[365.21,366.74,17,"There are two obstacles.","这里有两个障碍。"],[367.09,372.57,17,"Human scores are not differentiable, and humans are too expensive to put in the training loop.","人类打分不可微，而且让人参与训练循环的成本太高。"],[372.92,382.04,17,"The answer is to learn a reward model from human comparisons, and then optimize the policy against it with RL.","解决办法是：先从人类的比较中学出一个奖励模型，再用强化学习针对它优化策略。"],[383.29,389.86,18,"Here's the basic picture from OpenAI's twenty twenty work on learning to summarize from human feedback.","这是 OpenAI 在 2020 年“从人类反馈中学习摘要”工作中的基本框架。"],[390.21,394.14,18,"It's the paper that really kicked off modern RLHF.","正是这篇论文真正开启了现代 RLHF。"],[394.49,400.6,18,"The key sentence is at the top: it's often much easier to compare answers than to write them.","关键的一句话在最上面：比较答案往往比写答案容易得多。"],[400.95,408.27,18,"So the loop goes like this. Sample many prompts, and let the initial language model generate several outputs.","所以流程是这样的：采样很多提示，让初始语言模型生成多个输出。"],[408.62,410.45,18,"Then have humans rank them.","然后让人类对它们进行排序。"],[410.8,415.8,18,"Then train a reward model, the pink box, to predict those human preferences.","接着训练一个奖励模型，也就是粉色的框，去预测这些人类偏好。"],[416.15,419.84,18,"That reward model becomes a stand-in for the human.","这个奖励模型就成了人类的替身。"],[420.19,423.29,18,"Over the next few slides we'll build this up from scratch.","接下来几页，我们会从零开始把它搭建起来。"],[423.64,429.16,18,"We start with the most basic question: why can't we just directly maximise the human score?","先从最基本的问题开始：为什么不能直接最大化人类打分？"],[430.41,432.42,19,"Let's set up the problem concretely.","我们把问题具体地设定一下。"],[432.77,437.06,19,"We have an article, and a language model that writes summaries.","我们有一篇文章，还有一个写摘要的语言模型。"],[437.41,442.57,19,"Here a human gives the first summary a score of eight, because it's accurate.","这里，人给第一个摘要打了八分，因为它准确。"],[442.92,446.61,19,"And the second one gets one point two, because it's off-topic.","第二个只得了一点二分，因为它跑题了。"],[446.96,456.16,19,"Our goal is the formula in the first box: choose parameters theta to maximize the expected human score of the summaries the model samples.","我们的目标就是第一个框里的公式：选择参数 theta，使模型采样出的摘要的期望人类打分最大。"],[456.51,458.38,19,"Why not just backpropagate?","为什么不直接反向传播？"],[458.73,464.46,19,"Because R of s is a number typed in by a person. It's not a function of theta.","因为 R(s) 是一个人敲进去的数字，它不是 theta 的函数。"],[464.81,470.66,19,"And sampling words is discrete, so there's no gradient flowing from the score back to the model.","而且采样词语是离散的，所以没有梯度能从分数流回模型。"],[471.01,473.03,19,"The way out is policy gradient.","出路就是策略梯度。"],[473.38,481.45,19,"The gradient of the expected reward equals the expected value of the reward, times the gradient of the log-probability of the sample.","期望奖励的梯度，等于奖励乘以样本对数概率梯度的期望。"],[481.8,486.52,19,"In words: you don't need the gradient of the score, only the score itself.","换句话说：你不需要分数的梯度，只需要分数本身。"],[486.87,492.0,19,"Push up the log-probability of samples in proportion to how well they scored.","按样本得分的高低，按比例提高它们的对数概率。"],[492.35,496.73,19,"Make high-scoring summaries more likely. That's really all RL is doing here.","让高分摘要更可能被生成。强化学习在这里做的，其实就这么多。"],[497.98,500.49,20,"RL itself is not new.","强化学习本身并不新。"],[500.84,510.33,20,"The basic policy gradient method, REINFORCE, is from Williams in nineteen ninety-two, and Sutton and Barto's textbook is from nineteen ninety-eight.","基本的策略梯度方法 REINFORCE 出自 Williams 1992 年的工作，Sutton 和 Barto 的教科书出版于 1998 年。"],[510.68,515.43,20,"Around twenty thirteen, deep RL had a big revival with Atari game-playing.","大约在 2013 年，深度强化学习凭借玩 Atari 游戏迎来了一次大复兴。"],[515.78,526.52,20,"But applying RL to modern language models is much more recent, starting around twenty nineteen to twenty twenty-two, with Ziegler, Stiennon and then InstructGPT.","但把强化学习用于现代语言模型要晚得多，大约从 2019 年到 2022 年才开始，代表工作有 Ziegler、Stiennon，然后是 InstructGPT。"],[526.87,527.79,20,"Why the delay?","为什么这么晚？"],[528.14,534.32,20,"Mostly because RL with language models was, and honestly still is, hard to get right.","主要是因为在语言模型上做强化学习，过去很难做好，说实话现在依然很难。"],[534.67,537.46,20,"It's unstable, and easy to break.","它不稳定，很容易崩。"],[537.81,546.04,20,"What made it practical were algorithms like PPO, from twenty seventeen, that keep updates stable even for large neural networks.","让它变得可行的是像 PPO 这样的算法，它出自 2017 年，即使对大型神经网络也能保持更新稳定。"],[546.39,553.39,20,"We'll open up PPO properly in part three. For now, let's finish building the RLHF pipeline.","我们会在第三部分好好拆解 PPO。现在先把 RLHF 的流程搭完。"],[554.64,562.53,21,"Here's the first practical problem: RL needs millions of scored samples, and we can't have a human score every single one.","第一个实际问题是：强化学习需要数百万个打过分的样本，我们不可能让人逐一打分。"],[562.88,568.47,21,"The solution is to treat what would a human say as its own NLP problem.","解决办法是：把“人会怎么打分”当作一个独立的 NLP 问题。"],[568.82,573.86,21,"Step one: collect human scores once, for a reasonable number of samples.","第一步：针对适量的样本，一次性收集人类打分。"],[574.21,579.93,21,"Step two: train a reward model that takes a piece of text and predicts that score.","第二步：训练一个奖励模型，输入一段文本，预测出这个分数。"],[580.28,587.5,21,"After that, any new summary can be scored instantly, here six point three, without a human in the loop.","之后，任何新的摘要都能被立刻打分，比如这里的六点三分，而不需要人参与。"],[587.85,590.8,21,"Notice that the reward model is just a text regressor.","请注意，奖励模型只是一个文本回归器。"],[591.15,598.21,21,"And it's usually initialized from the language model itself, so it starts with a good understanding of language.","而且它通常用语言模型本身来初始化，所以一开始就对语言有很好的理解。"],[598.56,604.64,21,"But there's a second problem hidden here: are those human scores reliable in the first place?","但这里还藏着第二个问题：这些人类打分本身可靠吗？"],[605.89,608.31,22,"They're not, and this slide shows why.","并不可靠，这一页说明了原因。"],[608.66,614.0,22,"Give the same summary to three annotators, and you might get eight, five and nine.","把同一个摘要交给三位标注者，你可能得到八分、五分和九分。"],[614.35,619.61,22,"Everyone has their own scale, and even one person's scale drifts over a long labeling session.","每个人都有自己的尺度，而且同一个人的尺度在长时间标注中也会漂移。"],[619.96,624.39,22,"But ask which of these is better, and people agree far more.","但如果问“哪个更好”，人们的一致性就高得多。"],[624.74,627.06,22,"Here, s one is accurate.","这里，s1 是准确的。"],[627.41,631.91,22,"S three is fluent but wrong, since it claims massive damage.","s3 很流畅但是错的，因为它声称造成了巨大破坏。"],[632.26,633.78,22,"And s two is off-topic.","而 s2 跑题了。"],[634.13,636.3,22,"Most people will rank them the same way.","大多数人都会给出同样的排序。"],[636.65,640.79,22,"So we collect comparisons and fit a Bradley-Terry model.","所以我们收集比较数据，并拟合一个 Bradley-Terry 模型。"],[641.14,648.2,22,"The formula says the probability that the winner is preferred over the loser is the sigmoid of the difference in their reward scores.","公式表示：胜者被偏好于败者的概率，等于两者奖励分数之差的 sigmoid。"],[648.55,653.4,22,"Only differences matter, so each annotator's private scale simply drops out.","只有差值才重要，所以每个标注者自己的尺度就被抵消掉了。"],[653.75,660.66,22,"We train the reward model to make that probability high for the pairs humans actually preferred.","我们训练奖励模型，让人类实际偏好的那些配对，这个概率尽可能高。"],[661.91,667.99,23,"Here's the full loop from the summarization paper, in three panels, and it's worth tracing once.","这是摘要论文中完整的流程，分三栏，值得完整走一遍。"],[668.34,670.74,23,"Panel one, collect human feedback.","第一栏，收集人类反馈。"],[671.09,678.13,23,"Take a Reddit post, sample several summaries from various policies, pick two, and a human says which is better.","取一篇 Reddit 帖子，用多种策略采样若干摘要，选出两个，让人判断哪个更好。"],[678.48,681.01,23,"Panel two, train the reward model.","第二栏，训练奖励模型。"],[681.36,684.43,23,"Feed both summaries in, and get two scores.","把两个摘要都输入进去，得到两个分数。"],[684.78,687.68,23,"Then use the loss on the log-sigmoid of their difference.","然后用它们差值的 log-sigmoid 来计算损失。"],[688.03,692.27,23,"That's exactly the Bradley-Terry loss from the previous slide.","这正是上一页讲的 Bradley-Terry 损失。"],[692.62,695.48,23,"Panel three, train the policy with PPO.","第三栏，用 PPO 训练策略。"],[695.83,702.84,23,"Sample a new post, the policy writes a summary, the reward model scores it, and that reward updates the policy.","采样一篇新帖子，策略写出摘要，奖励模型给它打分，这个奖励再用来更新策略。"],[703.19,710.41,23,"Notice that the dashed arrows only go back to the reward model in panel two, and to the policy in panel three.","注意，虚线箭头在第二栏只指回奖励模型，在第三栏只指回策略。"],[710.76,713.47,23,"The human is only needed in panel one.","只有第一栏需要人。"],[714.72,720.15,24,"Let's compress all of that into three steps you should be able to say from memory.","我们把这些压缩成三个步骤，你们应该能脱口而出。"],[720.5,728.9,24,"Step one, imitate: labelers write good answers and we do SFT, giving us a reference model, pi ref.","第一步，模仿：标注员写出好的答案，我们做 SFT，得到参考模型 pi ref。"],[729.25,736.73,24,"Step two, learn to judge: sample several answers per prompt, humans rank them, and we train a reward model.","第二步，学会评判：每个提示采样多个答案，人来排序，我们训练出奖励模型。"],[737.08,745.3,24,"Step three, optimize: the policy writes answers, the reward model scores them, and PPO pushes up the high-scoring ones.","第三步，优化：策略写出答案，奖励模型打分，PPO 提升高分答案的概率。"],[745.65,749.02,24,"The objective for step three is the formula in the middle.","第三步的目标就是中间这个公式。"],[749.37,751.52,24,"The first term says: get high reward.","第一项说的是：拿到高奖励。"],[751.87,757.31,24,"The second term, beta times the KL divergence from the reference model, is a leash.","第二项，beta 乘以与参考模型之间的 KL 散度，是一根牵引绳。"],[757.66,763.59,24,"Without it, the policy will drift into weird text that happens to fool the reward model.","没有它，策略就会漂向一些恰好能骗过奖励模型的怪异文本。"],[763.94,769.35,24,"With it, the model stays close to the sensible SFT model while improving.","有了它，模型在提升的同时，会保持在合理的 SFT 模型附近。"],[769.7,771.82,24,"Beta controls how long the leash is.","beta 控制这根绳子有多长。"],[772.17,776.97,24,"And remember the last line: humans are only needed in steps one and two.","还要记住最后一行：只有第一步和第二步需要人。"],[777.32,780.49,24,"Step three can run millions of times without them.","第三步可以在没有人的情况下运行数百万次。"],[781.74,786.12,25,"Does it actually work? Here's the headline result from the summarization paper.","它真的有效吗？这是摘要论文中最重要的结果。"],[786.47,793.09,25,"The y-axis is how often humans prefer the model's summary over the human-written reference summaries.","纵轴是人类更偏好模型摘要、而不是人写参考摘要的比例。"],[793.44,798.13,25,"So the dashed line at zero point five means as good as the reference.","所以零点五处的虚线，表示和参考摘要一样好。"],[798.48,800.52,25,"The x-axis is model size.","横轴是模型规模。"],[800.87,802.2,25,"Look at the three curves.","看这三条曲线。"],[802.55,805.42,25,"Pretrain-only, in blue, is far below.","只做预训练的蓝色曲线远远落在下面。"],[805.77,814.19,25,"Supervised fine-tuning, in green, improves with size, but stays below zero point five even at twelve point nine billion parameters.","绿色的监督微调随规模提升，但即使在一百二十九亿参数时仍低于零点五。"],[814.54,822.52,25,"The RLHF model, in orange, is above zero point five already at one point three billion, and keeps going up.","橙色的 RLHF 模型在十三亿参数时就已超过零点五，而且还在继续上升。"],[822.87,832.89,25,"So a small model trained with human feedback beat much larger supervised models, and even beat the human reference summaries.","所以，用人类反馈训练的小模型，打败了大得多的监督模型，甚至超过了人写的参考摘要。"],[833.24,839.29,25,"That's a strong argument that optimizing for preferences gives you something imitation doesn't.","这有力地说明，针对偏好去优化，能带来模仿所给不了的东西。"],[840.54,852.93,26,"InstructGPT, in twenty twenty-two, took this exact recipe, and scaled it from one task, summarization, to the huge variety of things people ask GPT-3 to do.","2022 年的 InstructGPT 采用了完全相同的方法，把它从摘要这一个任务，扩展到人们让 GPT-3 做的各种各样的事情。"],[853.28,856.09,26,"The three steps are the ones we just built.","这三个步骤就是我们刚刚搭建的那些。"],[856.44,865.08,26,"Step one: a labeler demonstrates the desired answer, here explaining the moon landing to a six-year-old, and GPT-3 is fine-tuned on it.","第一步：标注员示范期望的答案，这里是给六岁小孩解释登月，然后在这些数据上微调 GPT-3。"],[865.43,875.21,26,"Step two: several model outputs are sampled, and a labeler ranks them, here D better than C, better than A equals B, to train the reward model.","第二步：采样模型的多个输出，由标注员排序，这里是 D 优于 C、C 优于 A、A 等于 B，用来训练奖励模型。"],[875.56,883.16,26,"Step three: PPO optimizes the policy against that reward model, on new prompts like writing a story about frogs.","第三步：在新的提示上，比如写一个关于青蛙的故事，PPO 针对这个奖励模型优化策略。"],[883.51,890.59,26,"This figure is probably the most reproduced diagram in the history of LLM alignment, so it's worth knowing well.","这张图大概是大模型对齐史上被转载最多的图，值得好好掌握。"],[891.84,895.05,27,"A natural question is: where did the prompts come from?","一个很自然的问题是：这些提示从哪里来？"],[895.4,896.63,27,"There are three sources.","有三个来源。"],[896.98,905.47,27,"Labelers inventing diverse tasks, labelers writing few-shot style prompts, and real use cases from people on the OpenAI API waitlist.","标注员自己设计多样化任务，标注员编写少样本风格的提示，以及来自 OpenAI API 候补名单用户的真实用例。"],[905.82,907.16,27,"Look at the chart on the right.","看右边的图表。"],[907.51,914.24,27,"Generation dominates at about forty-six percent, then open QA, brainstorming and chat.","生成类任务占主导，约百分之四十六，其次是开放问答、头脑风暴和聊天。"],[914.59,918.79,27,"Closed-form things like classification and extraction are small.","像分类和抽取这样有固定答案的任务占比很小。"],[919.14,922.99,27,"That's important: most real requests have no single correct answer.","这一点很重要：大多数真实请求都没有唯一的正确答案。"],[923.34,928.17,27,"And that's exactly why you need human preferences rather than an answer key.","这正是为什么你需要人类偏好，而不是标准答案。"],[928.52,937.72,27,"Also look at the numbers at the bottom: about thirteen thousand prompts for SFT, thirty-three thousand for the reward model, and thirty-one thousand for PPO.","再看底部的数字：SFT 约一万三千个提示，奖励模型约三万三千个，PPO 约三万一千个。"],[938.07,941.75,27,"Compared with trillions of pre-training tokens, that's tiny.","和数万亿的预训练 token 相比，这实在太少了。"],[942.1,948.51,27,"A small amount of carefully collected human feedback changes the model's behaviour a lot.","少量精心收集的人类反馈，就能大幅改变模型的行为。"],[949.76,951.57,28,"And then, ChatGPT.","然后是 ChatGPT。"],[951.92,958.45,28,"OpenAI never published a paper for it, and kept most details secret, as the note on the left says.","OpenAI 从未为它发表论文，而且对大部分细节保密，正如左边的注释所说。"],[958.8,964.84,28,"But the blog post describes the method, and it's essentially InstructGPT adapted for dialogue.","但博客文章描述了方法，它本质上就是针对对话改造过的 InstructGPT。"],[965.19,969.16,28,"This first excerpt is the instruction fine-tuning part.","第一段摘录讲的是指令微调部分。"],[969.51,978.58,28,"Human AI trainers wrote conversations where they played both sides, the user and the assistant, with model-written suggestions to help them.","人类 AI 训练师编写对话，同时扮演用户和助手双方，并借助模型写的建议来辅助。"],[978.93,985.14,28,"That new dialogue data was mixed with the InstructGPT data, converted into dialogue format.","这些新的对话数据与 InstructGPT 的数据混合，后者被转换成了对话格式。"],[985.49,992.17,28,"So step one of the recipe is unchanged, just with multi-turn conversations instead of single prompts.","所以配方的第一步没变，只是用多轮对话取代了单轮提示。"],[993.42,997.58,29,"And here's the RLHF part of the same blog post.","这是同一篇博客中的 RLHF 部分。"],[997.93,1003.35,29,"To build the reward model, they took real conversations that trainers had with the chatbot.","为了构建奖励模型，他们选取了训练师与聊天机器人的真实对话。"],[1003.7,1008.68,29,"They picked a model message, sampled several alternatives, and had trainers rank them.","他们挑出一条模型消息，采样几个替代回复，再让训练师排序。"],[1009.03,1013.97,29,"Then they fine-tuned with PPO, and repeated this for several iterations.","然后用 PPO 微调，并重复了好几轮。"],[1014.32,1016.41,29,"That iteration is worth noticing.","这种迭代值得注意。"],[1016.76,1023.84,29,"Each round, the comparisons come from the current model's own outputs, so the reward model keeps up with the policy.","每一轮的比较数据都来自当前模型自己的输出，所以奖励模型能跟上策略的变化。"],[1024.19,1030.86,29,"So ChatGPT, the product that changed the field, was SFT plus RLHF with PPO.","所以，改变了整个领域的 ChatGPT，就是 SFT 加上基于 PPO 的 RLHF。"],[1031.21,1038.06,29,"But PPO is heavy: you need a reward model, a value model, online sampling and a lot of tuning.","但 PPO 很重：你需要奖励模型、价值模型、在线采样，还有大量调参。"],[1038.41,1043.49,29,"Is there a simpler way to learn from the same preference pairs? That's DPO.","有没有更简单的方法从同样的偏好对中学习？这就是 DPO。"]]},{"n":3,"title":"DPO, Biased Judges and Reward Hacking","blurb":"Direct Preference Optimization learns from preference pairs without a reward model or RL, then the limits: biased human and model judges, and reward hacking.","file":"lecture06_part3.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part3.jpg","duration":419.1,"first":30,"last":37,"slides":[{"n":30,"title":"DPO: Preference Learning without a Reward Model or RL","t":0.8},{"n":31,"title":"DPO in Practice: Data, Benefits, and Off-Policy Learning","t":73.73},{"n":32,"title":"2.3 When Human Feedback Falls Short","t":150.25},{"n":33,"title":"Biases of Human Feedback","t":170.02},{"n":35,"title":"Measuring Judge Bias: Change One Thing, Watch the Verdict","t":209.91},{"n":36,"title":"Results: Who Is Biased? (Attack Success Rate, lower is better)","t":279.18},{"n":37,"title":"Limits of RLHF: Reward Hacking","t":343.32}],"sents":[[0.8,8.26,30,"DPO, direct preference optimization, is one of the most influential ideas of twenty twenty-three.","DPO，直接偏好优化，是 2023 年最有影响力的想法之一。"],[8.61,10.75,30,"Compare the two pipelines at the top.","对比一下上面的两条流程。"],[11.1,17.98,30,"RLHF goes from preference pairs to a reward model, to online sampling with PPO.","RLHF 从偏好对出发，先训练奖励模型，再用 PPO 做在线采样。"],[18.33,24.31,30,"DPO goes from preference pairs straight to the policy, with one classification-style loss.","DPO 则从偏好对直接到策略，只用一个类似分类的损失。"],[24.66,31.36,30,"The key insight is that the optimal RLHF policy has a closed form, and you can flip it around.","关键洞察在于：RLHF 的最优策略有闭式解，而且你可以把它反过来写。"],[31.71,38.2,30,"The reward can be written as beta times the log-ratio between the policy and the reference model, plus a constant.","奖励可以写成 beta 乘以策略与参考模型的对数比值，再加上一个常数。"],[38.55,43.29,30,"Plug that into the Bradley-Terry model, and the reward model disappears.","把它代入 Bradley-Terry 模型，奖励模型就消失了。"],[43.64,45.74,30,"What's left is the DPO loss.","剩下的就是 DPO 损失。"],[46.09,55.34,30,"Read it like this. For the chosen answer y w and the rejected answer y l, compute how much more likely each has become relative to the reference model.","可以这样读：对被选中的答案 yw 和被拒绝的答案 yl，分别计算它们相对参考模型的概率提升了多少。"],[55.69,59.32,30,"Then push the chosen one up, and the rejected one down.","然后把被选中的往上推，把被拒绝的往下压。"],[59.67,66.18,30,"It's the same objective as RLHF, but with no reward model, no sampling and no PPO.","它和 RLHF 的目标相同，却不需要奖励模型、不需要采样、也不需要 PPO。"],[66.53,72.33,30,"That's why the paper's title says your language model is secretly a reward model.","这就是为什么论文标题说：你的语言模型其实暗中就是一个奖励模型。"],[73.58,75.84,31,"What does DPO look like in practice?","DPO 在实践中是什么样子的？"],[76.19,81.43,31,"One training example is a triple: a prompt, a chosen answer and a rejected one.","一个训练样本是一个三元组：一个提示、一个被选中的答案和一个被拒绝的答案。"],[81.78,89.11,31,"Here, for a cat that hasn't eaten since yesterday, the chosen answer says this can be serious, and to call a vet.","这里，对于一只从昨天起就没吃东西的猫，被选中的答案说这可能很严重，要联系兽医。"],[89.46,92.03,31,"The rejected one says: just wait.","被拒绝的答案则说：等等就好。"],[92.38,98.0,31,"These pairs can come from human labels, AI feedback or ranked model samples.","这些配对可以来自人工标注、AI 反馈，或者对模型样本的排序。"],[98.35,101.28,31,"People like DPO because it's cheap and stable.","大家喜欢 DPO，是因为它便宜又稳定。"],[101.63,107.7,31,"You only need the policy plus a frozen reference, so it costs about as much as SFT.","你只需要策略模型加一个冻结的参考模型，所以成本和 SFT 差不多。"],[108.05,112.19,31,"And it's been used in Zephyr, Llama 3 and Tulu 3.","它已被用于 Zephyr、Llama 3 和 Tülu 3。"],[112.54,117.32,31,"But look at the right column, because this distinction comes back all lecture.","但请看右边这一栏，因为这个区别会贯穿整堂课。"],[117.67,124.52,31,"PPO and GRPO are on-policy: they learn from answers the current model just generated, so they can explore.","PPO 和 GRPO 是同策略的：它们从当前模型刚生成的答案中学习，所以能够探索。"],[124.87,130.64,31,"DPO is off-policy: it learns from a fixed dataset, often written by other models.","DPO 是异策略的：它从一个固定的数据集中学习，这些数据往往由其他模型写成。"],[130.99,137.25,31,"That's cheap, but it can't explore, and the model is trained on answers it would never produce itself.","这样很便宜，但无法探索，而且模型是在它自己永远不会写出的答案上训练的。"],[137.6,142.81,31,"The fix is iterative or online DPO, or going back to on-policy RL.","解决办法是迭代式或在线 DPO，或者回到同策略强化学习。"],[143.16,148.85,31,"Either way, everything so far rests on the preference labels being right. Are they?","无论哪种方式，到目前为止的一切都建立在偏好标签正确的前提上。它们真的正确吗？"],[150.1,154.07,32,"So far we've assumed the preference labels are the ground truth.","到目前为止，我们一直假设偏好标签就是标准答案。"],[154.42,156.57,32,"This subsection questions that.","这一小节要质疑这一点。"],[156.92,161.31,32,"A reward model can only be as good as the judgments it learns from.","奖励模型的好坏，取决于它所学习的那些判断。"],[161.66,168.62,32,"And both human and LLM judges turn out to be biased, in ways we can actually measure.","而事实证明，无论是人类还是大模型评判者都有偏差，而且这些偏差是可以测量的。"],[169.87,181.34,33,"This is a piece of work from our own group, published at EMNLP twenty twenty-four: Humans or LLMs as the Judge? A Study on Judgement Biases.","这是我们课题组自己的一项工作，发表在 EMNLP 2024：《人类还是大模型当评判者？关于评判偏差的研究》。"],[181.69,183.39,33,"The motivation is simple.","动机很简单。"],[183.74,188.95,33,"The RLHF story we just told treats human preferences as the gold standard.","我们刚讲的 RLHF 故事，把人类偏好当作金标准。"],[189.3,197.44,33,"And more and more, people replace humans with LLMs as judges, both for evaluation and for producing preference data.","而且越来越多的人用大模型代替人来当评判者，既用于评测，也用于生成偏好数据。"],[197.79,204.07,33,"So we asked: how biased are these judges, human and LLM, and in what ways?","所以我们问：这些评判者，无论是人还是大模型，偏差有多大？又是哪些方面的偏差？"],[204.42,208.51,33,"Next, let's see how we measured it, and then what we found.","接下来，我们先看怎么测量，再看发现了什么。"],[209.76,214.63,35,"Here's the method, and the nice thing about it is that it doesn't need gold labels.","这是我们的方法，它的好处是不需要金标准标签。"],[214.98,220.4,35,"We took one hundred forty-two questions across Bloom's six levels of cognition.","我们选取了一百四十二个问题，覆盖布鲁姆认知分类的六个层次。"],[220.75,226.2,35,"For each one, we have two independently written answers, A one and A two.","每个问题都有两个独立撰写的答案，A1 和 A2。"],[226.55,232.28,35,"Then we edit A two in exactly one way, to get a perturbed version.","然后我们只对 A2 做一处修改，得到一个扰动版本。"],[232.63,239.27,35,"And we ask the judge twice: A one versus A two, and A one versus the perturbed A two.","然后让评判者判两次：A1 对 A2，以及 A1 对扰动后的 A2。"],[239.62,244.14,35,"If the verdict flips toward the perturbed answer, the perturbation worked.","如果判决翻转到扰动后的答案，扰动就成功了。"],[244.49,247.95,35,"The attack success rate is how often that happens.","攻击成功率就是这种情况发生的频率。"],[248.3,249.68,35,"There are four perturbations.","一共有四种扰动。"],[250.03,257.23,35,"Insert a factual error, like six times seven equals thirty-six. A fair judge should then prefer A one.","插入一个事实错误，比如六乘七等于三十六。公正的评判者此时应该偏好 A1。"],[257.58,261.37,35,"Add a gender stereotype. Again, it should prefer A one.","加入性别刻板印象。同样，应该偏好 A1。"],[261.72,265.35,35,"Add a fake reference, or add emojis and markdown.","加入一条伪造的参考文献，或者加入表情符号和 markdown 格式。"],[265.7,269.44,35,"Neither should change the verdict, because the content is the same.","这两种都不应该改变判决，因为内容是一样的。"],[269.79,271.9,35,"The key word is reference-free.","关键词是“无需参考答案”。"],[272.25,277.78,35,"We never need to know the right answer. We only check whether the verdict moves when it shouldn't.","我们从不需要知道正确答案，只需检查判决是否在不该变的时候变了。"],[279.03,284.69,36,"And here are the results. Lower is better, and the random line is what you'd get by guessing.","下面是结果。数值越低越好，random 那条线是随机猜测的水平。"],[285.04,286.97,36,"First, misinformation.","首先是错误信息。"],[287.32,295.83,36,"Strong LLMs like GPT-4o catch inserted errors well, while humans miss more, at about zero point two one.","像 GPT-4o 这样的强大模型能很好地发现插入的错误，而人类漏掉的更多，约为零点二一。"],[296.18,304.82,36,"Gender bias goes the other way: humans are the least biased, at zero point zero six, and every LLM judge is worse.","性别偏差则相反：人类偏差最小，只有零点零六，每个大模型评判者都更差。"],[305.17,309.15,36,"Authority bias, the fake references, fools everyone.","权威偏差，也就是伪造的参考文献，骗过了所有评判者。"],[309.5,314.77,36,"No judge does much better than random, and Claude-2 is fooled eighty-nine percent of the time.","没有哪个评判者明显好于随机猜测，Claude-2 有百分之八十九的情况被骗。"],[315.12,321.74,36,"And beauty bias: humans are quite swayed by emojis and markdown, at zero point four seven.","还有美观偏差：人类很容易被表情符号和 markdown 左右，达到零点四七。"],[322.09,327.62,36,"So there's no perfect judge. Humans and LLMs fail in different places.","所以不存在完美的评判者。人类和大模型在不同的地方出错。"],[327.97,330.96,36,"And the bottom line is the important bit for this lecture.","而底部这一行，是对这堂课最重要的一点。"],[331.31,334.56,36,"Reward models learn from exactly these judgments.","奖励模型正是从这些判断中学习的。"],[334.91,341.92,36,"They inherit the biases, and then RL, which is a very good optimizer, will find and exploit them.","它们继承了这些偏差，而强化学习是一个非常强的优化器，它会找到并利用这些偏差。"],[343.17,347.21,37,"That brings us to the fundamental limit of RLHF: reward hacking.","这就引出了 RLHF 的根本局限：奖励投机。"],[347.56,352.88,37,"Goodhart's law says: when a measure becomes a target, it ceases to be a good measure.","古德哈特定律说：当一个指标变成目标时，它就不再是一个好指标。"],[353.23,357.27,37,"The reward model is a measure. RL makes it a target.","奖励模型是一个指标，而强化学习把它变成了目标。"],[357.62,359.8,37,"You see this in several ways.","这体现在好几个方面。"],[360.15,368.36,37,"Over-optimization: as training goes on, the reward model score keeps rising, while true quality peaks and then falls.","过度优化：随着训练进行，奖励模型的分数不断上升，而真实质量先到达峰值然后下降。"],[368.71,376.29,37,"Length and style: longer, more confident, nicely formatted answers win, the very biases we just measured.","长度和风格：更长、更自信、格式更漂亮的答案胜出，这正是我们刚才测量到的偏差。"],[376.64,381.52,37,"Sycophancy: the model learns to agree with you, rather than be right.","谄媚：模型学会附和你，而不是追求正确。"],[381.87,388.73,37,"And cost: humans are slow and noisy, and they simply can't check a long proof or a large program.","还有成本：人类又慢又有噪声，而且根本无法检查一个长证明或一个大型程序。"],[389.08,394.04,37,"Look at the box on the right. What if the reward isn't learned at all, but checked?","看右边这个框。如果奖励根本不是学出来的，而是检查出来的呢？"],[394.39,399.21,37,"For math and code we can verify the answer: reward one if correct, zero otherwise.","对于数学和代码，我们可以验证答案：正确得一分，否则得零分。"],[399.56,403.86,37,"That's RL with verifiable rewards, RLVR.","这就是基于可验证奖励的强化学习，RLVR。"],[404.21,407.76,37,"It's much harder to hack, and it scales with compute.","它更难被投机，而且能随算力扩展。"],[408.11,412.86,37,"Hold that thought. It's where the whole reasoning half of the lecture comes from.","先记住这个想法，整堂课关于推理的后半部分都源于此。"],[413.21,417.21,37,"First, though, we need to understand the RL algorithms themselves.","不过首先，我们需要理解强化学习算法本身。"]]},{"n":4,"title":"RL for LLMs: PPO, REINFORCE and ReMax","blurb":"Text generation as an RL problem, what makes LLM rewards and compute different, the cost of PPO's critic, and ReMax's greedy baseline for REINFORCE.","file":"lecture06_part4.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part4.jpg","duration":947.2,"first":38,"last":55,"slides":[{"n":38,"title":"3 RL Algorithms for LLMs","t":0.8},{"n":39,"title":"Why Reinforcement Learning?","t":32.77},{"n":40,"title":"The RL Framework for Language Models","t":94.15},{"n":41,"title":"Generating Text as an RL Problem","t":143.98},{"n":42,"title":"What Is Different? (1) Heterogeneous Rewards","t":226.0},{"n":43,"title":"What Is Different? (2) Enormous Compute","t":286.82},{"n":44,"title":"The Evolution of RL Algorithms for LLMs","t":335.59},{"n":45,"title":"3.2 PPO: The Classic Recipe and Its Cost","t":388.77},{"n":46,"title":"PPO for RLHF: Actor–Critic with Clipping","t":409.23},{"n":47,"title":"The Price of PPO","t":487.51},{"n":48,"title":"3.3 Back to REINFORCE: ReMax","t":536.7},{"n":49,"title":"General RL vs. RL for LLMs","t":559.96},{"n":50,"title":"Back to the Classic: REINFORCE","t":616.73},{"n":51,"title":"REINFORCE at Scale: High Variance","t":670.73},{"n":52,"title":"ReMax: REINFORCE with a Greedy Baseline","t":728.32},{"n":53,"title":"ReMax: Unbiased, with Provably Lower Variance","t":799.89},{"n":54,"title":"ReMax in Practice: Lighter and Faster than PPO","t":847.63},{"n":55,"title":"Algorithms Drive Infrastructure","t":895.2}],"sents":[[0.8,5.8,38,"So far we've treated RL as a black box that pushes up high-reward answers.","到目前为止，我们把强化学习当作一个提升高奖励答案的黑箱。"],[6.15,8.38,38,"Part three opens that box.","第三部分就来打开这个黑箱。"],[8.73,12.69,38,"We need RL because rewards can't be differentiated.","我们需要强化学习，是因为奖励无法求导。"],[13.04,19.85,38,"But which algorithm we pick decides the cost, the stability, and even what kind of rewards we can use.","但选择哪种算法，决定了成本、稳定性，甚至我们能用什么样的奖励。"],[20.2,25.58,38,"We'll go from PPO back to REINFORCE, then forward through ReMax, GRPO and DAPO.","我们会从 PPO 回溯到 REINFORCE，再往前讲 ReMax、GRPO 和 DAPO。"],[25.93,31.37,38,"And we'll finish with RLHF versus RLVR, and the open frontier.","最后讲 RLHF 与 RLVR 的对比，以及开放的前沿问题。"],[32.62,38.31,39,"Before the algorithms, let's step back and ask why RL deserves so much attention.","在讲算法之前，我们先退一步问：为什么强化学习值得这么多关注？"],[38.66,40.29,39,"There are three good arguments.","有三个很好的理由。"],[40.64,47.78,39,"The first is philosophical: imitation can only bring you up to the level of your data, while RL can go beyond it.","第一个是哲学上的：模仿只能把你带到数据的水平，而强化学习可以超越它。"],[48.13,56.12,39,"AlphaGo and AlphaTensor discovered moves and algorithms no human had shown them, by learning from their own trial and error.","AlphaGo 和 AlphaTensor 通过从自己的试错中学习，发现了人类从未教过它们的棋步和算法。"],[56.47,58.23,39,"The second is performance.","第二个是性能。"],[58.58,69.39,39,"With o1 and DeepSeek-R1, RL didn't just add a few points. Long reasoning behaviours appeared only after large-scale RL.","在 o1 和 DeepSeek-R1 上，强化学习不只是提高了几个点，长推理行为只有在大规模强化学习之后才出现。"],[69.74,71.39,39,"The third is data.","第三个是数据。"],[71.74,75.83,39,"RL generates its own training data through rollouts.","强化学习通过 rollout 生成自己的训练数据。"],[76.18,82.71,39,"That supply is essentially unlimited, costs no human writing, and raises no copyright issues.","这种供给基本上是无限的，不需要人来写，也不涉及版权问题。"],[83.06,84.45,39,"So the one-line summary:","所以一句话总结："],[84.8,92.75,39,"Pre-training and SFT imitate data that already exists. RL lets the model create new data, and learn from it.","预训练和 SFT 模仿的是已经存在的数据，而强化学习让模型创造新数据，并从中学习。"],[94.0,98.41,40,"Here's the RL setup for a language model, as simple as it gets.","这是语言模型的强化学习设定，已经简化到了极致。"],[98.76,100.59,40,"It's a loop with four steps.","这是一个包含四个步骤的循环。"],[100.94,109.34,40,"The model samples a response, the reward function evaluates it, it produces a score, and we use that score to improve the model.","模型采样一个回答，奖励函数对它进行评估，得出一个分数，我们再用这个分数改进模型。"],[109.69,117.94,40,"The objective at the bottom says: average over prompts x drawn from some prompt distribution, and over responses y sampled from the model.","底部的目标函数是说：对从某个提示分布中抽取的提示 x、以及从模型中采样的回答 y 取平均。"],[118.29,120.86,40,"And maximize the expected reward.","然后最大化期望奖励。"],[121.21,124.94,40,"Notice that the reward function r is a black box here.","注意，这里的奖励函数 r 是一个黑箱。"],[125.29,132.74,40,"It could be a reward model trained on human preferences, a unit test, an answer checker, or an environment.","它可以是用人类偏好训练的奖励模型、单元测试、答案检查器，或者一个环境。"],[133.09,134.62,40,"The algorithm doesn't care.","算法并不在乎。"],[134.97,142.58,40,"That's exactly why the same RL machinery carries us from alignment to reasoning to agents: we just swap the reward function.","正因如此，同一套强化学习机制能带我们从对齐走到推理，再走到智能体：我们只需更换奖励函数。"],[143.83,147.13,41,"Let's make the RL vocabulary concrete for text.","我们把强化学习的术语在文本上具体化。"],[147.48,151.46,41,"The state is the prompt plus the tokens generated so far.","状态是提示加上目前已生成的 token。"],[151.81,153.67,41,"The action is the next token.","动作是下一个 token。"],[154.02,156.64,41,"The policy is the LLM itself.","策略就是大模型本身。"],[156.99,162.78,41,"The reward usually comes once, at the end, from a reward model or a verifier.","奖励通常只在最后给出一次，来自奖励模型或验证器。"],[163.13,165.98,41,"And one episode is one complete answer.","一个回合就是一个完整的回答。"],[166.33,171.24,41,"Then REINFORCE, from nineteen ninety-two, gives us the gradient.","然后，1992 年的 REINFORCE 给出了梯度。"],[171.59,177.41,41,"Sample an answer, score it, and make it more likely if it scored above a baseline b.","采样一个答案，给它打分，如果它的分数高于基线 b，就提高它的概率。"],[177.76,184.4,41,"In the formula, the term r minus b is the advantage: how much better than expected was this answer.","公式里，r 减 b 这一项就是优势：这个答案比预期好了多少。"],[184.75,191.13,41,"It multiplies the gradient of the log-probability, which is the direction that makes this answer more likely.","它乘以对数概率的梯度，也就是让这个答案更可能出现的方向。"],[191.48,192.47,41,"Why the baseline?","为什么需要基线？"],[192.82,200.29,41,"Without it, if all rewards are positive, you'd push up every answer, just some more than others, which is very noisy.","没有基线的话，如果所有奖励都是正的，你会提高每一个答案的概率，只是程度不同，这样噪声非常大。"],[200.64,205.67,41,"Subtracting a good baseline reduces variance without biasing the gradient.","减去一个好的基线，可以在不引入梯度偏差的情况下降低方差。"],[206.02,213.88,41,"And here's the key insight for the rest of this section: the main difference between PPO, ReMax and GRPO is just how they get b.","这是本节剩余部分的关键洞察：PPO、ReMax 和 GRPO 的主要区别，只在于它们如何得到 b。"],[214.23,216.26,41,"PPO learns a value model.","PPO 学习一个价值模型。"],[216.61,219.48,41,"ReMax uses the reward of the greedy answer.","ReMax 使用贪心答案的奖励。"],[219.83,222.69,41,"GRPO uses the average of other samples.","GRPO 使用其他样本的平均奖励。"],[223.04,224.6,41,"Remember these three.","请记住这三种。"],[225.85,233.18,42,"What makes RL for LLMs different from textbook RL? There are two things, and this is the first.","大模型的强化学习和教科书里的强化学习有什么不同？有两点，这是第一点。"],[233.53,237.23,42,"Rewards are very heterogeneous across prompts.","不同提示之间的奖励差异非常大。"],[237.58,243.85,42,"On the left, for RLHF, each prompt's reward-model scores sit in quite different ranges.","左边是 RLHF，每个提示的奖励模型分数落在相当不同的区间里。"],[244.2,249.92,42,"One prompt's scores cluster around five, while another's spread out between ten and twenty.","有的提示分数集中在五分左右，有的则分散在十分到二十分之间。"],[250.27,257.42,42,"On the right, for RLVR, accuracy per prompt varies hugely between easy and hard levels.","右边是 RLVR，每个提示的准确率在简单和困难级别之间差异巨大。"],[257.77,262.51,42,"Some prompts are almost always solved, others almost never.","有些提示几乎总能解出来，有些则几乎从来解不出。"],[262.86,263.87,42,"Why does that matter?","这为什么重要？"],[264.22,271.26,42,"Because a raw reward of plus two means something completely different for an easy prompt than for a hard one.","因为同样是加二的原始奖励，对简单提示和困难提示来说意义完全不同。"],[271.61,279.58,42,"If the algorithm doesn't account for that, gradients get dominated by whichever prompts happen to have large reward scales, and training becomes unstable.","如果算法不考虑这一点，梯度就会被那些奖励尺度恰好很大的提示所主导，训练就会变得不稳定。"],[279.93,285.42,42,"So we need algorithms that are robust to this kind of heterogeneous data.","所以我们需要对这种异质数据鲁棒的算法。"],[286.67,288.94,43,"The second difference is sheer scale.","第二个不同是纯粹的规模。"],[289.29,295.79,43,"On the left, pre-training data has gone from about three hundred billion tokens to eighteen trillion.","左边，预训练数据从大约三千亿 token 增长到了十八万亿。"],[296.14,300.06,43,"On the right, model size has grown much faster than GPU memory.","右边，模型规模的增长速度远远超过了 GPU 显存。"],[300.41,307.48,43,"In RL this hurts even more than in pre-training, because you often need several models in memory at the same time.","在强化学习中，这比在预训练中更要命，因为你常常需要同时把好几个模型放进显存。"],[307.83,313.22,43,"The policy, a reference model, a reward model, and in PPO, a value model too.","策略模型、参考模型、奖励模型，在 PPO 里还要加一个价值模型。"],[313.57,318.07,43,"Every extra model copy is expensive, and generating rollouts is slow.","每多一份模型副本都很昂贵，而且生成 rollout 很慢。"],[318.42,324.54,43,"So our second requirement is that algorithms be computationally efficient and stable at scale.","所以我们的第二个要求是：算法在大规模下要计算高效且稳定。"],[324.89,330.66,43,"Keep both requirements in mind: robust to heterogeneous rewards, and cheap in compute.","请记住这两个要求：对异质奖励鲁棒，以及计算便宜。"],[331.01,334.19,43,"They'll explain each design choice we see next.","它们能解释接下来我们看到的每一个设计选择。"],[335.44,337.82,44,"Here's the map for the rest of this section.","这是本节剩余部分的地图。"],[338.17,342.46,44,"REINFORCE comes from nineteen ninety-two, before LLMs.","REINFORCE 来自 1992 年，早于大模型时代。"],[342.81,348.96,44,"PPO came from OpenAI in twenty seventeen, and powered InstructGPT and ChatGPT.","PPO 由 OpenAI 在 2017 年提出，支撑了 InstructGPT 和 ChatGPT。"],[349.31,356.32,44,"Then ReMax, from our school, CUHK-Shenzhen, together with Nanjing University, in twenty twenty-three.","然后是 ReMax，来自我们学校香港中文大学深圳，与南京大学合作，发表于 2023 年。"],[356.67,362.47,44,"Then GRPO from DeepSeek in twenty twenty-four, and many variants after that.","然后是 DeepSeek 在 2024 年提出的 GRPO，以及之后的许多变体。"],[362.82,365.85,44,"The bracket says these are all variants of REINFORCE.","这个括号说明，它们都是 REINFORCE 的变体。"],[366.2,373.48,44,"PPO adds a learned critic and clipping on top, while ReMax and GRPO stay much closer to the original.","PPO 在此基础上加了学习得到的评论家和裁剪，而 ReMax 和 GRPO 更接近原始版本。"],[373.83,378.57,44,"Viewed through the lens of the baseline from two slides ago, they're one family.","从两页前讲的基线的视角来看，它们是一家人。"],[378.92,387.37,44,"So the story goes: PPO and why it's expensive, back to REINFORCE, then ReMax, GRPO and DAPO, and finally the frontier.","所以故事是这样展开的：PPO 及其昂贵之处，回到 REINFORCE，然后是 ReMax、GRPO 和 DAPO，最后是前沿。"],[388.62,390.31,45,"Let's start with the classic.","我们从经典算法开始。"],[390.66,396.66,45,"PPO is the algorithm behind InstructGPT and ChatGPT, so it deserves respect.","PPO 是 InstructGPT 和 ChatGPT 背后的算法，值得尊重。"],[397.01,402.17,45,"But it was designed for general RL problems, like robots and games.","但它是为通用强化学习问题设计的，比如机器人和游戏。"],[402.52,407.83,45,"And as we'll see, LLM training pays a high price for that generality.","我们将看到，大模型训练为这种通用性付出了高昂的代价。"],[409.08,411.83,46,"This is PPO as it's used in RLHF.","这是 RLHF 中使用的 PPO。"],[412.18,416.76,46,"The first thing to notice is the top row: four models in GPU memory at once.","首先要注意的是最上面：同时有四个模型在 GPU 显存里。"],[417.11,423.1,46,"The policy and the critic are being trained. The reward model and the reference model are frozen.","策略模型和评论家在训练，奖励模型和参考模型则是冻结的。"],[423.45,424.96,46,"One iteration goes like this.","一次迭代是这样的。"],[425.31,427.29,46,"Sample answers from the policy.","从策略中采样答案。"],[427.64,432.59,46,"Score them with the reward model, minus a KL penalty for drifting from the reference.","用奖励模型打分，再减去偏离参考模型的 KL 惩罚。"],[432.94,442.29,46,"Then the critic, or value model, estimates how good each prefix of the answer is, and from that we get an advantage for every token.","然后评论家，也就是价值模型，估计答案每个前缀有多好，由此得到每个 token 的优势。"],[442.64,445.38,46,"Finally, update with the clipped objective.","最后，用裁剪后的目标函数进行更新。"],[445.73,451.29,46,"About that objective: rho is the ratio between the new and old probability of a token.","关于这个目标函数：rho 是一个 token 新旧概率之比。"],[451.64,462.14,46,"Taking the minimum with a clipped version means the update gets no extra credit for moving that ratio outside a small window, say zero point eight to one point two.","与裁剪版本取最小值，意味着把这个比值推到一个小窗口之外不会获得额外收益，比如零点八到一点二。"],[462.49,467.05,46,"So each step stays small and safe. That's the proximal in the name.","所以每一步都保持小而安全，这就是名字里“近端”的含义。"],[467.4,472.9,46,"The strengths are real: it's stable, well studied, and it gives token-level credit.","它的优点是实实在在的：稳定、研究充分，并且能给出 token 级别的功劳分配。"],[473.25,481.54,46,"But the critic is as big as the policy, there are many hyperparameters, and learning per-token values from one final reward is hard.","但评论家和策略一样大，超参数很多，而且从一个最终奖励中学出每个 token 的价值很难。"],[481.89,486.11,46,"So the question to hold on to is: can we drop the critic?","所以要记住的问题是：我们能不能去掉评论家？"],[487.36,489.34,47,"Let's put numbers on that cost.","我们给这个成本标上数字。"],[489.69,492.75,47,"GPU memory is roughly twice that of SFT.","GPU 显存大约是 SFT 的两倍。"],[493.1,500.26,47,"That's because the value model is as large as the policy, and both need parameters, gradients and optimizer states.","这是因为价值模型和策略一样大，两者都需要存储参数、梯度和优化器状态。"],[500.61,504.17,47,"Training time is two to four times that of SFT.","训练时间是 SFT 的两到四倍。"],[504.52,512.34,47,"Each step involves generation, scoring and two backward passes, and most of the time actually goes into generating the rollouts.","每一步都包含生成、打分和两次反向传播，而大部分时间其实花在生成 rollout 上。"],[512.69,516.13,47,"And tuning: there are at least five extra hyperparameters.","还有调参：至少多出五个额外的超参数。"],[516.48,523.47,47,"Like the value model's learning rate, GAE gamma and lambda, the clipping range, and how often to update the critic.","比如价值模型的学习率、GAE 的 gamma 和 lambda、裁剪范围，以及评论家的更新频率。"],[523.82,529.29,47,"All of that machinery exists because PPO was built for general RL problems.","所有这些机制之所以存在，是因为 PPO 是为通用强化学习问题打造的。"],[529.64,535.3,47,"So the honest question is the one at the bottom: does LLM training really need all of this?","所以真正该问的就是底部这个问题：大模型训练真的需要这一切吗？"],[536.55,538.82,48,"That's what this subsection answers.","这一小节就来回答这个问题。"],[539.17,544.78,48,"It turns out RL for LLMs is a simpler problem than general RL.","事实证明，大模型的强化学习比通用强化学习要简单。"],[545.13,551.21,48,"Feedback is fast, transitions are deterministic, and there's one reward per answer.","反馈很快，状态转移是确定的，而且每个答案只有一个奖励。"],[551.56,558.56,48,"In that setting, a nineteen ninety-two algorithm, REINFORCE, plus the right baseline, is enough.","在这种设定下，一个 1992 年的算法 REINFORCE，加上合适的基线，就足够了。"],[559.81,562.44,49,"Let's compare the two settings side by side.","我们把两种设定并排比较一下。"],[562.79,566.71,49,"At the top, general RL, for example StarCraft II.","上面是通用强化学习，比如星际争霸二。"],[567.06,570.85,49,"Feedback is slow, around an hour of simulation per game.","反馈很慢，每局大约需要一小时的模拟。"],[571.2,578.65,49,"The environment is stochastic: you take an action, and the opponent or random noise decides what happens next.","环境是随机的：你做出一个动作，接下来发生什么由对手或随机噪声决定。"],[579.0,581.71,49,"And rewards can appear all along the way.","奖励也可能在过程中随时出现。"],[582.06,584.47,49,"Below, RL for LLMs.","下面是大模型的强化学习。"],[584.82,587.89,49,"Feedback is fast, about ten seconds of inference.","反馈很快，大约十秒的推理时间。"],[588.24,594.6,49,"Transitions are deterministic: the next state is literally the old text with one token appended.","状态转移是确定的：下一个状态就是在原文本后面加上一个 token。"],[594.95,598.28,49,"And there's typically one reward for the whole answer.","而且通常整个答案只有一个奖励。"],[598.63,605.05,49,"A value model is very useful when the world is stochastic and rewards are spread over long episodes.","当世界是随机的、奖励分散在很长的回合中时，价值模型非常有用。"],[605.4,608.15,49,"Here, much of that justification goes away.","而在这里，这些理由大多不再成立。"],[608.5,615.33,49,"So the question becomes: can we design a lightweight RL algorithm without a value model at all?","所以问题就变成了：我们能不能设计一个完全不需要价值模型的轻量级强化学习算法？"],[616.58,620.26,50,"The answer starts with going back to the classic: REINFORCE.","答案要从回到经典开始：REINFORCE。"],[620.61,628.16,50,"It fits our setting perfectly: fast feedback, deterministic transitions, and a reward for the whole trajectory.","它完美契合我们的设定：反馈快、转移确定、整个轨迹一个奖励。"],[628.51,631.86,50,"Look at the formula and the three labels under it.","看这个公式以及它下面的三个标注。"],[632.21,641.2,50,"The gradient of the expected reward equals the expectation of the gradient of the log-likelihood, multiplied by the reward.","期望奖励的梯度，等于对数似然梯度乘以奖励之后的期望。"],[641.55,649.19,50,"So it's really just likelihood training, the same thing you do in SFT, but each sample is weighted by its reward.","所以它其实就是似然训练，和 SFT 里做的一样，只不过每个样本都用它的奖励来加权。"],[649.54,655.24,50,"Good answers get a big push up. Bad ones get little, or even a push down.","好的答案会被大幅提升，差的答案提升很少，甚至被压低。"],[655.59,662.93,50,"In practice you estimate this by Monte Carlo: sample some answers, score them, reweight, and take a gradient step.","实践中，你用蒙特卡洛来估计它：采样一些答案，打分，重新加权，然后做一步梯度更新。"],[663.28,665.38,50,"That's it. No value model needed.","就这么简单，不需要价值模型。"],[665.73,669.33,50,"So why didn't everyone just use this from the start?","那为什么大家不一开始就用它呢？"],[670.58,677.42,51,"Because vanilla REINFORCE has very high variance, and at scale that makes RLHF unstable.","因为原始的 REINFORCE 方差非常大，在大规模下会让 RLHF 变得不稳定。"],[677.77,680.64,51,"Look at the three panels from left to right.","从左到右看这三张图。"],[680.99,686.18,51,"On the left are the reward-model score distributions for four different prompts.","左边是四个不同提示的奖励模型分数分布。"],[686.53,693.35,51,"They sit in quite different places. Across prompts, scores can range from about minus fourteen to plus seven.","它们落在相当不同的位置。不同提示之间，分数范围大约从负十四到正七。"],[693.7,696.33,51,"That's the heterogeneity we talked about earlier.","这就是我们之前讲的异质性。"],[696.68,702.64,51,"In the middle is the gradient norm during training of OPT with one point three billion parameters.","中间是训练十三亿参数的 OPT 时的梯度范数。"],[702.99,707.51,51,"The red REINFORCE curve explodes, spiking by orders of magnitude.","红色的 REINFORCE 曲线爆炸了，飙升了好几个数量级。"],[707.86,713.85,51,"On the right is the evaluation reward. REINFORCE's reward actually goes down over training.","右边是评估奖励。REINFORCE 的奖励在训练过程中反而下降了。"],[714.2,720.68,51,"The blue curve is ReMax: the same algorithm family plus one thing, a baseline that cuts the variance.","蓝色曲线是 ReMax：同一个算法家族，只多了一样东西，一个降低方差的基线。"],[721.03,724.95,51,"Gradients stay flat, and reward goes up steadily.","梯度保持平稳，奖励稳步上升。"],[725.3,726.92,51,"Let's see what that baseline is.","我们来看看这个基线是什么。"],[728.17,729.51,52,"Here's ReMax.","这就是 ReMax。"],[729.86,739.24,52,"Keep the simplest RL algorithm, REINFORCE, and add one cheap but strong baseline: the reward of the greedy answer.","保留最简单的强化学习算法 REINFORCE，再加上一个廉价但强大的基线：贪心答案的奖励。"],[739.59,740.47,52,"Follow the figure.","跟着图走一遍。"],[740.82,743.27,52,"For a prompt, we generate two answers.","对一个提示，我们生成两个答案。"],[743.62,748.85,52,"One is sampled randomly, and one is greedy, always picking the most likely token.","一个是随机采样的，一个是贪心的，每一步都选概率最大的 token。"],[749.2,752.9,52,"Both get scored, here zero point seven and zero point five.","两者都被打分，这里分别是零点七和零点五。"],[753.25,759.96,52,"The advantage is the difference, plus zero point two, so we push the sampled answer up.","优势就是两者之差，加零点二，所以我们提升这个采样答案的概率。"],[760.31,764.5,52,"If the sample had scored worse than the greedy answer, we'd push it down.","如果采样答案的分数比贪心答案低，我们就会压低它。"],[764.85,765.98,52,"Why does this work?","为什么这样有效？"],[766.33,773.78,52,"The greedy reward is prompt-specific, so it automatically adjusts for whether this prompt tends to get high or low scores.","贪心奖励是针对每个提示的，所以它会自动根据这个提示通常得分高还是低来调整。"],[774.13,777.37,52,"That's exactly the heterogeneity problem solved.","这正好解决了异质性问题。"],[777.72,783.57,52,"And since the greedy answer doesn't depend on the random sample, the gradient stays unbiased.","而且由于贪心答案不依赖于随机样本，梯度保持无偏。"],[783.92,790.54,52,"The cost is one extra greedy decode: no critic, and about half the memory of PPO.","代价只是多一次贪心解码：不需要评论家，显存约为 PPO 的一半。"],[790.89,798.49,52,"And I'm proud to say the first author, Ziniu Li, did his PhD right here at CUHK-Shenzhen, in our school.","我很自豪地说，第一作者李子牛就是在我们港中大深圳、在我们学院读的博士。"],[799.74,803.9,53,"Here's the theory behind that intuition, from the ReMax paper.","这是 ReMax 论文中支撑这个直觉的理论。"],[804.25,811.21,53,"The baseline is defined at the top: the reward of the sequence you get by taking the argmax token at every step.","基线定义在最上面：每一步都取概率最大的 token，得到的序列的奖励。"],[811.56,815.16,53,"Two properties matter, and they're in the two boxes.","有两个性质很重要，分别在这两个框里。"],[815.51,818.15,53,"First, the gradient is unbiased.","第一，梯度是无偏的。"],[818.5,826.85,53,"In expectation, maximizing the advantage is the same as maximizing the reward, because the greedy baseline doesn't depend on the sampled answer.","在期望意义下，最大化优势等同于最大化奖励，因为贪心基线不依赖于采样的答案。"],[827.2,829.44,53,"So we're still optimizing the right thing.","所以我们优化的仍然是正确的目标。"],[829.79,836.79,53,"Second, the variance is provably reduced, under reasonable conditions, compared with plain REINFORCE.","第二，在合理的条件下，可以证明它比原始 REINFORCE 的方差更小。"],[837.14,838.91,53,"You don't need to follow the proofs today.","今天你们不需要跟上这些证明。"],[839.26,846.23,53,"The one sentence to remember is the line near the top: same objective in expectation, far less noise.","要记住的一句话是靠近顶部的那一行：期望意义下目标相同，噪声却小得多。"],[847.48,851.95,54,"And in practice, ReMax is lighter and faster than PPO.","在实践中，ReMax 比 PPO 更轻、更快。"],[852.3,854.22,54,"On the left is the architecture.","左边是架构图。"],[854.57,859.56,54,"Because there's no value model, there's simply one fewer big network to store and train.","因为没有价值模型，所以需要存储和训练的大网络就少了一个。"],[859.91,862.4,54,"On the right are the measured costs.","右边是实测的成本。"],[862.75,870.38,54,"Relative to PPO, ReMax uses about fifty-four percent of the GPU memory, and sixty-two percent of the training time.","相对于 PPO，ReMax 只用了约百分之五十四的 GPU 显存和百分之六十二的训练时间。"],[870.73,877.39,54,"There's also a hidden saving: much less hyperparameter tuning, since everything to do with the critic disappears.","还有一个隐藏的节省：调参工作少了很多，因为和评论家相关的一切都消失了。"],[877.74,881.3,54,"The claim at the bottom is the historically important one.","下面这句话在历史上很重要。"],[881.65,887.6,54,"ReMax was the first value-model-free RL algorithm shown to run stably at LLM scale.","ReMax 是第一个被证明能在大模型规模上稳定运行的无价值模型强化学习算法。"],[887.95,893.8,54,"That idea, replacing the critic with extra samples, is exactly what GRPO builds on next.","用额外样本取代评论家，这个思路正是接下来 GRPO 的基础。"],[895.05,899.03,55,"Before we get to GRPO, here's a point that's easy to miss.","在讲 GRPO 之前，有一点很容易被忽略。"],[899.38,905.18,55,"Algorithms drive infrastructure, and infrastructure in turn shapes which algorithms are practical.","算法驱动基础设施，而基础设施反过来又决定了哪些算法是可行的。"],[905.53,910.18,55,"On the left is DeepSpeed-Chat, from Microsoft, twenty twenty-three.","左边是微软 2023 年的 DeepSpeed-Chat。"],[910.53,916.28,55,"It was designed mainly around PPO, and training and inference were coupled, so sampling was slow.","它主要是围绕 PPO 设计的，训练和推理耦合在一起，所以采样很慢。"],[916.63,923.2,55,"On the right is HybridFlow, released as verl, from ByteDance in twenty twenty-four.","右边是字节跳动 2024 年的 HybridFlow，以 verl 的名字发布。"],[923.55,929.06,55,"It supports PPO, ReMax, Safe-RLHF, GRPO and more.","它支持 PPO、ReMax、Safe-RLHF、GRPO 等多种算法。"],[929.41,934.0,55,"And it decouples training from inference, so sampling is fast.","而且它把训练和推理解耦，所以采样很快。"],[934.35,935.66,55,"Why does that matter?","这为什么重要？"],[936.01,939.94,55,"Once sampling becomes cheap, you can afford many samples per prompt.","一旦采样变得便宜，你就能为每个提示生成很多样本。"],[940.29,945.31,55,"And that's exactly what made the next step, GRPO, practical.","而这正是让下一步 GRPO 变得可行的原因。"]]},{"n":5,"title":"GRPO, RLVR and the Frontier of RL for LLMs","blurb":"Group baselines in GRPO and its variants, the move from human preferences to verifiable rewards, asynchronous RL infrastructure, and smarter exploration on hard prompts.","file":"lecture06_part5.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part5.jpg","duration":1226.9,"first":56,"last":80,"slides":[{"n":56,"title":"3.4 From ReMax to GRPO and DAPO","t":0.8},{"n":57,"title":"From ReMax to GRPO: More Samples, Better Baseline","t":27.52},{"n":58,"title":"GRPO: Group Relative Policy Optimization","t":79.17},{"n":59,"title":"PPO vs. GRPO in One Picture (DeepSeekMath)","t":143.88},{"n":60,"title":"ReMax vs. GRPO: Two Ways to Drop the Critic","t":200.15},{"n":64,"title":"The GRPO Family: What Each Variant Fixes","t":258.19},{"n":65,"title":"A Map of RL Algorithms for LLMs","t":329.59},{"n":66,"title":"3.5 From RLHF to RLVR","t":398.31},{"n":67,"title":"SFT Memorizes and RL Generalizes","t":417.7},{"n":68,"title":"Comparison: SFT vs. RLHF vs. RLVR","t":485.89},{"n":69,"title":"RLHF Data vs. RLVR Data: Five Cases","t":549.18},{"n":70,"title":"How RLHF and RLVR Work","t":622.14},{"n":71,"title":"RLHF vs. RLVR — and Why RLVR Took Over","t":689.29},{"n":72,"title":"3.6 Frontier: Infrastructure and Exploration","t":767.5},{"n":73,"title":"Where RL for LLMs Is Going","t":788.32},{"n":74,"title":"Infrastructure: From Synchronous to Asynchronous RL","t":843.11},{"n":75,"title":"GRPO's Open Problem: No Gradient on Hard Prompts","t":897.1},{"n":76,"title":"An Exploration View: Why Are All Samples Wrong?","t":956.66},{"n":77,"title":"Knapsack RL: Spend the Exploration Budget Where It Pays","t":1008.81},{"n":78,"title":"Smarter Exploration: Tree-Structured Rollouts","t":1062.77},{"n":79,"title":"Summary: RL Algorithms for LLMs","t":1113.53},{"n":80,"title":"Incentivize, Don't Teach","t":1163.75}],"sents":[[0.8,6.88,56,"To close the ReMax story: we've dropped the critic, using one greedy answer as the baseline.","为 ReMax 的故事做个收尾：我们用一个贪心答案作为基线，去掉了评论家。"],[7.23,12.27,56,"With faster infrastructure we can afford more samples, so the next step is natural.","有了更快的基础设施，我们能负担更多样本，所以下一步就很自然了。"],[12.62,18.82,56,"The baseline moves from one greedy answer to the average of a whole group, which gives GRPO.","基线从一个贪心答案变成整个组的平均值，这就得到了 GRPO。"],[19.17,26.12,56,"Then DAPO and others redesign clipping and normalization, to keep this stable at scale.","然后 DAPO 等方法重新设计了裁剪和归一化，让它在大规模下保持稳定。"],[27.37,29.34,57,"Here's the transition in one picture.","用一张图展示这个过渡。"],[29.69,31.94,57,"In twenty twenty-three, ReMax.","2023 年，ReMax。"],[32.29,39.07,57,"For a prompt x, we generate one sample y and one greedy answer, and the baseline is the greedy answer's reward.","对一个提示 x，我们生成一个样本 y 和一个贪心答案，基线就是贪心答案的奖励。"],[39.42,43.03,57,"That's a single-sample estimate of how good this prompt usually goes.","这是对这个提示通常表现如何的单样本估计。"],[43.38,46.17,57,"In twenty twenty-four, GRPO.","2024 年，GRPO。"],[46.52,53.68,57,"For the same prompt, we generate N samples, y one through y N, and the baseline is the mean of their rewards.","对同一个提示，我们生成 N 个样本，y1 到 yN，基线是它们奖励的均值。"],[54.03,57.52,57,"That's a multi-sample estimate, so it's more accurate.","这是多样本估计，所以更准确。"],[57.87,61.48,57,"GRPO also divides by the group's standard deviation.","GRPO 还会除以组内的标准差。"],[61.83,69.33,57,"That puts every prompt on the same scale, whether its rewards are naturally spread out or tightly bunched.","这样就把每个提示都放到了同一尺度上，无论它的奖励天然分散还是紧密集中。"],[69.68,77.77,57,"The arrow in the middle is the key: faster infrastructure means we can afford more samples, and more samples buy us a better baseline.","中间这个箭头是关键：更快的基础设施让我们负担得起更多样本，而更多样本换来更好的基线。"],[79.02,84.17,58,"Here's GRPO, group relative policy optimization, with a tiny example.","这是 GRPO，组相对策略优化，配一个小例子。"],[84.52,87.19,58,"One question, four sampled answers.","一个问题，四个采样答案。"],[87.54,95.37,58,"A verifier gives one if correct and zero if wrong, so the rewards are one, zero, one, zero.","验证器对正确答案给一分，错误给零分，所以奖励是一、零、一、零。"],[95.72,97.9,58,"The group mean is zero point five.","组的均值是零点五。"],[98.25,102.75,58,"Normalize by subtracting the mean and dividing by the standard deviation.","归一化的方法是减去均值，再除以标准差。"],[103.1,107.01,58,"The correct answers get plus one, and the wrong ones minus one.","正确答案得到加一，错误答案得到减一。"],[107.36,110.23,58,"Above average goes up, below average goes down.","高于平均的往上推，低于平均的往下压。"],[110.58,114.5,58,"Compared with PPO, the group replaces the value model entirely.","与 PPO 相比，这个组完全取代了价值模型。"],[114.85,118.4,58,"And notice why it fits so well with verifiable rewards.","再注意它为什么和可验证奖励如此契合。"],[118.75,124.9,58,"Zero-one rewards from a checker are exactly where comparing within a group makes sense.","来自检查器的零一奖励，恰恰是组内比较最有意义的场景。"],[125.25,131.08,58,"It was introduced in DeepSeekMath, and then used for DeepSeek-R1.","它在 DeepSeekMath 中被提出，随后被用于 DeepSeek-R1。"],[131.43,139.65,58,"A small personal note: the first author, Zhihong Shao at DeepSeek, also led DeepSeekMath-V2, which we'll see later.","说一点个人的事：第一作者 DeepSeek 的邵智宏，也主导了 DeepSeekMath-V2，我们稍后会讲到。"],[140.0,142.48,58,"And we interned together at Huawei.","我们曾一起在华为实习。"],[143.73,149.34,59,"Here's the same comparison as drawn in the DeepSeekMath paper, and it's worth staring at for a second.","这是 DeepSeekMath 论文中画的同样的对比，值得多看一会儿。"],[149.69,153.59,59,"At the top is the PPO clipped objective we saw earlier.","上面是我们之前看到的 PPO 裁剪目标函数。"],[153.94,158.8,59,"Below it, the PPO pipeline: the policy produces an output o.","下面是 PPO 的流程：策略模型生成输出 o。"],[159.15,164.69,59,"The reference model, reward model and value model, in the red box, all process it.","红框里的参考模型、奖励模型和价值模型都会处理它。"],[165.04,169.25,59,"And GAE combines rewards and values into an advantage.","GAE 再把奖励和价值组合成优势。"],[169.6,173.35,59,"Now look at the GRPO row. The value model is simply gone.","现在看 GRPO 这一行，价值模型直接没了。"],[173.7,179.67,59,"The policy produces a group of outputs, o one to o G, and the reward model scores each one.","策略模型生成一组输出，o1 到 oG，奖励模型给每一个打分。"],[180.02,185.54,59,"A simple group computation turns those rewards into advantages, A one to A G.","一个简单的组计算把这些奖励转换为优势，A1 到 AG。"],[185.89,188.52,59,"The KL to the reference model is still there.","与参考模型之间的 KL 仍然保留着。"],[188.87,196.15,59,"So GRPO keeps PPO's clipped update, but replaces the learned critic with a statistic of the group.","所以 GRPO 保留了 PPO 的裁剪更新，但用组的统计量取代了学习出来的评论家。"],[196.5,198.75,59,"One big network fewer.","少了一个大网络。"],[200.0,207.18,60,"Let's put ReMax and GRPO side by side, because they're two answers to the same question: how do we drop the critic?","我们把 ReMax 和 GRPO 并排比较，因为它们是对同一个问题的两种回答：如何去掉评论家？"],[207.53,212.5,60,"ReMax uses the reward of the greedy answer. GRPO uses the group average.","ReMax 用贪心答案的奖励，GRPO 用组的平均值。"],[212.85,217.28,60,"ReMax needs two rollouts per prompt. GRPO needs G samples.","ReMax 每个提示需要两次 rollout，GRPO 需要 G 个样本。"],[217.63,226.56,60,"ReMax was designed for RLHF with a reward model. GRPO shines in RLVR with zero-one verifier rewards.","ReMax 是为带奖励模型的 RLHF 设计的，GRPO 则在使用零一验证器奖励的 RLVR 中大放异彩。"],[226.91,228.42,60,"Each has a weak spot.","两者各有弱点。"],[228.77,233.38,60,"ReMax has only one sample per prompt, so its estimate is noisier.","ReMax 每个提示只有一个样本，所以估计噪声更大。"],[233.73,235.49,60,"GRPO has a subtler problem.","GRPO 的问题更隐蔽。"],[235.84,243.95,60,"If all samples in a group are correct, or all are wrong, every advantage is zero, and that prompt gives no signal at all.","如果一个组里的样本全对或全错，所有优势都是零，这个提示就完全不提供信号。"],[244.3,246.87,60,"We'll come back to that one in the frontier section.","我们会在前沿部分再回到这个问题。"],[247.22,252.44,60,"And the shared core: no critic, the REINFORCE family, and a KL to the reference.","而它们的共同核心是：没有评论家，属于 REINFORCE 家族，并且对参考模型施加 KL 约束。"],[252.79,256.79,60,"Same idea: let extra samples replace the value model.","思路相同：让额外的样本取代价值模型。"],[258.04,263.9,64,"Once GRPO took off, a whole family of variants appeared, each fixing a specific problem.","GRPO 火起来之后，出现了一整个变体家族，每个都在修复一个具体的问题。"],[264.25,268.22,64,"You don't need to memorize the table, but notice the pattern.","你们不需要背这张表，但要注意其中的规律。"],[268.57,276.27,64,"Dr. GRPO removes the length and standard-deviation normalizations, which created a bias toward certain answer lengths.","Dr. GRPO 去掉了长度和标准差归一化，因为它们会造成对某些答案长度的偏好。"],[276.62,284.23,64,"DAPO tackles entropy collapse with clip-higher, letting low-probability tokens grow faster, so the model keeps exploring.","DAPO 用 clip-higher 来应对熵坍缩，让低概率 token 增长得更快，从而让模型持续探索。"],[284.58,291.34,64,"It also skips groups that are all right or all wrong, and averages the loss at the token level.","它还会跳过全对或全错的组，并在 token 级别对损失取平均。"],[291.69,299.59,64,"GSPO computes the importance ratio per sequence rather than per token, which is much more stable for mixture-of-experts models.","GSPO 按序列而不是按 token 计算重要性比率，这对混合专家模型稳定得多。"],[299.94,305.87,64,"CISPO clips the importance weight instead of dropping tokens, so rare tokens keep their gradient.","CISPO 裁剪的是重要性权重，而不是丢弃 token，所以罕见 token 能保留它们的梯度。"],[306.22,310.97,64,"REINFORCE plus plus normalizes advantages across the whole batch.","REINFORCE++ 在整个批次上对优势做归一化。"],[311.32,317.25,64,"And VAPO goes the other way, and brings back a critic, carefully pre-trained for long chains of thought.","而 VAPO 反其道而行之，重新引入了评论家，并针对长思维链精心做了预训练。"],[317.6,320.09,64,"The one-line takeaway is at the bottom.","一句话的要点在底部。"],[320.44,328.19,64,"Almost all of these fixes are about stability at scale, meaning long answers, long training runs, and big MoE models.","这些修复几乎都是为了大规模下的稳定性，也就是长答案、长时间训练和大型 MoE 模型。"],[329.44,333.71,65,"Here's a map to place everything we've seen, plus a few things we haven't.","这是一张地图，可以把我们见过的一切，以及一些还没讲到的方法，放进去。"],[334.06,339.89,65,"Read it from left to right, from online methods that explore, to offline methods that are cheap.","从左往右读：从会探索的在线方法，到便宜的离线方法。"],[340.24,346.4,65,"On the far left, actor-critic methods with a learned value: PPO, VinePPO, VAPO.","最左边是带学习价值函数的 actor-critic 方法：PPO、VinePPO、VAPO。"],[346.75,356.31,65,"Next, critic-free policy gradient, where the baseline comes from samples: REINFORCE, RLOO, ReMax, GRPO and its variants.","接下来是无评论家的策略梯度，基线来自样本：REINFORCE、RLOO、ReMax、GRPO 及其变体。"],[356.66,364.78,65,"Then offline preference methods with no sampling at all: DPO and its relatives, like IPO, KTO, ORPO and SimPO.","然后是完全不采样的离线偏好方法：DPO 及其亲属，比如 IPO、KTO、ORPO 和 SimPO。"],[365.13,370.65,65,"Plus iterative or online DPO, which moves back toward the middle.","还有迭代式或在线 DPO，它又往中间靠了回去。"],[371.0,379.41,65,"And on the right, self-training: sample, filter the good answers, then imitate them, as in STaR and ReST.","最右边是自训练：采样、筛选出好的答案，再去模仿它们，比如 STaR 和 ReST。"],[379.76,384.77,65,"The note at the bottom adds a second axis: where the reward comes from.","底部的注释加了第二个维度：奖励从哪里来。"],[385.12,392.21,65,"A human-preference reward model, a verifier, a value model, or an LLM judge with a rubric.","人类偏好奖励模型、验证器、价值模型，或者带评分细则的大模型评判者。"],[392.56,396.91,65,"That second axis is the one that drives the rest of today's story.","正是这第二个维度，推动着今天剩下的故事。"],[398.16,400.39,66,"Which brings us to that second axis.","这就把我们带到了第二个维度。"],[400.74,404.67,66,"We've finished the algorithms. Now let's look at the reward itself.","算法讲完了，现在我们来看奖励本身。"],[405.02,409.94,66,"When the answer can be checked automatically, we no longer need a learned reward model at all.","当答案可以被自动检查时，我们就完全不需要学习出来的奖励模型了。"],[410.29,416.3,66,"That shift, from RLHF to RLVR, is what made reasoning models possible.","从 RLHF 到 RLVR 的这一转变，正是推理模型得以出现的原因。"],[417.55,425.56,67,"Before comparing RLHF and RLVR, here's a striking result about RL versus SFT in general.","在比较 RLHF 和 RLVR 之前，先看一个关于强化学习与 SFT 的惊人结果。"],[425.91,431.84,67,"It's from a twenty twenty-five paper titled SFT Memorizes, RL Generalizes.","它来自 2025 年的一篇论文，标题是《SFT 记忆，RL 泛化》。"],[432.19,435.43,67,"The task is visual navigation in V-IRL.","任务是 V-IRL 中的视觉导航。"],[435.78,440.25,67,"The x-axis is training compute, and the y-axis is success rate.","横轴是训练算力，纵轴是成功率。"],[440.6,450.44,67,"Dashed lines are in-distribution. Solid lines are out-of-distribution, meaning test cases with rules the model didn't see in training.","虚线是分布内，实线是分布外，也就是测试用例中的规则是模型在训练时没见过的。"],[450.79,456.5,67,"Look at red, SFT. In-distribution it shoots up to nearly one hundred percent.","看红色的 SFT。分布内，它迅速升到接近百分之百。"],[456.85,463.76,67,"But out-of-distribution it collapses toward zero. It has memorized the training cases.","但在分布外，它跌到接近零。它记住了训练样本。"],[464.11,465.92,67,"Now look at blue, RL.","再看蓝色的 RL。"],[466.27,473.83,67,"It improves more slowly in-distribution, but its out-of-distribution performance keeps climbing, to around eighty-five percent.","它在分布内提升得更慢，但分布外的表现持续攀升，达到约百分之八十五。"],[474.18,480.5,67,"That's the intuition: SFT copies surface patterns, while RL learns something that transfers.","直觉就是：SFT 复制表面模式，而强化学习学到的是能迁移的东西。"],[480.85,484.49,67,"It's one reason the field leaned so hard into RL.","这也是整个领域如此大力投入强化学习的原因之一。"],[485.74,489.69,68,"Here's a compact comparison of the three post-training approaches.","这是三种后训练方法的简明对比。"],[490.04,493.47,68,"SFT learns from step-by-step demonstrations.","SFT 从逐步的示范中学习。"],[493.82,498.87,68,"RLHF learns from human preferences: which outcome is better.","RLHF 从人类偏好中学习：哪个结果更好。"],[499.22,506.52,68,"RLVR, like in DeepSeek-R1-Zero, learns from rule-based rewards: is the outcome correct?","RLVR，比如 DeepSeek-R1-Zero，从基于规则的奖励中学习：结果对不对？"],[506.87,509.77,68,"Look at the row on dependency on human prior.","看“对人类先验的依赖”这一行。"],[510.12,513.82,68,"SFT has the strongest: the human tells you every step.","SFT 的依赖最强：人告诉你每一步。"],[514.17,518.34,68,"RLHF is in the middle: humans only judge outcomes.","RLHF 居中：人只评判结果。"],[518.69,525.36,68,"RLVR is the weakest: a rule just checks the final answer, and the model has to figure out how to get there.","RLVR 最弱：规则只检查最终答案，怎么得到答案要模型自己去摸索。"],[525.71,536.34,68,"In complexity, RLHF is the heaviest, with a reward model plus PPO. RLVR is medium, a verifier plus GRPO.","在复杂度上，RLHF 最重，要奖励模型加 PPO；RLVR 居中，是验证器加 GRPO。"],[536.69,542.06,68,"For stability, SFT is the easiest, and RLHF the hardest.","在稳定性上，SFT 最容易，RLHF 最难。"],[542.41,547.78,68,"The arrow at the bottom is the trend: less human prior, more self-discovery.","底部的箭头就是趋势：更少的人类先验，更多的自我发现。"],[549.03,552.35,69,"Let's make the data difference concrete with five cases.","我们用五个例子把数据上的区别讲具体。"],[552.7,559.88,69,"Creative writing, like a poem about autumn: RLHF data works fine, two poems and a preference.","创意写作，比如写一首关于秋天的诗：RLHF 数据完全适用，两首诗加一个偏好。"],[560.23,564.68,69,"But there's no checkable answer, so RLVR doesn't apply.","但这里没有可检查的答案，所以 RLVR 用不上。"],[565.03,572.51,69,"Safety, like how to pick a lock: preferences work, and you can only write coarse rule-based checks.","安全，比如怎么开锁：偏好数据可用，而规则只能写得很粗略。"],[572.86,575.98,69,"Now math: seventeen times twenty-four.","再看数学：十七乘以二十四。"],[576.33,580.06,69,"With RLHF, humans have to check the work.","用 RLHF 的话，需要人来检查解题过程。"],[580.41,585.99,69,"With RLVR, you compare against four hundred eight, and give a one or a zero.","用 RLVR 的话，只要和四百零八比对，给一分或零分。"],[586.34,592.21,69,"Code: humans reading code is slow and error-prone. Running unit tests is fast and objective.","代码：让人读代码又慢又容易出错，运行单元测试则又快又客观。"],[592.56,597.42,69,"And agent tasks, like booking the cheapest flight to Tokyo.","还有智能体任务，比如预订飞往东京最便宜的航班。"],[597.77,602.73,69,"You can judge the whole transcript, or you can simply check the final booking state.","你可以评判整个交互过程，也可以只检查最终的预订状态。"],[603.08,605.17,69,"So, the summary at the bottom.","所以，底部是总结。"],[605.52,612.15,69,"RLHF data is preference pairs: expensive and subjective, but it works everywhere.","RLHF 数据是偏好对：昂贵又主观，但哪里都能用。"],[612.5,620.74,69,"RLVR data is a prompt plus ground truth or tests: cheap to score at scale, but only for checkable tasks.","RLVR 数据是提示加标准答案或测试：大规模打分很便宜，但只适用于可检查的任务。"],[621.99,627.95,70,"Here are the two pipelines side by side, and this is a good slide to check your understanding.","这里把两条流程并排放在一起，这一页很适合检验你的理解。"],[628.3,630.78,70,"On top, RLHF.","上面是 RLHF。"],[631.13,639.89,70,"Step one: learn a reward model from human-ranked pairs with the Bradley-Terry loss, pushing the chosen answer's score above the rejected one.","第一步：用 Bradley-Terry 损失从人类排序的配对中学习奖励模型，把被选答案的分数推到被拒答案之上。"],[640.24,645.15,70,"Step two: optimize the policy with PPO against that frozen reward model.","第二步：针对这个冻结的奖励模型，用 PPO 优化策略。"],[645.5,650.61,70,"There's a KL penalty to stay close to the SFT model, and a value model on top.","其中有一个 KL 惩罚让它靠近 SFT 模型，此外还要一个价值模型。"],[650.96,652.95,70,"Below, RLVR.","下面是 RLVR。"],[653.3,658.78,70,"A math or code prompt comes with its ground truth or tests.","一个数学或代码提示，附带标准答案或测试。"],[659.13,665.58,70,"The policy samples a group of answers, and a rule-based verifier gives each one a one or a zero.","策略采样一组答案，基于规则的验证器给每个答案一分或零分。"],[665.93,672.71,70,"The group-relative advantage, reward minus mean over standard deviation, feeds a GRPO update.","组相对优势，即奖励减去均值再除以标准差，用于 GRPO 更新。"],[673.06,678.87,70,"Count the models. Below, there's no reward model, and often no critic.","数一数模型。下面这条流程没有奖励模型，通常也没有评论家。"],[679.22,683.48,70,"The rules are hard to hack, and the whole thing scales with compute.","规则很难被投机，而且整个流程能随算力扩展。"],[683.83,687.89,70,"That's the recipe behind DeepSeek-R1 and the o-series.","这正是 DeepSeek-R1 和 o 系列背后的配方。"],[689.14,691.59,71,"So why did RLVR take over?","那么 RLVR 为什么会胜出？"],[691.94,693.97,71,"On the left are the trade-offs.","左边是各自的取舍。"],[694.32,699.25,71,"RLHF handles open-ended goals like helpfulness, style and safety.","RLHF 能处理开放式的目标，比如有用性、风格和安全。"],[699.6,706.88,71,"But its reward is a proxy, so it gets hacked, and labels are costly, noisy and biased.","但它的奖励只是代理，所以会被投机，而且标注昂贵、有噪声、有偏差。"],[707.23,715.02,71,"RLVR gives an exact, hard-to-hack signal, and is cheap enough for millions of rollouts.","RLVR 给出精确、难以投机的信号，而且足够便宜，可以做数百万次 rollout。"],[715.37,720.56,71,"But it only works for checkable tasks, and the zero-one reward is sparse.","但它只适用于可检查的任务，而且零一奖励很稀疏。"],[720.91,725.83,71,"On the right are five reasons it dominates now.","右边是它现在占主导地位的五个原因。"],[726.18,730.78,71,"The signal scales: compute, not labeling, becomes the bottleneck.","信号可扩展：瓶颈变成了算力，而不是标注。"],[731.13,736.25,71,"Reasoning pays off, and math, code and agent tasks are all checkable.","推理很有回报，而数学、代码和智能体任务都是可检查的。"],[736.6,742.18,71,"RL teaches models to use long chains of thought, which gives test-time scaling.","强化学习教会模型使用长思维链，从而带来测试时扩展。"],[742.53,746.89,71,"The stack is simpler, with GRPO needing no reward model and no critic.","技术栈更简单，GRPO 既不需要奖励模型，也不需要评论家。"],[747.24,751.48,71,"And R1-Zero showed publicly that pure RL works.","而 R1-Zero 公开证明了纯强化学习是可行的。"],[751.83,755.91,71,"But read the bottom line: RLHF is not dead.","但请看底部这一行：RLHF 并没有死。"],[756.26,763.99,71,"Open-ended tasks still need preference or rubric rewards, and even R1's final stage uses reward models.","开放式任务仍然需要偏好或评分细则奖励，即使是 R1 的最后阶段也用了奖励模型。"],[764.34,766.1,71,"Real systems use both.","真实的系统两者都用。"],[767.35,771.24,72,"So that's the shift from learned rewards to checked rewards.","以上就是从学习出来的奖励到检查出来的奖励的转变。"],[771.59,774.23,72,"To finish part three, let's look at the frontier.","作为第三部分的收尾，我们来看看前沿。"],[774.58,778.38,72,"With stable algorithms in hand, the bottlenecks move elsewhere.","有了稳定的算法之后，瓶颈转移到了别处。"],[778.73,786.92,72,"They move to systems, keeping GPUs busy, and to exploration, learning from prompts the model can't yet solve.","转移到系统上，也就是让 GPU 保持忙碌；以及转移到探索上，也就是从模型还解不出的提示中学习。"],[788.17,790.77,73,"Here's how I'd summarize the state of the field.","我会这样总结这个领域的现状。"],[791.12,796.74,73,"Algorithms are largely achieved: PPO, ReMax and GRPO give us stable training.","算法基本上已经解决：PPO、ReMax 和 GRPO 让我们能稳定训练。"],[797.09,799.46,73,"What's still in progress are three things.","仍在推进中的有三件事。"],[799.81,806.08,73,"Infrastructure, with systems like verl, OpenRLHF and AReaL, is about training efficiency.","基础设施，比如 verl、OpenRLHF 和 AReaL 这样的系统，关乎训练效率。"],[806.43,812.31,73,"Environments, for math, coding and agents, are about training diversity.","环境，包括数学、编程和智能体环境，关乎训练的多样性。"],[812.66,817.76,73,"That's because the model can only learn skills you have an environment and reward for.","因为模型只能学会那些你为之准备了环境和奖励的技能。"],[818.11,827.47,73,"And exploration is about discovery: getting the model to find genuinely new solutions, not just sharpen what it already knows.","而探索关乎发现：让模型找到真正新的解法，而不只是打磨它已经会的东西。"],[827.82,830.2,73,"The sentence at the bottom is the takeaway.","底部这句话就是要点。"],[830.55,836.01,73,"Once training is stable, the bottleneck moves to systems, environments and exploration.","一旦训练稳定了，瓶颈就转移到系统、环境和探索上。"],[836.36,841.71,73,"Let's look at one example from infrastructure, and then a few from exploration.","我们先看一个基础设施的例子，再看几个探索方面的例子。"],[842.96,848.65,74,"First, infrastructure. The picture contrasts synchronous and asynchronous RL training.","首先是基础设施。这张图对比了同步和异步的强化学习训练。"],[849.0,853.67,74,"In synchronous training, the whole batch of rollouts has to finish before training starts.","在同步训练中，整批 rollout 都必须完成后才能开始训练。"],[854.02,861.93,74,"But answer lengths vary enormously. One rollout might be a few hundred tokens, and another tens of thousands.","但答案长度差异巨大，一个 rollout 可能只有几百个 token，另一个则有几万个。"],[862.28,866.8,74,"So every GPU waits for the slowest rollout, and utilization is poor.","所以每块 GPU 都要等最慢的那个 rollout，利用率很低。"],[867.15,874.07,74,"In asynchronous training, a scheduler keeps generation and training running at the same time, through a queue.","在异步训练中，调度器通过一个队列，让生成和训练同时进行。"],[874.42,880.06,74,"The catch is that some samples were generated by a slightly older version of the policy.","问题在于，有些样本是由稍旧版本的策略生成的。"],[880.41,885.49,74,"So they're a bit stale, and you need corrections for that. But GPUs stay busy.","所以它们有点过时，需要做一些修正，但 GPU 一直保持忙碌。"],[885.84,892.88,74,"This becomes even more important for agentic RL, where rollouts include tool calls with unpredictable latency.","这对智能体强化学习更加重要，因为那里的 rollout 包含延迟不可预测的工具调用。"],[893.23,895.7,74,"We'll come back to that at the end of the lecture.","我们会在这堂课的最后再回到这一点。"],[896.95,901.78,75,"Now exploration, starting with GRPO's open problem.","现在讲探索，先从 GRPO 的一个开放问题开始。"],[902.13,907.13,75,"Look at the llamas. White means a correct answer, and black means wrong.","看这些羊驼。白色代表正确答案，黑色代表错误。"],[907.48,911.68,75,"On the left, a mixed group: three right and one wrong.","左边是一个混合组：三个对，一个错。"],[912.03,918.92,75,"The advantages are non-zero, plus zero point five and minus one point five, so the model learns something.","优势不为零，分别是加零点五和减一点五，所以模型能学到东西。"],[919.27,922.83,75,"On the right, a hard prompt where every sample is wrong.","右边是一个困难的提示，所有样本都是错的。"],[923.18,929.47,75,"The rewards are all zero, so the mean is zero, every advantage is zero, and the gradient is zero.","奖励全为零，所以均值为零，每个优势都为零，梯度也为零。"],[929.82,935.07,75,"That prompt is completely wasted, no matter how much compute you spent sampling it.","这个提示被完全浪费了，无论你花了多少算力去采样它。"],[935.42,942.65,75,"And over training, the share of these unsolvable prompts drops only slowly, so accuracy gains slow down too.","而且在训练过程中，这些“无解”提示的占比下降得很慢，所以准确率的提升也随之放缓。"],[943.0,949.54,75,"The core issue, in red: on hard prompts all samples look the same, so the gradient vanishes.","红色的核心问题是：在困难提示上，所有样本看起来都一样，所以梯度消失了。"],[949.89,955.26,75,"And these hard prompts are exactly the ones we most want to learn from.","而这些困难提示，恰恰是我们最想从中学习的。"],[956.51,960.09,76,"So why are all samples wrong? There are two views.","那么，为什么所有样本都错了？有两种观点。"],[960.44,965.12,76,"The old view: the model lacks the knowledge. It simply can't solve this prompt.","旧观点：模型缺乏知识，它根本解不出这个提示。"],[965.47,971.46,76,"The new view, from the Knapsack RL paper: maybe the model just hasn't tried enough times.","新观点来自 Knapsack RL 论文：也许模型只是尝试的次数还不够。"],[971.81,973.77,76,"The theorem formalizes this.","这个定理把它形式化了。"],[974.12,986.95,76,"If a prompt's success rate is p, the expected number of rollouts until you first get a useful, non-zero gradient is one over p, plus one over one minus p, minus one.","如果一个提示的成功率是 p，那么首次得到有用的非零梯度所需 rollout 的期望次数，是 p 分之一加上一减 p 分之一，再减一。"],[987.3,990.1,76,"For small p, that's roughly one over p.","当 p 很小时，大约就是 p 分之一。"],[990.45,992.45,76,"So look at the rule of thumb on the right.","所以看右边的经验法则。"],[992.8,999.39,76,"If the model solves a prompt one percent of the time, you need around a hundred rollouts before you see a single useful signal.","如果模型只有百分之一的概率解出某个提示，你需要大约一百次 rollout 才能看到一个有用的信号。"],[999.74,1003.27,76,"But GRPO typically gives every prompt the same eight or so.","但 GRPO 通常给每个提示同样的大约八次。"],[1003.62,1007.41,76,"Hard prompts aren't hopeless. They're under-sampled.","困难提示并非没有希望，只是采样不够。"],[1008.66,1012.82,77,"The natural fix is to stop giving every prompt the same budget.","自然的解决办法，就是不再给每个提示相同的预算。"],[1013.17,1018.26,77,"At the top, uniform allocation: every prompt gets the same number of rollouts.","上面是均匀分配：每个提示得到相同数量的 rollout。"],[1018.61,1022.28,77,"The budget is spread thin, and hard prompts are never solved.","预算被摊得很薄，困难提示永远解不出来。"],[1022.63,1031.4,77,"Below, task-aware allocation: treat rollouts as items in a knapsack, and give more budget to the prompts where extra rollouts actually pay off.","下面是任务感知分配：把 rollout 当作背包里的物品，把更多预算给那些多采样确实有回报的提示。"],[1031.75,1039.21,77,"The value of each allocation is the probability of getting a non-zero gradient, times the information gain from it.","每种分配的价值，等于得到非零梯度的概率，乘以由此带来的信息增益。"],[1039.56,1046.85,77,"Easy prompts that are always solved don't need many rollouts. Prompts at the edge of the model's ability get more.","总能解出的简单提示不需要很多 rollout，而处在模型能力边缘的提示会得到更多。"],[1047.2,1052.73,77,"Then you solve it as a classic knapsack optimization, under a fixed total budget.","然后在固定的总预算下，把它当作经典的背包优化问题来求解。"],[1053.08,1061.37,77,"The point is simple: the same compute, spent more wisely, turns wasted hard prompts into training signal.","要点很简单：同样的算力，花得更聪明，就能把浪费的困难提示变成训练信号。"],[1062.62,1068.31,78,"A second idea for smarter exploration is to change the shape of the rollouts themselves.","更聪明探索的第二个想法，是改变 rollout 本身的形状。"],[1068.66,1072.65,78,"On the top is vanilla sampling: every sample starts again from the prompt.","上面是普通采样：每个样本都从提示重新开始。"],[1073.0,1078.55,78,"So if eight answers share the same first few steps, you pay to generate those steps eight times.","所以如果八个答案共享相同的前几步，你就要为这几步付出八次生成的代价。"],[1078.9,1082.65,78,"Below is TreePO. Rollouts are organized as a tree.","下面是 TreePO，rollout 被组织成一棵树。"],[1083.0,1088.84,78,"They share prefixes, branch at promising points, and reuse cached states.","它们共享前缀，在有希望的节点分叉，并复用缓存的状态。"],[1089.19,1095.95,78,"That saves compute on the shared parts, and lets you spend it exploring different continuations where it matters.","这在共享部分节省了算力，让你能把它花在关键之处、去探索不同的后续。"],[1096.3,1101.89,78,"The paper reports roughly thirty percent more efficient exploration at the same compute.","论文报告，在相同算力下，探索效率大约提高了百分之三十。"],[1102.24,1106.03,78,"Notice the link to the search methods we'll see later in part five.","注意这和我们稍后在第五部分会看到的搜索方法之间的联系。"],[1106.38,1112.13,78,"Tree search is coming back, not at inference time, but inside RL training.","树搜索正在回归，不是在推理时，而是在强化学习训练之中。"],[1113.38,1117.27,79,"Let's wrap up part three with three problems and three answers.","我们用三个问题和三个答案来总结第三部分。"],[1117.62,1122.36,79,"Too much data and compute, so we need computation-efficient algorithms.","数据和算力太多，所以我们需要计算高效的算法。"],[1122.71,1126.21,79,"That took us from PPO back to REINFORCE.","这把我们从 PPO 带回到 REINFORCE。"],[1126.56,1133.08,79,"Heterogeneous data and unstable training, so we need low-variance, stable algorithms.","数据异质、训练不稳定，所以我们需要低方差、稳定的算法。"],[1133.43,1138.29,79,"That's ReMax, then GRPO, then DAPO and its relatives.","这就是 ReMax，然后是 GRPO，再然后是 DAPO 及其同类。"],[1138.64,1146.41,79,"And once training is stable, the focus moves to exploration: finding new knowledge and new abilities.","而一旦训练稳定，重点就转向探索：发现新的知识和新的能力。"],[1146.76,1152.81,79,"That happens through agentic training, asynchronous RL, tree search and budget allocation.","途径包括智能体训练、异步强化学习、树搜索和预算分配。"],[1153.16,1158.9,79,"If you remember one thing: most of the algorithm story is about how to get a good baseline cheaply.","如果只记住一件事：算法的故事大部分是关于如何廉价地得到一个好的基线。"],[1159.25,1162.35,79,"And the frontier is about how to explore.","而前沿则是关于如何探索。"],[1163.6,1168.48,80,"Let's close the first act with a slogan: incentivize, don't teach.","我们用一句口号结束第一幕：激励，而不是教。"],[1168.83,1176.74,80,"With imitation learning, SFT, we hand the model human-written responses, and those carry our biases and our limits.","在模仿学习也就是 SFT 中，我们把人写的回答交给模型，而这些回答带着我们的偏见和局限。"],[1177.09,1186.05,80,"With RL on final rewards, especially rule-based ones, we only say whether the outcome was right, and let the model find its own way there.","而在基于最终奖励、尤其是基于规则奖励的强化学习中，我们只告诉模型结果对不对，让它自己找到通往答案的路。"],[1186.4,1188.79,80,"The analogy is AlphaGo Zero.","可以类比 AlphaGo Zero。"],[1189.14,1192.84,80,"Learning from human game records can't easily beat humans.","从人类棋谱中学习，很难打败人类。"],[1193.19,1198.16,80,"But learning from the win or loss signal alone discovered strategies nobody had played.","但仅从输赢信号中学习，却发现了没有人下过的策略。"],[1198.51,1209.08,80,"DeepSeek-R1-Zero applies exactly that idea to language: skip SFT, and run RL with verifiable rewards directly on the base model.","DeepSeek-R1-Zero 把完全相同的思路用在语言上：跳过 SFT，直接在基座模型上做基于可验证奖励的强化学习。"],[1209.43,1212.13,80,"And that's the bridge to the second act.","这就是通往第二幕的桥梁。"],[1212.48,1217.83,80,"So far, RL has been about alignment: making the model behave the way people prefer.","到目前为止，强化学习一直关乎对齐：让模型按照人们偏好的方式行事。"],[1218.18,1225.06,80,"Now we'll see what happens when the same tool, fed by verifiable rewards, is used to make the model think.","现在我们来看，当同样的工具以可验证奖励为驱动、被用来让模型思考时，会发生什么。"]]},{"n":6,"title":"Large Reasoning Models: OpenAI o1 and o3","blurb":"From emergent chain-of-thought to long CoT: how o1 outlines, plans, backtracks and self-evaluates, reasoning tokens, train- and test-time compute, and o3.","file":"lecture06_part6.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part6.jpg","duration":1164.1,"first":81,"last":106,"slides":[{"n":81,"title":"4 Large Reasoning Models","t":0.8},{"n":82,"title":"It Changes Because of RL and LRMs","t":35.05},{"n":83,"title":"Recap: Chain-of-Thought Used to Be an Emergent Ability of Large LLMs","t":86.88},{"n":84,"title":"Complex Reasoning Tasks with Chain-of-Thought (CoT)","t":133.83},{"n":85,"title":"Longer Chain-of-Thought (CoT)","t":181.67},{"n":86,"title":"4.2 OpenAI o1 and o3","t":234.28},{"n":87,"title":"Examples from OpenAI o1: Math","t":256.56},{"n":88,"title":"Examples from OpenAI o1: Health Science","t":300.18},{"n":89,"title":"o1's Chain of Thought","t":347.61},{"n":90,"title":"o1 CoT: Outlining (a Coding Example)","t":390.45},{"n":91,"title":"o1 CoT: Planning","t":424.85},{"n":92,"title":"o1 CoT: Backtracking","t":461.42},{"n":93,"title":"o1 CoT: Self-Evaluation","t":496.63},{"n":94,"title":"Summary: What Long CoT Gives Us","t":532.63},{"n":95,"title":"How o1 Works","t":588.63},{"n":96,"title":"o1 Techniques: Scaling Train-Time and Test-Time Compute","t":624.44},{"n":97,"title":"Implementation: Reasoning Tokens","t":678.36},{"n":98,"title":"Hacking Reasoning Tokens: How Models Catch Up Fast","t":731.28},{"n":99,"title":"Why Hacking Is Getting Harder","t":806.13},{"n":100,"title":"o1: RL Teaches the Model How to Think","t":880.99},{"n":101,"title":"AIME: o1 Improves with Train- and Test-Time Compute","t":915.79},{"n":102,"title":"OpenAI o3 and o4-mini","t":953.36},{"n":103,"title":"o3 and o4-mini on Reasoning Benchmarks","t":998.43},{"n":104,"title":"Demo: o1 Reasoning over Images (1/2)","t":1055.21},{"n":105,"title":"Demo: o1 Reasoning over Images (2/2)","t":1092.19},{"n":106,"title":"Thinking with Images: Zooming and Rotating","t":1119.67}],"sents":[[0.8,2.65,81,"That closes the first act.","第一幕到此结束。"],[3.0,10.3,81,"We now have the tool, RL, and we've seen the reward shift from human preferences to verifiers.","我们现在有了工具，也就是强化学习，也看到了奖励从人类偏好转向了验证器。"],[10.65,18.6,81,"Part four, the start of the reasoning act, asks what happens when you apply that tool with verifiable rewards at scale.","第四部分是推理这一幕的开始，它要问：当你在大规模上用可验证奖励来使用这个工具时，会发生什么？"],[18.95,26.12,81,"The answer is large reasoning models: models that learn to think longer, check their own work and backtrack.","答案是大型推理模型：学会更长时间思考、检查自己的工作并回溯的模型。"],[26.47,33.65,81,"We'll look at what reasoning means, at OpenAI's o1 and o3, and at how we measure it.","我们会看推理意味着什么，看 OpenAI 的 o1 和 o3，以及如何衡量推理能力。"],[34.9,41.14,82,"Here's why this matters, in one chart: progress on AI benchmarks over the past five years.","用一张图说明这为什么重要：过去五年 AI 基准测试的进展。"],[41.49,43.22,82,"Look at the left side first.","先看左边。"],[43.57,51.87,82,"TriviaQA, MMLU, grade-school math and competition math climbed steadily from twenty twenty to twenty twenty-three.","TriviaQA、MMLU、小学数学和竞赛数学，从 2020 年到 2023 年稳步攀升。"],[52.22,54.76,82,"And most are now close to saturated.","其中大多数现在已经接近饱和。"],[55.11,59.08,82,"Now look at the right side, around twenty twenty-four and twenty twenty-five.","再看右边，大约 2024 年和 2025 年。"],[59.43,69.57,82,"Graduate-level science in GPQA, the AIME math competition, and real software engineering tasks in SWE-bench Verified all shoot up almost vertically.","GPQA 中的研究生水平科学、AIME 数学竞赛，以及 SWE-bench Verified 中的真实软件工程任务，都几乎垂直上升。"],[69.92,72.98,82,"Even Humanity's Last Exam is starting to climb.","就连“人类最后的考试”也开始攀升了。"],[73.33,78.51,82,"Those steep curves line up with the arrival of large reasoning models trained with RL.","这些陡峭的曲线，恰好与用强化学习训练的大型推理模型的出现时间吻合。"],[78.86,82.48,82,"Benchmarks that looked out of reach for years moved in months.","那些多年来看似遥不可及的基准，在几个月内就被突破。"],[82.83,85.48,82,"That's the phenomenon this part tries to explain.","这正是这一部分想要解释的现象。"],[86.73,90.96,83,"Let's start with a quick recap of chain-of-thought, which you may have seen before.","我们先快速回顾一下思维链，你们之前可能见过。"],[91.31,97.63,83,"In twenty twenty-two, Wei and colleagues showed that prompting a model to think step by step helps a lot.","2022 年，Wei 等人证明，提示模型一步步思考会有很大帮助。"],[97.98,102.87,83,"But only once the model is big, roughly one hundred billion parameters.","但前提是模型足够大，大约一千亿参数。"],[103.22,109.95,83,"Smaller models produce chains that sound fluent but don't follow logically, and chain-of-thought can even hurt them.","更小的模型生成的推理链听起来流畅，逻辑上却不成立，思维链甚至会损害它们的表现。"],[110.3,115.08,83,"So at that time, reasoning looked like a by-product of scale.","所以在那个时候，推理看起来像是规模的副产品。"],[115.43,120.47,83,"Something you could coax out with the right prompt, if the model was big enough.","只要模型足够大，用对提示就能把它引出来。"],[120.82,124.71,83,"The question for this part, in the red box, is the big shift.","红框中这一部分的问题，就是一个重大转变。"],[125.06,132.43,83,"Can training, and RL in particular, rather than scale alone, actually teach a model to reason?","训练，尤其是强化学习，而不仅仅是规模，能否真正教会模型推理？"],[133.68,136.61,84,"Here's what a typical chain-of-thought solution looks like.","这是一个典型的思维链解答的样子。"],[136.96,139.59,84,"The problem is a competition-style word problem.","题目是一道竞赛风格的应用题。"],[139.94,148.23,84,"Aya walks nine kilometres at two different speeds, with the same coffee-shop stop each time, and we need the total time at a third speed.","Aya 以两种不同的速度走九公里，每次都在咖啡店停留相同的时间，我们要求她以第三种速度行走时的总时间。"],[148.58,151.12,84,"The solution is clean and linear.","解答干净利落、线性推进。"],[151.47,154.36,84,"Set up two equations, and subtract them.","列出两个方程，然后相减。"],[154.71,158.68,84,"Solve a quadratic to get s equals two point five.","解一个二次方程，得到 s 等于二点五。"],[159.03,164.47,84,"Find that the coffee stop takes zero point four hours, and compute the answer, two hundred four minutes.","求出咖啡店停留时间为零点四小时，再算出答案，两百零四分钟。"],[164.82,170.73,84,"Notice what's missing. There's no hesitation, no checking, no wait, is that right?","注意少了什么：没有犹豫，没有检查，没有“等等，这对吗？”"],[171.08,173.9,84,"It's the polished solution you'd find in an answer key.","这是你会在标准答案里看到的那种打磨过的解答。"],[174.25,180.27,84,"Keep this in mind, because next we'll see the same problem solved in a very different style.","记住这一点，因为接下来我们会看到同一道题用截然不同的风格来解。"],[181.52,186.61,85,"Here's the same problem solved by a reasoning model, and look at the red sentences.","这是推理模型对同一道题的解答，请看红色的句子。"],[186.96,192.75,85,"Wait, let me make sure. Now check if that makes sense. Yes, seems correct.","“等等，让我确认一下。”“现在检查一下这是否合理。”“是的，看起来是对的。”"],[193.1,197.51,85,"The model restates the problem, and lists the key facts.","模型重述了题目，并列出关键事实。"],[197.86,201.81,85,"It double-checks that the coffee time is the same in both cases.","它再次确认两种情况下的咖啡店时间是相同的。"],[202.16,210.57,85,"It solves the quadratic, verifies the square root, and finally checks the answer, two hundred four minutes, against the conditions.","它解出二次方程，验证了平方根，最后对照条件检查答案，两百零四分钟。"],[210.92,215.41,85,"This is what we mean by long chain-of-thought plus self-reflection.","这就是我们所说的长思维链加自我反思。"],[215.76,221.28,85,"The chain is much longer than the clean solution we just saw, and that's not inefficiency.","这条链比我们刚看到的简洁解答长得多，但这并不是低效。"],[221.63,227.33,85,"It's the model searching, catching potential mistakes, and verifying itself.","这是模型在搜索、在捕捉潜在错误、在自我验证。"],[227.68,232.88,85,"This behaviour, more than anything else, is what defines a large reasoning model.","这种行为，比其他任何东西都更能定义一个大型推理模型。"],[234.13,236.95,86,"We've seen what a reasoning trace looks like.","我们已经看到了推理过程是什么样子的。"],[237.3,244.17,86,"Now let's look at the model that started this wave: OpenAI's o1, followed by o3.","现在来看掀起这股浪潮的模型：OpenAI 的 o1，以及之后的 o3。"],[244.52,251.35,86,"The key claim from o1 is that RL on chain-of-thought keeps improving with two kinds of compute.","o1 的核心论断是：在思维链上做强化学习，会随着两种算力的增加而持续提升。"],[251.7,255.16,86,"More training, and more thinking time at inference.","更多的训练，以及推理时更长的思考时间。"],[256.41,263.2,87,"Here's an example from OpenAI's o1 announcement: a hard math problem about a monic polynomial.","这是 OpenAI 发布 o1 时的一个例子：一道关于首一多项式的数学难题。"],[263.55,267.75,87,"On the left, GPT-4o jumps straight into algebra.","左边，GPT-4o 直接开始做代数推导。"],[268.1,272.83,87,"On the right, o1-preview first shows Thought for five seconds.","右边，o1-preview 先显示“思考了五秒”。"],[273.18,279.3,87,"Then it carefully restates what's given, and what needs to be found, before solving.","然后在求解之前，仔细重述了已知条件和要求的东西。"],[279.65,284.58,87,"The visible difference is that o1 spends time thinking before answering.","肉眼可见的区别是，o1 在回答之前会花时间思考。"],[284.93,289.85,87,"And on hard math like this, that thinking translates into much higher accuracy.","而在这样的数学难题上，这种思考会转化为高得多的准确率。"],[290.2,298.78,87,"You can find the full set of examples, cipher, coding, crossword, science, on OpenAI's blog post linked at the bottom.","完整的例子，包括密码、编程、填字、科学等，可以在底部链接的 OpenAI 博客文章中找到。"],[300.03,304.24,88,"And it's not just math. Here's a health science example from the same post.","而且不只是数学。这是同一篇文章中的一个健康科学例子。"],[304.59,313.56,88,"There's a list of phenotypes: intellectual disability, developmental delay, macrodontia, a triangular face and so on.","这里有一串表型：智力障碍、发育迟缓、巨牙症、三角脸等等。"],[313.91,316.11,88,"And the model has to make a diagnosis.","模型需要做出诊断。"],[316.46,325.88,88,"o1 reasons through which conditions match and which can be excluded, and arrives at KBG syndrome, explaining how each phenotype fits.","o1 推理哪些病症吻合、哪些可以排除，最终得出 KBG 综合征，并解释每个表型如何对应。"],[326.23,334.6,88,"This kind of differential diagnosis is real reasoning: generate hypotheses, check them against evidence, eliminate.","这种鉴别诊断是真正的推理：提出假设，对照证据检验，再逐一排除。"],[334.95,340.61,88,"That's especially interesting for us, because medical reasoning is a domain our own group works on.","这对我们来说尤其有意思，因为医学推理正是我们课题组研究的领域。"],[340.96,346.21,88,"And we'll come back to it in part six, with HuatuoGPT-o1.","我们会在第六部分通过 HuatuoGPT-o1 再回到这个话题。"],[347.46,349.94,89,"So what does o1 actually learn?","那么，o1 到底学到了什么？"],[350.29,354.56,89,"Here's OpenAI's own description, and every sentence names a skill.","这是 OpenAI 自己的描述，每一句都点出了一项技能。"],[354.91,358.69,89,"It learns to hone its chain of thought and refine its strategies.","它学会打磨自己的思维链，并改进所用的策略。"],[359.04,362.59,89,"It learns to recognize and correct its mistakes.","它学会识别并纠正自己的错误。"],[362.94,366.21,89,"It learns to break tricky steps into simpler ones.","它学会把棘手的步骤拆分成更简单的步骤。"],[366.56,371.46,89,"And it learns to try a different approach when the current one isn't working.","当前方法行不通时，它学会尝试不同的方法。"],[371.81,375.93,89,"Notice that none of these are facts. They're thinking habits.","注意，这些都不是事实知识，而是思维习惯。"],[376.28,380.86,89,"The kind of thing a good student develops over years of practice.","就是一个好学生经过多年练习才养成的那种东西。"],[381.21,389.05,89,"Over the next four slides, we'll look at short excerpts of o1's chain of thought that show each of these habits in action.","接下来四页，我们会看 o1 思维链的几个简短片段，分别展示这些习惯是如何起作用的。"],[390.3,392.33,90,"First habit: outlining.","第一个习惯：列提纲。"],[392.68,398.79,90,"In this coding example, before writing any code, the model writes an implementation outline.","在这个编程例子中，模型在写任何代码之前，先写了一个实现提纲。"],[399.14,404.32,90,"Capture the input string, remove spaces, and parse it into arrays.","获取输入字符串，去掉空格，再把它解析成数组。"],[404.67,411.55,90,"It even notices the specific input format, brackets and commas, and plans how to split it row by row.","它甚至注意到了具体的输入格式，也就是方括号和逗号，并计划如何逐行拆分。"],[411.9,416.13,90,"This is exactly what a good programmer does: plan the structure before typing.","这正是好程序员会做的事：先规划结构，再动手敲代码。"],[416.48,423.45,90,"It reduces errors, because the hard decisions are made explicitly, up front.","这样能减少错误，因为困难的决定都被明确地提前做好了。"],[424.7,428.06,91,"Second habit: planning and strategy selection.","第二个习惯：规划与策略选择。"],[428.41,430.75,91,"Here the model faces a cipher puzzle.","这里模型面对的是一个密码谜题。"],[431.1,435.14,91,"Notice the language: the cipher seems connected to the plaintext.","注意它的措辞：“密文似乎和明文有联系。”"],[435.49,440.43,91,"Given the time constraints, perhaps the easiest way is to try to see patterns.","“考虑到时间限制，也许最简单的办法是试着找规律。”"],[440.78,444.41,91,"Option one: try to find a mapping from letters to letters.","“方案一：尝试找出字母到字母的映射。”"],[444.76,449.48,91,"The model is explicitly weighing approaches, and choosing one.","模型在明确地权衡不同方法，并从中选择一种。"],[449.83,457.36,91,"Then it sets up a concrete first step: write the ciphertext and plaintext letters on top of each other.","然后它设定了具体的第一步：把密文和明文的字母上下对齐写出来。"],[457.71,460.02,91,"That's planning, in natural language.","这就是用自然语言进行的规划。"],[461.27,463.53,92,"Third habit: backtracking.","第三个习惯：回溯。"],[463.88,465.86,92,"This one is a polynomial problem.","这是一道多项式题。"],[466.21,473.55,92,"The model computes something, and then says: wait, actually, this may not help us directly without specific terms.","模型计算了一些东西，然后说：“等等，其实如果没有具体的项，这可能帮不上直接的忙。”"],[473.9,477.34,92,"An alternative is to consider the known polynomials.","“另一种办法是考虑已知的多项式。”"],[477.69,480.79,92,"That wait, actually, is the important part.","这句“等等，其实”才是关键。"],[481.14,487.0,92,"The model realizes it's heading down an unproductive path, abandons it, and tries something else.","模型意识到自己正走在一条无效的路上，于是放弃它，转而尝试别的办法。"],[487.35,491.78,92,"In a classical search algorithm, this is backtracking in a search tree.","在经典的搜索算法中，这就是在搜索树上回溯。"],[492.13,495.23,92,"Here it happens inside a single stream of text.","而在这里，它发生在一条连续的文本流之中。"],[496.48,499.25,93,"And the fourth habit: self-evaluation.","第四个习惯：自我评估。"],[499.6,503.21,93,"This is a verbal reasoning question with multiple options.","这是一道有多个选项的语言推理题。"],[503.56,506.04,93,"The model goes through them one by one.","模型逐一分析这些选项。"],[506.39,510.36,93,"Option A... is that a good explanation? Hmm.","“选项 A……这是一个好的解释吗？嗯。”"],[510.71,513.96,93,"Option B... does this make sense with the main clause?","“选项 B……这和主句意思搭得上吗？”"],[514.31,517.99,93,"It's critiquing its own candidate answers before committing.","它在做出决定之前，先批判性地审视自己的候选答案。"],[518.34,522.88,93,"That's the same skill as a verifier, just built into the model's own thinking.","这和验证器的能力是一样的，只不过内置在了模型自己的思考里。"],[523.23,531.23,93,"Keep this idea of self-verification in mind. It comes back in a big way with DeepSeekMath-V2 later on.","请记住这个自我验证的想法，它稍后会在 DeepSeekMath-V2 中以重要的方式回归。"],[532.48,536.84,94,"Let's summarize what long chain-of-thought gives us, in three points.","我们用三点来总结长思维链带给我们的东西。"],[537.19,538.95,94,"First, test-time scaling.","第一，测试时扩展。"],[539.3,546.13,94,"If the model can think longer on harder problems, then spending more compute at inference buys better answers.","如果模型能在更难的问题上思考更久，那么在推理时投入更多算力，就能换来更好的答案。"],[546.48,548.7,94,"That's a new dial we didn't have before.","这是我们以前没有的一个新旋钮。"],[549.05,554.82,94,"Second, chain-of-thought starts to look like search and planning in the classical sense.","第二，思维链开始像经典意义上的搜索和规划。"],[555.17,558.95,94,"Outline, plan, try, backtrack, evaluate.","列提纲、规划、尝试、回溯、评估。"],[559.3,564.76,94,"All the habits we just saw are search operations, expressed in language.","我们刚才看到的所有习惯，都是用语言表达出来的搜索操作。"],[565.11,571.17,94,"Third, and this is the crucial one for today: RL was needed to induce this behaviour.","第三点，也是今天最关键的一点：需要强化学习才能诱导出这种行为。"],[571.52,574.2,94,"Prompting alone doesn't reliably produce it.","仅靠提示并不能可靠地产生它。"],[574.55,581.64,94,"The model has to be rewarded for getting answers right, and then it discovers that thinking like this pays off.","模型必须因为答对而获得奖励，然后它会发现，这样思考是有回报的。"],[581.99,587.23,94,"So how did OpenAI train o1 to think like this? Let's look at what they told us.","那么 OpenAI 是如何训练 o1 这样思考的？我们来看看他们透露了什么。"],[588.48,592.73,95,"Here's how OpenAI described the training, in their own words.","下面是 OpenAI 用他们自己的话对训练过程的描述。"],[593.08,599.0,95,"They trained the models to spend more time thinking through problems before responding, much like a person would.","他们训练模型在回答之前花更多时间把问题想清楚，就像人一样。"],[599.35,605.74,95,"Through training, the models learn to refine their thinking, try different strategies, and recognize their mistakes.","通过训练，模型学会打磨自己的思考过程、尝试不同的策略，并认识到自己的错误。"],[606.09,610.28,95,"Notice that they don't say they hand-wrote these thinking patterns.","注意，他们并没有说这些思考模式是人手工写出来的。"],[610.63,615.47,95,"The patterns are learned. What they don't publish is exactly how.","这些模式是学出来的。他们没有公开的，恰恰是具体怎么学的。"],[615.82,623.04,95,"So the next few slides are about the pieces OpenAI did reveal: how performance scales, and how reasoning tokens are handled.","所以接下来几页讲的是 OpenAI 确实透露了的部分：性能如何扩展，以及推理 token 是怎么处理的。"],[624.29,628.24,96,"This is probably the most important plot from the o1 release.","这大概是 o1 发布中最重要的一张图。"],[628.59,633.88,96,"Both panels show o1's accuracy on AIME, the American math olympiad qualifier.","两个子图展示的都是 o1 在 AIME 上的准确率，AIME 是美国数学奥赛的资格赛。"],[634.23,640.42,96,"On the left, the x-axis is training compute, meaning how much RL you do, on a log scale.","左图的横轴是训练算力，也就是做了多少强化学习，用的是对数刻度。"],[640.77,646.09,96,"Accuracy rises steadily, from around thirty percent to nearly seventy.","准确率稳步上升，从大约百分之三十涨到接近百分之七十。"],[646.44,652.6,96,"On the right, the x-axis is test-time compute, meaning how long the model thinks per problem.","右图的横轴是测试时算力，也就是模型在每道题上思考多久。"],[652.95,657.37,96,"Accuracy rises from around twenty to over seventy percent.","准确率从大约百分之二十涨到百分之七十以上。"],[657.72,661.04,96,"So there are two scaling laws here, not one.","所以这里有两条扩展规律，而不是一条。"],[661.39,668.29,96,"You can make the model better by training it with more RL, and you can make the same model better by letting it think longer.","你可以用更多强化学习训练让模型变强，也可以让同一个模型思考更久来变强。"],[668.64,676.96,96,"And as the quote says, the constraints on scaling this are quite different from pre-training: it's not about finding more internet text.","正如引文所说，这种扩展的约束和预训练很不一样：它不在于找到更多的互联网文本。"],[678.21,684.47,97,"How does the thinking work at the interface level? o1 introduced reasoning tokens.","在接口层面，思考是怎么实现的？o1 引入了推理 token。"],[684.82,690.76,97,"The model first generates reasoning tokens, its private thinking, then produces the visible answer.","模型先生成推理 token，也就是它私下的思考，然后输出可见的答案。"],[691.11,695.27,97,"And then the reasoning tokens are discarded from the context.","然后这些推理 token 会从上下文中被丢弃。"],[695.62,696.67,97,"Look at the diagram.","看这张示意图。"],[697.02,703.63,97,"In a multi-turn conversation, the input and output of each turn are carried forward to the next turn.","在多轮对话中，每一轮的输入和输出都会被带到下一轮。"],[703.98,707.65,97,"But the grey reasoning blocks are dropped each time.","但灰色的推理块每次都会被丢掉。"],[708.0,711.2,97,"That keeps the context from filling up with old thinking.","这样上下文就不会被旧的思考内容塞满。"],[711.55,716.95,97,"Two practical consequences. First, you pay for reasoning tokens even though you don't see them.","这带来两个实际后果。第一，推理 token 你看不见，但要为它付费。"],[717.3,726.57,97,"And look at the bottom: if reasoning plus output exceeds the context window, here one hundred twenty-eight K tokens, the output gets truncated.","再看底部：如果推理加输出超过了上下文窗口，这里是 128K token，输出就会被截断。"],[726.92,729.88,97,"So long thinking has a real cost.","所以长时间思考是有真实代价的。"],[731.13,737.44,98,"Once people realized that reasoning is partly bought with tokens, other labs found cheap ways to catch up.","当人们意识到推理能力部分是用 token 买来的，其他实验室就找到了廉价的追赶方法。"],[737.79,739.08,98,"There are four levers.","一共有四个杠杆。"],[739.43,744.68,98,"One, copy the traces: distill long chains of thought from a strong teacher.","第一，复制推理轨迹：从强大的教师模型那里蒸馏长思维链。"],[745.03,756.68,98,"s1 used just one thousand curated traces and LIMO used eight hundred seventeen, and both got big AIME gains from SFT alone.","s1 只用了一千条精选轨迹，LIMO 只用了 817 条，仅靠 SFT 就在 AIME 上大幅提升。"],[757.03,763.91,98,"Two, force longer thinking: s1's budget forcing appends the word wait when the model tries to stop.","第二，强制更长的思考：s1 的预算强制方法会在模型想停下时追加一个 Wait。"],[764.26,767.71,98,"So the model re-checks, and often fixes its answer.","于是模型会重新检查，而且常常能改正答案。"],[768.06,775.27,98,"Three, think more by default: thinking always on, maximum effort, longer RL rollouts.","第三，默认多思考：思考模式常开、推理强度拉满、RL rollout 更长。"],[775.62,781.0,98,"Four, think in parallel: sample many chains and vote, or pick with a verifier.","第四，并行思考：采样多条思维链然后投票，或者用验证器挑选。"],[781.35,784.11,98,"That's what the heavy or deep think modes do.","这就是 Heavy 或 Deep Think 模式在做的事。"],[784.46,791.81,98,"The box at the bottom shows how far this has gone in two thousand twenty-six: some models spend most of their output on reasoning.","底部的框展示了到二〇二六年这件事走了多远：有些模型的大部分输出都花在了推理上。"],[792.16,800.17,98,"And the red line is the warning. These gains are real on benchmarks, but they're paid for in latency and cost.","红色那行是警示。这些提升在基准测试上是真实的，但代价是延迟和成本。"],[800.52,804.73,98,"When you compare models, compare them at equal token budgets.","比较模型时，要在相同的 token 预算下比较。"],[805.98,810.42,99,"But this kind of catching up is getting harder, for four reasons.","但这种追赶正变得越来越难，原因有四个。"],[810.77,818.24,99,"First, traces are hidden: frontier APIs now return summaries or encrypted thinking, not the raw chain.","第一，推理轨迹被隐藏了：前沿 API 现在返回的是摘要或加密的思考，而不是原始思维链。"],[818.59,823.76,99,"And anti-distillation methods can rewrite traces so students learn less.","而且反蒸馏方法可以改写轨迹，让学生模型学到的更少。"],[824.11,830.78,99,"The slide shows a thirty-two B student dropping from fifty-four point two to forty-six point nine on AIME.","幻灯片上显示，一个 32B 的学生模型在 AIME 上从 54.2 掉到了 46.9。"],[831.13,834.4,99,"Second, weak models can't follow the path.","第二，弱模型跟不上这条路径。"],[834.75,844.38,99,"Research on the small-model learnability gap shows students of three billion parameters or less learn better from short chains, while long ones make them loop.","关于小模型可学习性差距的研究表明，三十亿参数及以下的学生模型从短思维链学得更好，长思维链反而让它们陷入循环。"],[844.73,847.5,99,"They copy the word wait, not the skill.","它们学会的是 wait 这个词，而不是这项能力。"],[847.85,854.86,99,"Third, reasoning has become agentic: thoughts are now interleaved with tool calls and environment feedback.","第三，推理已经变得智能体化：思考现在和工具调用、环境反馈交织在一起。"],[855.21,859.41,99,"So a trace without its environment can't be replayed.","所以脱离了环境的轨迹是无法重放的。"],[859.76,866.36,99,"And fourth, metrics now punish length: leaderboards report cost and tokens per task.","第四，评测指标现在会惩罚长度：排行榜会报告每个任务的成本和 token 数。"],[866.71,873.88,99,"The message at the bottom is worth remembering: a weak model can copy the words of a top model's reasoning, but not its path.","底部这句话值得记住：弱模型可以模仿顶级模型推理的字面，却模仿不了它的路径。"],[874.23,879.59,99,"The path comes from capacity, knowledge, and RL in environments.","这条路径来自模型容量、知识，以及在环境中的强化学习。"],[880.84,887.27,100,"So let's come back to the core message from OpenAI, because after all the tricks, this is the thing that matters.","让我们回到 OpenAI 的核心信息，因为抛开所有技巧，真正重要的是这一点。"],[887.62,895.89,100,"A large-scale reinforcement learning algorithm teaches the model how to think productively using its chain of thought, in a highly data-efficient training process.","一个大规模强化学习算法，用高度数据高效的训练过程，教会模型如何利用思维链进行高效思考。"],[896.24,897.97,100,"Three words to underline.","有三个词要划重点。"],[898.32,903.46,100,"Reinforcement learning: the method. Chain of thought: what it shapes.","强化学习：这是方法。思维链：这是它塑造的对象。"],[903.81,914.39,100,"Data-efficient: it doesn't need massive new datasets, because the model generates its own training data through rollouts, exactly as we discussed in part three.","数据高效：它不需要海量的新数据集，因为模型通过 rollout 自己生成训练数据，正如我们在第三部分讨论的那样。"],[915.64,925.49,101,"And here are those two scaling plots once more, now next to an actual AIME problem, so you can see what kind of question we're talking about.","这里再次给出那两张扩展曲线，旁边放了一道真实的 AIME 题，让你看看我们说的是什么样的题目。"],[925.84,929.62,101,"It's a combinatorics problem about sums over pairs of subsets.","这是一道关于子集对求和的组合数学题。"],[929.97,934.43,101,"It's the kind of thing that takes a strong high-school competitor a good while to solve.","这种题，一个很强的高中竞赛选手也要花不少时间才能解出来。"],[934.78,942.69,101,"The key point is the same as before: accuracy improves smoothly with both train-time compute and test-time compute.","关键点和之前一样：准确率随着训练时算力和测试时算力都平滑提升。"],[943.04,951.96,101,"But having the problem next to it reminds you that each dot is about solving genuinely hard, multi-step problems, not recalling facts.","但把题目放在旁边会提醒你：每一个点都代表在解真正困难的多步问题，而不是回忆事实。"],[953.21,961.23,102,"After o1 came o3 and o4-mini. This is OpenAI's model comparison page from that time.","o1 之后是 o3 和 o4-mini。这是 OpenAI 当时的模型对比页面。"],[961.58,970.37,102,"Look at the rows. o3 is described as the most powerful reasoning model, and o4-mini as the faster, more affordable one.","看这几行。o3 被描述为最强的推理模型，o4-mini 则是更快、更便宜的那个。"],[970.72,973.42,102,"All of them use reasoning tokens.","它们都使用推理 token。"],[973.77,979.87,102,"Now look at pricing per million tokens: o1 was fifteen dollars input and sixty output.","再看每百万 token 的价格：o1 输入 15 美元，输出 60 美元。"],[980.22,987.0,102,"o3 is ten and forty; o4-mini is one dollar ten and four dollars forty.","o3 是 10 美元和 40 美元；o4-mini 是 1.10 美元和 4.40 美元。"],[987.35,991.34,102,"So within months, reasoning got both stronger and much cheaper.","所以短短几个月内，推理能力既变强了，也便宜了很多。"],[991.69,997.03,102,"That's typical of this field: once a capability appears, the cost of it falls fast.","这正是这个领域的典型特点：一项能力一旦出现，它的成本就会迅速下降。"],[998.28,1003.09,103,"Here's how o3 and o4-mini compare on reasoning benchmarks.","来看 o3 和 o4-mini 在推理基准上的对比。"],[1003.44,1014.63,103,"On AIME two thousand twenty-four and two thousand twenty-five, accuracy goes from the seventies for o1 to over ninety for o3 and o4-mini without tools.","在 AIME 2024 和 2025 上，准确率从 o1 的七十多分提升到 o3 和 o4-mini 不用工具时的九十多分。"],[1014.98,1025.48,103,"On Codeforces, the Elo rating jumps from about one thousand nine hundred for o1 to over two thousand seven hundred when the newer models can use a terminal.","在 Codeforces 上，Elo 分数从 o1 的约 1900 跃升到新模型可以使用终端时的 2700 以上。"],[1025.83,1030.18,103,"On GPQA Diamond, PhD-level science, it's in the low eighties.","在博士级科学问题 GPQA Diamond 上，成绩在八十出头。"],[1030.53,1033.86,103,"Now look at Humanity's Last Exam, bottom right.","现在看右下角的 Humanity's Last Exam。"],[1034.21,1042.22,103,"Scores are still low, but notice the pattern: o3 without tools gets about twenty, with Python and browsing about twenty-five.","分数仍然很低，但注意规律：o3 不用工具约 20 分，用上 Python 和浏览约 25 分。"],[1042.57,1046.59,103,"And Deep Research, which is an agent, gets the highest.","而 Deep Research 作为一个智能体，得分最高。"],[1046.94,1053.81,103,"Tools and agency matter. That's an early hint of where the last part of this lecture is going.","工具和自主行动能力很重要。这也提前透露了本讲最后一部分的方向。"],[1055.06,1060.73,104,"Before o3, o1 could already reason over an uploaded image.","在 o3 之前，o1 就已经能对上传的图片进行推理了。"],[1061.08,1067.06,104,"In this o1 demo, the user uploads a hand-drawn schematic of a datacenter in space.","在这个 o1 演示中，用户上传了一张手绘的太空数据中心示意图。"],[1067.41,1072.14,104,"And asks the model to estimate a lower bound on the radiator surface area.","并要求模型估计散热器表面积的下界。"],[1072.49,1078.17,104,"And to explain how it handles the Sun, deep space, and the first law of thermodynamics.","还要解释它如何处理太阳、深空，以及热力学第一定律。"],[1078.52,1085.82,104,"That's a problem that needs reading a diagram, making physical assumptions and doing a multi-step calculation, all together.","这个问题需要同时读懂图示、做出物理假设，并完成多步计算。"],[1086.17,1090.79,104,"The model has to reason across both the picture and the physics.","模型必须同时围绕图片和物理知识进行推理。"],[1092.04,1100.15,105,"Here's a second o1 demo: a photo of a birdhouse on a tree, with the request to write a detailed manual for building it.","这是第二个 o1 演示：一张树上鸟屋的照片，要求写一份详细的制作说明书。"],[1100.5,1105.61,105,"It's a simple image, but the model has to work out the parts and steps from the picture alone.","图片很简单，但模型必须仅凭这张图推断出零件和步骤。"],[1105.96,1109.7,105,"Note that o1 looks at the image only once, as input.","注意，o1 只把图片作为输入看一次。"],[1110.05,1118.27,105,"The next slide shows what o3 added: looking again, more closely, at parts of the image during its reasoning.","下一页展示 o3 增加了什么：在推理过程中，重新、更仔细地查看图片的局部。"],[1119.52,1122.33,106,"This is what thinking with images means.","这就是“用图像思考”的含义。"],[1122.68,1129.13,106,"The user asks what's written on a notebook in a photo. The text is small and upside down.","用户问照片里笔记本上写了什么。字很小，而且是倒着的。"],[1129.48,1134.95,106,"Follow the reasoning trace. The model loads the image, and notices the text is upside down.","顺着推理轨迹看。模型加载图片，发现文字是倒过来的。"],[1135.3,1140.99,106,"It decides to crop the lower part where the writing is, rotates the crop, and then reads it.","它决定裁剪出有字的下半部分，把裁剪图旋转过来，然后读出内容。"],[1141.34,1147.54,106,"Zooming and rotating are tool operations, and they happen inside the chain of thought, not before it.","缩放和旋转是工具操作，它们发生在思维链内部，而不是之前。"],[1147.89,1152.3,106,"This matters because it shows that reasoning doesn't have to be pure text.","这很重要，因为它说明推理不必是纯文本的。"],[1152.65,1156.82,106,"The model can act on its inputs while it thinks.","模型可以在思考的同时对输入进行操作。"],[1157.17,1162.26,106,"Remember that idea; it's a small step from here to agents acting on the world.","记住这个想法；从这里到智能体作用于真实世界，只差一小步。"]]},{"n":7,"title":"Measuring Reasoning and Inference-Time Verification","blurb":"Why math, code, GPQA and Humanity's Last Exam are used to measure reasoning, then repeated sampling, value-guided decoding, and outcome versus process verifiers.","file":"lecture06_part7.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part7.jpg","duration":1042.8,"first":107,"last":130,"slides":[{"n":107,"title":"4.3 How Do We Measure Reasoning?","t":0.8},{"n":108,"title":"Why Benchmark on Math, Coding and GPQA?","t":22.04},{"n":109,"title":"GPQA: A Graduate-Level Google-Proof Q&A Benchmark","t":68.62},{"n":110,"title":"Multimodal Reasoning?","t":110.96},{"n":111,"title":"Humanity's Last Exam (HLE)","t":168.02},{"n":112,"title":"HLE: Example Questions (1/3)","t":211.74},{"n":113,"title":"HLE: Example Questions (2/3)","t":248.63},{"n":114,"title":"HLE: Example Questions (3/3)","t":282.06},{"n":115,"title":"Will HLE Be the Last Exam?","t":319.83},{"n":116,"title":"5 Paths to Reasoning","t":358.86},{"n":117,"title":"Efforts toward o1-Style Models","t":388.57},{"n":118,"title":"Inference-Time Verification","t":446.84},{"n":119,"title":"Inference-Time Verification: Approaches","t":495.39},{"n":120,"title":"Multi-Step Reasoning in Math","t":541.75},{"n":121,"title":"Challenge: Cascading Errors in Multi-Step Reasoning","t":582.27},{"n":122,"title":"A Straightforward Way: Repeated Sampling","t":611.54},{"n":123,"title":"Related Work: Verification with Multiple Candidates","t":654.36},{"n":124,"title":"Related Work: Reward-Guided Decoding","t":693.19},{"n":125,"title":"OVM: Value-Guided Decoding, Step by Step","t":743.72},{"n":126,"title":"Training OVM: Outcome Labels Are Enough","t":790.62},{"n":127,"title":"Process vs. Outcome Supervision: What Should a Label Mean?","t":849.45},{"n":128,"title":"OmegaPRM: Monte Carlo Estimation of Step Values","t":908.32},{"n":129,"title":"Drawbacks of Learned Verifiers","t":958.92},{"n":130,"title":"Verification at Scale: Automatic Theorem Proving","t":989.57}],"sents":[[0.8,5.83,107,"We've seen what reasoning models can do. Now, how do we measure it fairly?","我们已经看到了推理模型能做什么。那么，怎样公平地衡量它呢？"],[6.18,14.05,107,"Reasoning claims need benchmarks that are hard, that can be checked automatically, and that aren't already saturated.","关于推理能力的论断，需要的基准必须足够难、能自动判分，而且还没有饱和。"],[14.4,20.64,107,"That's why the field leans on math, code, GPQA and Humanity's Last Exam.","这就是为什么这个领域主要依赖数学、代码、GPQA 和 Humanity's Last Exam。"],[21.89,27.93,108,"Why do math, coding and GPQA dominate reasoning evaluation? Two reasons.","为什么数学、编程和 GPQA 主导了推理能力的评测？有两个原因。"],[28.28,32.66,108,"First, they have gold-standard answers that can be checked automatically.","第一，它们有能够自动核对的标准答案。"],[33.01,37.13,108,"A number, a passing test suite, a multiple-choice letter.","一个数字、一组通过的测试用例、一个选择题字母。"],[37.48,43.48,108,"No human judge is needed, so there's no judge bias, which we saw is a serious problem.","不需要人类裁判，所以也就没有裁判偏差，而我们已经看到这是个严重的问题。"],[43.83,52.63,108,"Second, performance on them is far from saturated, at least for the hardest versions, so they still separate strong models from weak ones.","第二，模型在这些基准上的表现远未饱和，至少最难的版本是这样，所以它们仍能区分强模型和弱模型。"],[52.98,60.59,108,"And notice the connection to training: the same property that makes them good benchmarks, automatic checking, is what makes them good for RLVR.","再注意它和训练的联系：让它们成为好基准的那个性质，也就是自动判分，同样让它们非常适合 RLVR。"],[60.94,67.22,108,"That's not a coincidence; it's why reasoning progress has concentrated in these domains.","这不是巧合；这正是推理方面的进展集中在这些领域的原因。"],[68.47,70.55,109,"GPQA is a good example.","GPQA 就是一个很好的例子。"],[70.9,79.7,109,"It's a multiple-choice set of very hard questions in biology, physics and chemistry, written and validated by domain experts.","它是一个由领域专家编写并验证的选择题集，包含生物、物理和化学方面非常难的题目。"],[80.05,90.17,109,"The key number is in bold: when experts answer questions outside their own field, say a physicist answering chemistry, they get only thirty-four percent.","关键数字用粗体标出：当专家回答自己领域以外的问题，比如物理学家答化学题时，准确率只有百分之三十四。"],[90.52,94.68,109,"And that's even with more than thirty minutes and full access to Google.","而且这还是在花了超过三十分钟、可以随意使用 Google 的情况下。"],[95.03,100.58,109,"That's what Google-proof means. You can't just look up the answer; you have to understand and reason.","这就是“防 Google”的含义。你没法直接查到答案，必须理解并推理。"],[100.93,105.32,109,"Look at the two examples. Even reading them is hard unless you're a chemist.","看这两个例子。除非你是化学家，否则光是读懂它们都很难。"],[105.67,109.56,109,"This is the level at which reasoning models are now being compared.","推理模型如今就是在这个水平上进行比较的。"],[110.81,119.4,110,"Here's a chart from the o1 release comparing GPT-4o, in teal, with o1's improvement, in orange.","这是 o1 发布时的一张图，青色是 GPT-4o，橙色是 o1 带来的提升。"],[119.75,124.35,110,"On MATH, it jumps from about sixty to about ninety-five.","在 MATH 上，从大约六十跳到了大约九十五。"],[124.7,131.13,110,"On GPQA physics, from about sixty to about ninety-three. Big gains on text-based reasoning.","在 GPQA 物理上，从大约六十涨到大约九十三。文本推理上的提升非常大。"],[131.48,136.12,110,"But look at the two multimodal benchmarks, MathVista and MMMU.","但看看这两个多模态基准，MathVista 和 MMMU。"],[136.47,139.63,110,"The gains are much smaller, around ten points.","提升要小得多，大约十分。"],[139.98,147.68,110,"And as the note says, o1's chain of thought was text-only: no images inside the thinking.","正如下面的说明所写，o1 的思维链是纯文本的：思考过程中没有图像。"],[148.03,155.51,110,"So the natural question was: could a model draw auxiliary lines while it thinks, the way you would on a geometry problem?","所以自然的问题是：模型能不能在思考时画辅助线，就像你做几何题那样？"],[155.86,162.01,110,"That's the gap that o3's thinking with images, which we just saw, started to close.","这正是我们刚才看到的 o3“用图像思考”开始填补的空白。"],[162.36,166.62,110,"Multimodal LLMs get their own lecture later in the course.","多模态大模型在本课程后面会有专门的一讲。"],[167.87,175.46,111,"As models saturated older benchmarks, people built harder ones. The most ambitious is Humanity's Last Exam.","随着模型把旧基准刷到饱和，人们构建了更难的基准。其中最雄心勃勃的就是 Humanity's Last Exam。"],[175.81,185.83,111,"It's a global effort: questions from nearly a thousand subject experts at over five hundred institutions in fifty countries, mostly professors and researchers.","这是一项全球性的合作：题目来自五十个国家、五百多个机构的近一千名学科专家，大多是教授和研究人员。"],[186.18,191.22,111,"To attract really hard questions, there was a five hundred thousand dollar prize pool.","为了吸引真正难的题目，他们设立了五十万美元的奖金池。"],[191.57,200.06,111,"Five thousand dollars for each of the top fifty questions, and five hundred dollars for each of the next five hundred, plus co-authorship on the paper.","前五十道题每道奖励五千美元，接下来的五百道题每道五百美元，另外还能成为论文的共同作者。"],[200.41,205.34,111,"The design idea is clever: questions were kept only if frontier models failed them.","设计思路很巧妙：只有前沿模型答错的题目才会被保留。"],[205.69,210.34,111,"So by construction, it targets the edge of what models can do.","所以从构造上讲，它瞄准的就是模型能力的边界。"],[211.59,217.27,112,"Here are some example questions. Try reading them, just to feel how hard they are.","这里是一些例题。试着读一读，感受一下它们有多难。"],[217.62,225.48,112,"On the left, a classics question: a Roman tombstone inscription, and you have to translate the Palmyrene script.","左边是一道古典学题目：一段罗马墓碑铭文，你需要翻译其中的帕尔米拉文字。"],[225.83,234.31,112,"On the right, an ecology question about a specific sesamoid bone in hummingbirds, and how many paired tendons it supports.","右边是一道生态学题目，关于蜂鸟身上一块特定的籽骨，以及它支撑着多少对肌腱。"],[234.66,239.59,112,"These require deep, specialist knowledge, not just general reasoning.","这些题需要深厚的专业知识，而不只是一般的推理能力。"],[239.94,247.23,112,"Notice also that each question is credited to an expert at a named institution, like Oxford or MIT.","还要注意，每道题都署名了出题专家及其所在机构，比如牛津或 MIT。"],[248.48,251.83,113,"Two more: mathematics and computer science.","再看两道：数学和计算机科学。"],[252.18,261.48,113,"The math question is about natural cotransformations between functors in higher category theory, the kind of thing only a specialist would even parse.","数学题是关于高阶范畴论中函子之间的自然余变换，只有专家才能看懂题意。"],[261.83,267.04,113,"The computer science question is about Markov chains on edge-indicators of graphs.","计算机科学题是关于图的边指示函数上的马尔可夫链。"],[267.39,271.83,113,"It asks which graph classes have a uniform stationary distribution.","它问的是哪些图类具有均匀的平稳分布。"],[272.18,274.15,113,"These are research-level questions.","这些都是研究级别的问题。"],[274.5,280.66,113,"A model can't pattern-match its way through; it needs both knowledge and careful multi-step reasoning.","模型无法靠模式匹配蒙混过关；它既需要知识，也需要严谨的多步推理。"],[281.91,286.23,114,"And two final examples: chemistry and linguistics.","最后两个例子：化学和语言学。"],[286.58,296.74,114,"The chemistry one asks about the types of electrocyclizations and cycloaddition in a thermal cascade reaction, with the answer in a precise format.","化学题问的是一个热级联反应中电环化和环加成的类型，并要求以精确的格式作答。"],[297.09,302.84,114,"The linguistics one asks you to identify the closed syllables in a verse of Biblical Hebrew.","语言学题要求你找出一节圣经希伯来语经文中的闭音节。"],[303.19,307.95,114,"And it has to follow recent scholarship on the Tiberian pronunciation tradition.","而且要依据关于提比利亚发音传统的最新学术研究。"],[308.3,310.36,114,"The breadth here is the point.","关键就在于这种广度。"],[310.71,318.43,114,"HLE isn't just math and code; it spans the whole range of human expertise, which is why it was pitched as a last exam.","HLE 不只有数学和代码；它覆盖了人类专业知识的全部范围，这也是它被称为“最后一场考试”的原因。"],[319.68,324.41,115,"But will it really be the last exam? Almost certainly not.","但它真的会是最后一场考试吗？几乎可以肯定不会。"],[324.76,331.19,115,"We've already seen scores on it rise quickly, and every benchmark so far has eventually been saturated.","我们已经看到它上面的分数在快速上涨，而迄今为止的每个基准最终都被刷到了饱和。"],[331.54,335.21,115,"As a joke, we'll soon need Humanity's Last Last Exam.","开个玩笑，我们很快就需要“人类的最后的最后一场考试”了。"],[335.56,342.95,115,"The deeper lesson is that evaluation is a moving target, and building good benchmarks is a research problem in itself.","更深层的教训是：评测是一个移动的靶子，构建好的基准本身就是一个研究问题。"],[343.3,349.08,115,"So, to close part four: we've seen what reasoning models do and how we measure them.","那么，第四部分就到这里：我们看到了推理模型能做什么，以及如何衡量它们。"],[349.43,357.46,115,"But how did the field actually get there, especially in the open, without knowing OpenAI's recipe? That's part five.","但这个领域究竟是怎么走到这一步的，尤其是在不知道 OpenAI 配方的情况下，开源社区是怎么做到的？这就是第五部分。"],[358.71,362.63,116,"Part five follows the paths the community took toward reasoning models.","第五部分将沿着社区通往推理模型的几条路径展开。"],[362.98,367.33,116,"Some were tried and turned out to be limited; one turned out to be the breakthrough.","有些路径尝试后发现有局限；有一条最终成为了突破口。"],[367.68,374.78,116,"We'll go through inference-time verification with learned verifiers, and distillation of long chains of thought.","我们会依次讲：使用学习型验证器的推理时验证，以及长思维链的蒸馏。"],[375.13,382.47,116,"Then DeepSeek-R1 and pure RL, and an open small-scale reproduction called SimpleRL.","然后是 DeepSeek-R1 和纯强化学习，以及一个叫 SimpleRL 的开源小规模复现。"],[382.82,387.17,116,"And finally DeepSeekMath-V2, where rewards check whole proofs.","最后是 DeepSeekMath-V2，它的奖励会检查整个证明。"],[388.42,393.61,117,"When o1 appeared without a published recipe, many groups tried to reproduce it.","当 o1 出现却没有公开配方时，许多团队都尝试去复现它。"],[393.96,396.38,117,"Two families of approaches stood out.","其中有两类方法尤为突出。"],[396.73,407.72,117,"On the left, tree search: things like ReST-MCTS, which run Monte Carlo tree search over reasoning steps, guided by a process reward model.","左边是树搜索：比如 ReST-MCTS，它在过程奖励模型的引导下，对推理步骤进行蒙特卡洛树搜索。"],[408.07,414.33,117,"Then they train on the good paths. It's principled, but it's complex during both training and testing.","然后在好的路径上训练。这很有原则性，但在训练和测试时都很复杂。"],[414.68,425.1,117,"On the right, distillation: for example the O1 Replication Journey, which builds long thought traces from search trees, including mistakes and reflections.","右边是蒸馏：比如 O1 Replication Journey，它从搜索树中构造长思考轨迹，其中包括错误和反思。"],[425.45,431.5,117,"Then it fine-tunes a model on them. That's simpler, but it's hard to surpass the teacher model.","然后用这些轨迹微调模型。这更简单，但很难超越教师模型。"],[431.85,439.65,117,"Keep those two drawbacks in mind, complexity and the teacher ceiling, because they explain why pure RL eventually won.","记住这两个缺点：复杂性和教师天花板，因为它们解释了为什么纯强化学习最终胜出。"],[440.0,445.44,117,"Let's look first at the search and verification line, where our group also contributed.","我们先来看搜索与验证这条路线，我们组在这方面也有贡献。"],[446.69,454.16,118,"Before training-time methods, there's a line of work that improves reasoning purely at inference time.","在训练时方法之前，有一类工作完全在推理阶段提升推理能力。"],[454.51,459.65,118,"It doesn't change the model's parameters at all; you could call it real-time alignment.","它完全不改变模型参数；你可以称之为实时对齐。"],[460.0,464.36,118,"The idea is to treat decoding as an action-selection problem in RL.","思路是把解码看成强化学习中的动作选择问题。"],[464.71,474.85,118,"At each step, the generator proposes several possible next steps, and we pick which ones to keep so as to maximize the expected final reward.","在每一步，生成器提出几个可能的下一步，我们选择保留哪些，以最大化期望的最终奖励。"],[475.2,480.21,118,"That turns generation into a tree-structured search, as in the figure.","这就把生成变成了一个树状结构的搜索，如图所示。"],[480.56,486.33,118,"From the question, we branch into candidate steps at each level, and follow the highlighted path to the answer.","从问题出发，在每一层分支出候选步骤，然后沿着高亮的路径走到答案。"],[486.68,493.99,118,"The key ingredient is something that can score partial solutions. That's the verifier, or value model.","关键要素是一个能给部分解打分的东西。那就是验证器，或者说价值模型。"],[495.24,497.58,119,"Here's the landscape of these approaches.","这是这类方法的全景图。"],[497.93,504.66,119,"On the left is Tree of Thoughts, which searches over thoughts but relies on domain-specific heuristics.","左边是 Tree of Thoughts，它在“思考”上做搜索，但依赖特定领域的启发式规则。"],[505.01,509.98,119,"For example, it uses a hand-designed evaluation for the Game of twenty-four.","比如，它为二十四点游戏手工设计了评估方法。"],[510.33,514.58,119,"On the right are domain-agnostic guided decoding algorithms.","右边是与领域无关的引导式解码算法。"],[514.93,524.33,119,"TS-LLM, controlled decoding from DeepMind and OpenAI, and OVM from our group here at CUHK-Shenzhen and SRIBD.","包括 TS-LLM、DeepMind 和 OpenAI 的受控解码，以及我们港中大深圳和深圳大数据研究院团队的 OVM。"],[524.68,529.59,119,"They all use a learned model to guide the search, at the sentence or token level.","它们都用一个学习得到的模型来引导搜索，可以在句子级或 token 级进行。"],[529.94,535.1,119,"So they can be applied to any task without hand-crafted heuristics.","因此它们无需手工设计的启发式规则，就能应用到任何任务上。"],[535.45,540.35,119,"Let's now build up the OVM idea from scratch, starting with the basic setting.","现在我们从零开始构建 OVM 的思路，先从基本设定讲起。"],[541.6,544.69,120,"Here's the setting: multi-step reasoning in math.","设定是这样的：数学中的多步推理。"],[545.04,552.8,120,"A question goes into the generator, which produces a solution path: step one, step two, step three, then the answer.","一个问题输入生成器，生成器产生一条解题路径：第一步、第二步、第三步，然后是答案。"],[553.15,560.35,120,"This example is from GSM8K. Beth bakes four batches of two dozen cookies, shared among sixteen people.","这个例子来自 GSM8K。Beth 烤了四批、每批两打饼干，分给十六个人。"],[560.7,563.54,120,"Step one: four times two is eight dozen.","第一步：四乘二等于八打。"],[563.89,567.09,120,"Step two: eight times twelve is ninety-six cookies.","第二步：八乘十二等于九十六块饼干。"],[567.44,573.3,120,"Step three: ninety-six divided by sixteen is six. Final answer: six.","第三步：九十六除以十六等于六。最终答案：六。"],[573.65,580.87,120,"Simple enough. But this step-by-step structure is also where things go wrong, as the next slide shows.","很简单。但正如下一页所示，这种一步接一步的结构也正是出错的地方。"],[582.12,584.77,121,"The challenge is cascading errors.","挑战在于错误的级联。"],[585.12,591.0,121,"If step two is wrong, step three builds on it and is wrong too, and the answer is wrong.","如果第二步错了，第三步建立在它之上也会错，最后答案也错了。"],[591.35,594.57,121,"One small slip early on propagates all the way through.","早期的一个小失误会一路传播到底。"],[594.92,600.23,121,"Generation is autoregressive, so the model doesn't naturally go back and fix an earlier step.","生成是自回归的，所以模型不会自然地回头修正前面的步骤。"],[600.58,605.12,121,"The longer the chain, the more chances for a slip, and the more damage it does.","链条越长，出错的机会越多，造成的损害也越大。"],[605.47,610.14,121,"Any method that improves multi-step reasoning has to deal with this.","任何想要改进多步推理的方法都必须处理这个问题。"],[611.39,616.82,122,"The most straightforward fix is repeated sampling: just let the model try more than once.","最直接的办法是重复采样：让模型多试几次。"],[617.17,625.08,122,"This figure is from OpenAI's two thousand twenty-one verifiers paper: a six B model fine-tuned on GSM8K.","这张图来自 OpenAI 二〇二一年关于验证器的论文：一个在 GSM8K 上微调的 6B 模型。"],[625.43,630.01,122,"On the left, with one attempt, the solve rate stays below twenty-two percent.","左边，只尝试一次时，解题率一直低于百分之二十二。"],[630.36,637.35,122,"On the right, with a hundred attempts, the chance that at least one is correct reaches about eighty-four percent.","右边，尝试一百次时，至少有一次正确的概率达到大约百分之八十四。"],[637.7,644.89,122,"That gap is the key insight: the model often can produce a correct answer; it just doesn't do so reliably.","这个差距就是关键洞见：模型常常能给出正确答案，只是不够稳定。"],[645.24,649.96,122,"So if we could pick the right answer from many attempts, we'd get a big boost.","所以如果能从多次尝试中挑出正确答案，我们就能获得大幅提升。"],[650.31,652.96,122,"Which raises the question: how do you pick?","这就引出了一个问题：该怎么挑？"],[654.21,655.83,123,"The answer is a verifier.","答案是验证器。"],[656.18,661.04,123,"Step one: sample multiple candidate solution paths, path one to path K.","第一步：采样多条候选解题路径，从路径一到路径 K。"],[661.39,670.69,123,"Step two: give all of them to a verifier, a classifier trained to predict the probability that a solution is correct, and take the argmax.","第二步：把它们全部交给验证器，也就是一个训练来预测解答正确概率的分类器，然后取 argmax。"],[671.04,677.38,123,"This is often called best-of-N with a verifier. It's simple and works surprisingly well.","这通常被称为带验证器的 best-of-N。它很简单，效果却出奇地好。"],[677.73,682.2,123,"But it has a weakness: the verifier only looks at complete paths.","但它有一个弱点：验证器只看完整的路径。"],[682.55,691.79,123,"All the computation spent on paths that went wrong at step one is wasted, and the errors have already propagated by the time we check.","所有花在第一步就出错的路径上的计算都浪费了，而等到我们检查时，错误早已传播开了。"],[693.04,695.93,124,"Here's the contrast between the two paradigms.","这是两种范式的对比。"],[696.28,703.54,124,"On top, complete-path verification, or sample-then-filter: generate whole paths, then pick the best.","上面是完整路径验证，也叫先采样再过滤：生成完整路径，再挑最好的。"],[703.89,708.87,124,"Errors still propagate inside each path; we only filter at the end.","错误仍然在每条路径内部传播；我们只在最后过滤。"],[709.22,715.93,124,"At the bottom, guided decoding: check partial paths at every stage, and keep only the promising ones.","下面是引导式解码：在每个阶段检查部分路径，只保留有希望的那些。"],[716.28,721.68,124,"At stage one, there are two candidate steps; the better one is kept and expanded.","在第一阶段有两个候选步骤；更好的那个被保留并继续扩展。"],[722.03,727.18,124,"At stage two, again we keep the better branch, and so on until the answer.","在第二阶段，我们同样保留更好的分支，依此类推直到得出答案。"],[727.53,732.86,124,"We filter in the middle, so bad branches are cut early and compute goes to promising ones.","我们在中途就进行过滤，所以坏的分支被尽早剪掉，算力都花在有希望的分支上。"],[733.21,738.69,124,"Guided decoding is more efficient, but it needs a model that can score a partial path.","引导式解码更高效，但它需要一个能给部分路径打分的模型。"],[739.04,742.32,124,"How do we train that? That's what OVM does.","这个模型怎么训练？这正是 OVM 要做的。"],[743.57,746.8,125,"Here's OVM's decoding procedure, step by step.","这是 OVM 的解码流程，一步一步来看。"],[747.15,751.77,125,"At each step, sample K candidate next steps, here three.","在每一步，采样 K 个候选的下一步，这里是三个。"],[752.12,760.69,125,"Score each partial path with the value model, which estimates the probability that this partial solution will eventually reach a correct answer.","用价值模型给每条部分路径打分，它估计的是这个部分解最终能得到正确答案的概率。"],[761.04,765.12,125,"Keep the top b paths, here two, and prune the rest.","保留得分最高的 b 条路径，这里是两条，剪掉其余的。"],[765.47,770.16,125,"Then repeat until you reach an answer, and return the best path.","然后重复，直到得出答案，并返回最好的那条路径。"],[770.51,775.86,125,"So it's a beam search, but the beam is ranked by a learned value rather than by token likelihood.","所以这是一种束搜索，只不过束是按学到的价值排序，而不是按 token 的似然。"],[776.21,779.29,125,"The line at the bottom is the key conceptual point.","底部这一行是关键的概念要点。"],[779.64,785.55,125,"The value means how promising this partial path is, not whether this step is correct.","价值的含义是：这条部分路径有多大希望，而不是这一步对不对。"],[785.9,789.22,125,"That distinction will matter a lot in two slides.","这个区别在两页之后会非常重要。"],[790.47,796.36,126,"How do we train the value model? This is the nice part: outcome labels are enough.","价值模型怎么训练？这是最妙的地方：结果标签就够了。"],[796.71,803.7,126,"Sample many solution paths for a question. For each one, we only check whether the final answer is correct.","对一个问题采样许多条解题路径。对每一条，我们只检查最终答案是否正确。"],[804.05,807.74,126,"Then every prefix of that path inherits the label.","然后这条路径的每个前缀都继承这个标签。"],[808.09,815.63,126,"If path A ends correct, all its prefixes get label one; if path B ends wrong, all its prefixes get zero.","如果路径 A 最终正确，它所有前缀的标签都是一；如果路径 B 最终错误，它所有前缀的标签都是零。"],[815.98,818.9,126,"Then we train with a simple squared error.","然后用简单的平方误差来训练。"],[819.25,827.57,126,"Why does this learn a value? The same prefix shows up in many sampled paths, some ending correctly and some not.","为什么这样能学到价值？同一个前缀会出现在许多采样路径中，有的最终正确，有的不正确。"],[827.92,834.91,126,"Minimizing squared error pushes the value of a prefix toward the average label of its continuations.","最小化平方误差会把一个前缀的价值推向它所有后续路径标签的平均值。"],[835.26,839.12,126,"And that is exactly the probability of success from there.","而这恰好就是从该处出发获得成功的概率。"],[839.47,845.03,126,"And no step-level annotation is needed, only final answers, which are cheap to check.","而且不需要步骤级标注，只需要最终答案，而这很容易检查。"],[845.38,848.05,126,"Cheap labels, useful signal.","标签便宜，信号有用。"],[849.3,854.59,127,"Now the conceptual contrast: process supervision versus outcome supervision.","现在来看概念上的对比：过程监督与结果监督。"],[854.94,861.32,127,"Look at the example: a wrong path whose first two steps are locally correct, and the third step is wrong.","看这个例子：一条错误路径，前两步在局部上都是正确的，第三步错了。"],[861.67,865.06,127,"A process reward model asks, is this step correct?","过程奖励模型问的是：这一步对吗？"],[865.41,870.03,127,"It gives steps one and two a perfect score, and step three a zero.","它给第一步和第二步打满分，给第三步打零分。"],[870.38,875.71,127,"Our outcome-supervised value model asks, will this path reach the right answer?","我们的结果监督价值模型问的是：这条路径能得到正确答案吗？"],[876.06,882.3,127,"It gives step one maybe zero point three, step two zero point one, and step three zero.","它可能给第一步 0.3，第二步 0.1，第三步 0。"],[882.65,887.95,127,"Because even though the early steps were fine, the path was already heading toward a dead end.","因为尽管前面几步没问题，这条路径早已在走向死胡同。"],[888.3,894.9,127,"For planning, the second question is the one you want. It's about foreseeing the future, not grading the past.","对规划来说，你想要的是第二个问题。它关注的是预见未来，而不是给过去打分。"],[895.25,906.92,127,"And with only outcome labels, OVM-7B reached state of the art among models up to thirteen B on GSM8K, without GPT-4 or code execution.","而且仅凭结果标签，OVM-7B 就在 GSM8K 上达到了 13B 以内模型的最佳水平，既没用 GPT-4，也没用代码执行。"],[908.17,917.95,128,"Another way to get step-level signal without human labels is OmegaPRM, from Google DeepMind. It uses Monte Carlo estimation.","另一种无需人工标注就能获得步骤级信号的方法是 Google DeepMind 的 OmegaPRM。它使用蒙特卡洛估计。"],[918.3,923.33,128,"In panel a, take a prefix of a solution and roll it out several times.","在子图 a 中，取一个解答的前缀，然后把它展开 rollout 好几次。"],[923.68,933.26,128,"Here, two out of three rollouts reach the correct answer, twenty-four, so the prefix gets a Monte Carlo value of zero point six seven.","这里三次 rollout 中有两次得到了正确答案 24，所以这个前缀的蒙特卡洛值是 0.67。"],[933.61,940.16,128,"In panel b, to find where a wrong solution first goes wrong, it uses binary search over steps.","在子图 b 中，为了找出错误解答第一次出错的位置，它在步骤上做二分查找。"],[940.51,947.38,128,"Check the value at the midpoint, and narrow down until it finds the first step where the value drops to zero.","检查中点处的值，不断缩小范围，直到找到价值降为零的第一个步骤。"],[947.73,957.52,128,"Notice that this is the same idea as OVM's value: the quality of a partial solution is measured by how often it leads to a correct answer.","注意，这和 OVM 的价值是同一个思想：部分解的质量，由它多常能通向正确答案来衡量。"],[958.77,968.25,129,"But here's the catch with all of these learned verifiers, value models and process reward models: they're learned, so they're noisy or biased.","但所有这些学习型验证器，包括价值模型和过程奖励模型，都有一个问题：它们是学出来的，所以有噪声或偏差。"],[968.6,978.37,129,"And when you use them as a reward for RL, or even for search, the policy will find and exploit their mistakes, just like reward hacking in RLHF.","当你把它们用作强化学习的奖励，甚至只是用于搜索时，策略都会找到并利用它们的错误，就像 RLHF 中的奖励投机一样。"],[978.72,988.17,129,"So the natural question is the one on the slide: what if we use rule-based rewards or verification instead, something that can't be fooled?","所以自然的问题就是幻灯片上这个：如果我们改用基于规则的奖励或验证，用一种骗不了的东西，会怎样？"],[989.42,996.39,130,"The cleanest example of rule-based verification at scale is automatic theorem proving in a formal language like Lean.","大规模基于规则验证的最干净的例子，是在 Lean 这样的形式化语言中进行自动定理证明。"],[996.74,1001.71,130,"A proof either type-checks or it doesn't. There's no judge to fool.","一个证明要么能通过类型检查，要么不能。没有可以糊弄的裁判。"],[1002.06,1012.5,130,"This plot, from Kimina-Prover Preview, shows pass rate on the miniF2F test set against the sample budget, on a log scale.","这张来自 Kimina-Prover Preview 的图，展示了在 miniF2F 测试集上的通过率随采样预算的变化，横轴是对数刻度。"],[1012.85,1018.56,130,"The solid lines are whole-proof generation methods, and the dashed lines are tree search methods.","实线是整体证明生成方法，虚线是树搜索方法。"],[1018.91,1026.5,130,"Kimina-Prover, the blue line at the top, trained with large-scale RL against the Lean checker, reaches over eighty percent.","Kimina-Prover 是最上面的蓝线，它针对 Lean 检查器进行了大规模强化学习训练，通过率超过百分之八十。"],[1026.85,1032.04,130,"And it does so with far fewer samples than the tree-search methods on the right.","而且它所用的采样数远少于右边的树搜索方法。"],[1032.39,1040.96,130,"So with a perfect verifier, RL with whole-proof generation beats elaborate search. That's a strong hint about what comes next.","所以有了完美的验证器，整体证明生成加强化学习就能胜过复杂的搜索。这强烈预示着接下来会发生什么。"]]},{"n":8,"title":"Long-CoT Distillation, DeepSeek-R1 and SimpleRL","blurb":"Synthesizing long CoT for distillation, what is really new in DeepSeek-R1, and SimpleRL's open reproduction: rule-based rewards, length dynamics and emerging reflection.","file":"lecture06_part8.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part8.jpg","duration":1180.8,"first":131,"last":156,"slides":[{"n":131,"title":"5.2 Distilling Long Chain-of-Thought","t":0.8},{"n":132,"title":"Synthesizing Long CoT: Stream of Search and Journey Learning","t":15.45},{"n":133,"title":"Drawbacks of Long-CoT SFT (Distillation)","t":71.63},{"n":134,"title":"5.3 DeepSeek-R1","t":101.99},{"n":135,"title":"What Is Really New in R1?","t":124.32},{"n":136,"title":"Long CoT Patterns Emerging in RL Training","t":156.44},{"n":137,"title":"Self-Reflection Emerging in RL","t":204.81},{"n":138,"title":"DeepSeek-R1: Two Main Parts","t":250.03},{"n":139,"title":"DeepSeek-R1: The Full Training Pipeline","t":297.06},{"n":140,"title":"Rewards in RL: Reward Models vs. Rule-Based Rewards","t":385.91},{"n":141,"title":"DeepSeek-R1: Performance on Par with OpenAI-o1","t":436.07},{"n":142,"title":"5.4 Reproducing R1 in the Open: SimpleRL","t":490.93},{"n":143,"title":"The SimpleRL Recipe: Rule-Based Rewards","t":520.76},{"n":144,"title":"Experiment Setup","t":572.55},{"n":145,"title":"SimpleRL-Zero: RL from Scratch (1/3)","t":629.02},{"n":146,"title":"SimpleRL-Zero: RL from Scratch (2/3)","t":671.71},{"n":147,"title":"SimpleRL-Zero: RL from Scratch (3/3)","t":722.38},{"n":148,"title":"Phase 1: Why Does Length Decrease at First?","t":770.34},{"n":149,"title":"Phase 2: Length and Performance Increase Together","t":814.53},{"n":150,"title":"Phase 3: Length and Performance Saturate Together","t":858.6},{"n":151,"title":"Emergence of Reflection: An Example","t":905.46},{"n":152,"title":"Emergence of Reflection: Keyword Statistics","t":942.78},{"n":153,"title":"SimpleRL: RL with Imitation Warmup (1/2)","t":995.89},{"n":154,"title":"SimpleRL: RL with Imitation Warmup (2/2)","t":1046.1},{"n":155,"title":"Some Hypotheses","t":1092.42},{"n":156,"title":"Summary of SimpleRL","t":1138.18}],"sents":[[0.8,5.0,131,"So learned verifiers are noisy, and search is complex.","所以，学习型验证器有噪声，搜索又很复杂。"],[5.35,14.05,131,"The second path the community tried is simpler: if a strong model can already reason, can a smaller model just imitate its long chains of thought?","社区尝试的第二条路更简单：如果一个强模型已经会推理，小模型能不能直接模仿它的长思维链？"],[15.3,22.1,132,"The first question is how to get long chain-of-thought data at all. Two influential ideas.","第一个问题是：到底怎样才能获得长思维链数据。这里有两个很有影响力的思路。"],[22.45,28.61,132,"On top, Stream of Search: instead of training only on the optimal path, train on the whole search process.","上面是 Stream of Search：不只在最优路径上训练，而是在整个搜索过程上训练。"],[28.96,35.58,132,"That includes dead ends, state expansions and backtracking, written out as one stream of text.","其中包括死胡同、状态扩展和回溯，全部写成一段连续的文本流。"],[35.93,42.12,132,"On the right you see the contrast with the optimal path, which only includes the correct steps.","右边是与最优路径的对比，最优路径只包含正确的步骤。"],[42.47,46.73,132,"At the bottom, journey learning, from the O1 Replication Journey.","下面是来自 O1 Replication Journey 的旅程学习。"],[47.08,53.08,132,"Run a tree search, then select nodes to build exploration paths that include mistakes.","先运行树搜索，再挑选节点构建包含错误的探索路径。"],[53.43,61.5,132,"Use an LLM to write the reflection in between, like, my previous steps were incorrect, let me reconsider.","用一个 LLM 在中间写出反思，比如“我之前的步骤是错的，让我重新考虑”。"],[61.85,64.93,132,"And then post-train on these long thoughts.","然后在这些长思考上进行后训练。"],[65.28,70.23,132,"The shared idea: teach the model the journey, not just the destination.","二者共同的思想是：教给模型的是旅程，而不只是终点。"],[71.48,79.36,133,"But distillation, or long-CoT SFT, has a fundamental limit, and it's the same one we saw at the very start of the lecture.","但蒸馏，也就是长思维链 SFT，有一个根本性的局限，和我们在本讲一开始看到的一样。"],[79.71,87.29,133,"SFT doesn't generalize well. It can't learn genuinely new patterns; it learns from a teacher it can't outperform.","SFT 泛化得不好。它学不到真正新的模式；它是在向一个自己无法超越的老师学习。"],[87.64,97.04,133,"So if you want a model that goes beyond its teacher, or if there is no teacher, because you're the one trying to build the best model, imitation won't get you there.","所以如果你想要一个超越老师的模型，或者根本没有老师，因为你自己就在打造最好的模型，那么模仿是做不到的。"],[97.39,100.59,133,"The answer on the slide is short: try RL.","幻灯片上的答案很简短：试试强化学习。"],[101.84,109.04,134,"We've seen the two detours: learned verifiers that can be hacked, and distillation that can't beat its teacher.","我们已经看过两条弯路：可能被投机利用的学习型验证器，以及无法超越老师的蒸馏。"],[109.39,113.5,134,"DeepSeek-R1 took the third path, and published it.","DeepSeek-R1 走了第三条路，并且把它公开了。"],[113.85,122.92,134,"Pure RL with rule-based rewards, applied at scale, produces long chains of thought and self-reflection on its own.","大规模应用基于规则奖励的纯强化学习，就能自发地产生长思维链和自我反思。"],[124.17,128.34,135,"So what was actually new in R1? Not RL itself.","那么 R1 真正新的地方是什么？不是强化学习本身。"],[128.69,136.47,135,"As we've seen, RL for language models has been around for years, with RLHF since two thousand twenty.","正如我们所见，语言模型上的强化学习已经存在好几年了，RLHF 从二〇二〇年就有了。"],[136.82,142.91,135,"What was new was the emergence of long chain-of-thought plus self-reflection, from RL alone.","新的是：仅靠强化学习，就涌现出了长思维链和自我反思。"],[143.26,148.83,135,"The model was never shown examples of reflection, yet it started doing it.","模型从没见过反思的示例，却自己开始反思了。"],[149.18,155.04,135,"In the paper, they call it the aha moment. That's the result that made everyone sit up.","论文里把它称为“顿悟时刻”。正是这个结果让所有人都为之一振。"],[156.29,158.8,136,"Here's the evidence for long chains emerging.","这是长思维链涌现的证据。"],[159.15,165.25,136,"This plot shows DeepSeek-R1-Zero's average response length during RL training.","这张图展示了 DeepSeek-R1-Zero 在强化学习训练过程中的平均回复长度。"],[165.6,171.83,136,"Look at the starting point, marked in red: this is not an SFT model, just the base model.","看用红色标出的起点：这不是 SFT 模型，只是基座模型。"],[172.18,175.28,136,"At the start, responses are a few hundred tokens.","一开始，回复只有几百个 token。"],[175.63,181.87,136,"Over about eight thousand training steps, the average length climbs steadily to nearly ten thousand tokens.","经过大约八千个训练步，平均长度稳步攀升到接近一万个 token。"],[182.22,184.36,136,"Nobody told the model to think longer.","没有人告诉模型要想得更久。"],[184.71,189.49,136,"The reward only checks whether the final answer is correct and well-formatted.","奖励只检查最终答案是否正确、格式是否规范。"],[189.84,194.79,136,"The model discovered on its own that thinking longer gets more answers right.","模型自己发现了：想得更久，就能答对更多题。"],[195.14,203.41,136,"Kimi k1.5, released around the same time, used a similarly simple RL recipe.","差不多同一时间发布的 Kimi k1.5，也采用了类似的简单强化学习配方。"],[204.66,207.28,137,"And here's the famous aha moment.","这就是著名的“顿悟时刻”。"],[207.63,213.88,137,"The question is to find the sum of the real solutions of an equation with nested square roots.","题目是求一个带嵌套根号的方程的所有实数解之和。"],[214.23,219.86,137,"The model starts solving by squaring both sides, and expanding into a fourth-degree polynomial.","模型一开始把两边平方，然后展开成一个四次多项式。"],[220.21,225.35,137,"Then, in red: Wait, wait. Wait. That's an aha moment I can flag here.","然后是红色这句：等等，等等。等等。这是一个我可以标记的顿悟时刻。"],[225.7,231.48,137,"And it goes back, re-evaluates step by step, and tries a cleaner approach.","然后它回过头去，一步步重新评估，并尝试一种更简洁的方法。"],[231.83,238.74,137,"The line at the bottom is the important point: no tree search and no reward model.","底部这一行才是要点：没有树搜索，也没有奖励模型。"],[239.09,244.52,137,"Just a rule-based reward on the final answer, and this reflective behaviour emerged on its own.","只有针对最终答案的规则奖励，这种反思行为就自己涌现出来了。"],[244.87,248.63,137,"That's what incentivize, don't teach, looks like in practice.","这就是“激励，而不是教”在实践中的样子。"],[249.88,256.57,138,"The R1 paper actually has two main parts, and it's important not to mix them up.","R1 论文实际上有两个主要部分，千万不要把它们混为一谈。"],[256.92,262.77,138,"DeepSeek-R1-Zero is pure RL on math and code data, with no SFT at all.","DeepSeek-R1-Zero 是在数学和代码数据上的纯强化学习，完全没有 SFT。"],[263.12,267.17,138,"That's the scientific result: reasoning emerges from RL alone.","这是科学上的结论：推理能力可以仅靠强化学习涌现。"],[267.52,271.94,138,"DeepSeek-R1 is the product model: SFT plus RL.","DeepSeek-R1 是产品模型：SFT 加强化学习。"],[272.29,279.29,138,"It starts with a small amount of cold-start SFT data, partly generated by R1-Zero and then cleaned up.","它从少量冷启动 SFT 数据开始，这些数据部分由 R1-Zero 生成，然后经过清洗。"],[279.64,282.66,138,"Why add SFT back? Two reasons on the slide.","为什么又把 SFT 加回来？幻灯片上给了两个原因。"],[283.01,284.84,138,"It speeds up RL training.","它能加速强化学习训练。"],[285.19,295.66,138,"And it makes the model more user-friendly, because R1-Zero's outputs were hard to read, and R1 also adds non-reasoning data like writing and QA.","而且它让模型更好用，因为 R1-Zero 的输出很难读懂，R1 还加入了写作、问答等非推理数据。"],[296.91,299.27,139,"Here's the full pipeline in one slide.","这一页展示了完整的训练流程。"],[299.62,307.47,139,"Top row, R1-Zero: start from DeepSeek-V3-Base, a six hundred seventy-one B mixture-of-experts model.","上面一行是 R1-Zero：从 DeepSeek-V3-Base 出发，这是一个 671B 的混合专家模型。"],[307.82,315.43,139,"Run GRPO with rule-based rewards for accuracy and format, and you get R1-Zero, with no SFT.","用基于准确性和格式的规则奖励运行 GRPO，就得到了 R1-Zero，完全没有 SFT。"],[315.78,321.93,139,"AIME goes from fifteen point six percent to seventy-one, but the outputs are hard to read.","AIME 从百分之十五点六提升到七十一，但输出很难读懂。"],[322.28,325.61,139,"Bottom row, R1 in four stages.","下面一行是 R1 的四个阶段。"],[325.96,331.21,139,"One: cold-start SFT on a few thousand readable long-CoT examples.","第一：在几千条可读性好的长思维链样例上进行冷启动 SFT。"],[331.56,336.25,139,"Two: reasoning RL with GRPO, adding a language-consistency reward.","第二：用 GRPO 做推理强化学习，并加入语言一致性奖励。"],[336.6,345.99,139,"Three: rejection sampling, generating about six hundred K reasoning and two hundred K general examples for another round of SFT.","第三：拒绝采样，生成大约 60 万条推理数据和 20 万条通用数据，用于再一轮 SFT。"],[346.34,352.23,139,"Four: RL for everything, with rules for reasoning and reward models for helpfulness.","第四：面向一切的强化学习，推理用规则奖励，有用性用奖励模型。"],[352.58,359.27,139,"Notice the red note: RLHF is back. The two halves of today's lecture meet right here.","注意红色的标注：RLHF 回来了。今天这一讲的前后两半正是在这里交汇。"],[359.62,362.9,139,"The results: roughly on par with o1.","结果：大致与 o1 持平。"],[363.25,373.36,139,"And distillation: SFT on eight hundred K R1 samples gives a thirty-two B model seventy-two point six percent on AIME.","再看蒸馏：用 80 万条 R1 样本做 SFT，能让一个 32B 模型在 AIME 上达到百分之七十二点六。"],[373.71,379.31,139,"That's versus forty-seven percent from running RL on that thirty-two B model directly.","而直接在这个 32B 模型上做强化学习，只有百分之四十七。"],[379.66,384.51,139,"For small models, distilling from a strong RL-trained teacher is very effective.","对小模型来说，从一个经强化学习训练的强教师那里蒸馏非常有效。"],[385.76,392.06,140,"Since R1 mixes rule-based rewards and reward models, let's look at how the two can be combined.","既然 R1 混用了规则奖励和奖励模型，我们来看看两者可以怎样结合。"],[392.41,396.58,140,"This figure is from OpenAI's work on rule-based rewards for safety.","这张图来自 OpenAI 关于安全性规则奖励的工作。"],[396.93,400.87,140,"The prompt goes to the policy, which produces several completions.","提示输入策略模型，策略模型生成多个回复。"],[401.22,404.29,140,"Every completion gets a reward model score.","每个回复都会得到一个奖励模型的分数。"],[404.64,411.13,140,"If it's a safety-relevant prompt, like how to build a bomb, it's also routed to a rule-based reward.","如果是与安全相关的提示，比如如何制造炸弹，它还会被送到基于规则的奖励。"],[411.48,418.59,140,"That's a small linear model over features, such as whether the response refuses, or whether it's judgmental.","那是一个基于特征的小型线性模型，特征比如回复是否拒绝、是否带有评判意味。"],[418.94,423.07,140,"The two scores are added into a total reward, which drives PPO.","两个分数相加得到总奖励，用来驱动 PPO。"],[423.42,425.82,140,"The lesson: it's not RM versus rules.","启示是：这不是奖励模型和规则二选一。"],[426.17,434.67,140,"You use rules where you can write them down precisely, and a learned reward model where you can't, and you combine them.","能精确写成规则的地方就用规则，写不出来的地方就用学习得到的奖励模型，然后把它们结合起来。"],[435.92,441.71,141,"And here's the bottom line for R1: performance on par with OpenAI's o1.","这就是 R1 的最终结论：性能与 OpenAI 的 o1 相当。"],[442.06,448.0,141,"Compare the hatched dark-blue bar, DeepSeek-R1, with the grey bar next to it, o1.","比较带斜线的深蓝色柱子，也就是 DeepSeek-R1，和它旁边的灰色柱子 o1。"],[448.35,454.27,141,"On AIME two thousand twenty-four, seventy-nine point eight versus seventy-nine point two.","在 AIME 2024 上，是 79.8 对 79.2。"],[454.62,459.65,141,"On MATH-500, ninety-seven point three versus ninety-six point four.","在 MATH-500 上，是 97.3 对 96.4。"],[460.0,468.43,141,"On Codeforces and SWE-bench Verified they're essentially tied, and o1 is a bit ahead on GPQA and MMLU.","在 Codeforces 和 SWE-bench Verified 上两者基本持平，o1 在 GPQA 和 MMLU 上略微领先。"],[468.78,475.95,141,"Also notice DeepSeek-V3, the non-reasoning base, far behind on AIME at thirty-nine point two.","还要注意 DeepSeek-V3，这个非推理的基座模型，在 AIME 上远远落后，只有 39.2。"],[476.3,481.57,141,"The big deal wasn't only the numbers. It was that the weights and the recipe were open.","真正重要的不只是这些数字，而是权重和配方都是公开的。"],[481.92,489.53,141,"Within weeks, groups all over the world were trying to reproduce it, and one of those reproductions is our next topic.","几周之内，世界各地的团队都在尝试复现它，而其中一个复现就是我们的下一个话题。"],[490.78,497.7,142,"R1 showed that pure RL works at the scale of a six hundred seventy-one billion parameter model.","R1 证明了纯强化学习在 6710 亿参数规模的模型上是有效的。"],[498.05,500.98,142,"But most of us don't have that kind of compute.","但我们大多数人没有那样的算力。"],[501.33,512.67,142,"So this subsection asks a practical question: can R1-Zero's recipe be reproduced on a small open model, with only eight K training examples?","所以这一小节提出一个很实际的问题：R1-Zero 的配方，能不能只用 8K 训练样本，在一个小型开源模型上复现？"],[513.02,519.36,142,"We'll look at SimpleRL, an early open reproduction from Junxian He's group at HKUST.","我们来看 SimpleRL，这是港科大何俊贤老师团队较早的一个开源复现。"],[520.61,524.38,143,"Here's the SimpleRL recipe, and the key word is simple.","这是 SimpleRL 的配方，关键词就是“简单”。"],[524.73,528.8,143,"Look at the diagram: it's the standard PPO pipeline we saw earlier.","看这张图：它就是我们之前见过的标准 PPO 流程。"],[529.15,534.35,143,"But the learned reward model has been replaced by a rule-based reward, highlighted in red.","但学习得到的奖励模型被替换成了基于规则的奖励，用红色标出。"],[534.7,542.88,143,"So, interestingly, this reproduction used PPO rather than GRPO. The reward source matters more than the exact algorithm.","有意思的是，这个复现用的是 PPO 而不是 GRPO。奖励的来源比具体用哪个算法更重要。"],[543.23,545.86,143,"The reward function has just three cases.","奖励函数只有三种情况。"],[546.21,549.32,143,"If the answer is correct, the reward is plus one.","如果答案正确，奖励是正一。"],[549.67,553.61,143,"If the format is right but the answer is wrong, minus zero point five.","如果格式正确但答案错误，奖励是负零点五。"],[553.96,558.87,143,"If the format is wrong, for example no boxed final answer, minus one.","如果格式错误，比如没有把最终答案放进 boxed 框里，奖励是负一。"],[559.22,568.32,143,"On the right is what correct format means: reason as long as you like, then put the final answer in a box, so a script can extract and check it.","右边展示了什么叫格式正确：想推理多久都行，最后把答案放进框里，这样脚本就能提取并检查它。"],[568.67,571.15,143,"That's the entire supervision signal.","这就是全部的监督信号。"],[572.4,578.32,144,"Here's the setup, and the table shows just how little this uses compared with other approaches.","这是实验设置，表格显示了它和其他方法相比用的数据有多少。"],[578.67,585.75,144,"All four columns start from the same base model, Qwen2.5-Math-7B.","四列都从同一个基座模型 Qwen2.5-Math-7B 出发。"],[586.1,594.8,144,"Qwen's own Instruct model used two point five million SFT examples, a seventy-two B reward model, and sixty-six K RL queries.","Qwen 自己的 Instruct 模型用了 250 万条 SFT 样本、一个 72B 的奖励模型，以及 6.6 万条强化学习查询。"],[595.15,602.05,144,"rStar-Math used around seven point three million SFT examples and millions of RL rollouts.","rStar-Math 用了大约 730 万条 SFT 样本，以及数百万次强化学习 rollout。"],[602.4,609.66,144,"Eurus-2-PRIME used two hundred thirty K SFT examples and one hundred fifty K RL queries.","Eurus-2-PRIME 用了 23 万条 SFT 样本和 15 万条强化学习查询。"],[610.01,620.92,144,"SimpleRL-Zero, in the last column: zero SFT data, no reward model, and eight K queries from the original MATH training set, with eight samples each.","最后一列的 SimpleRL-Zero：零 SFT 数据、没有奖励模型，只有来自原始 MATH 训练集的 8K 条查询，每条采样 8 次。"],[621.27,627.62,144,"Then they evaluate on challenging benchmarks like AIME and AMC, which are much harder than the training data.","然后在 AIME、AMC 这样有挑战性的基准上评测，它们比训练数据难得多。"],[628.87,635.04,145,"And here are the results. The dark blue bars are the base model; the yellow bars are SimpleRL-Zero.","这是实验结果。深蓝色的柱子是基座模型，黄色的柱子是 SimpleRL-Zero。"],[635.39,645.31,145,"On average, RL directly on the base model with eight K MATH question-answer pairs gives a gain of eighteen point six absolute points.","平均来看，直接在基座模型上用 8K 条 MATH 问答对做强化学习，带来了 18.6 个绝对百分点的提升。"],[645.66,648.53,145,"You can see that on the red arrow on the right.","右边的红色箭头展示了这一点。"],[648.88,656.88,145,"It outperforms Qwen's own Instruct model on average, and it's comparable to Eurus-2-PRIME, which used far more data.","它的平均成绩超过了 Qwen 自己的 Instruct 模型，并且和用了多得多数据的 Eurus-2-PRIME 相当。"],[657.23,661.81,145,"That's what the slide means by roughly fifty times data efficiency.","这就是幻灯片上说的大约五十倍的数据效率。"],[662.16,670.31,145,"So the core R1-Zero claim holds at small scale too: RL with simple rule-based rewards on a decent base model goes a long way.","所以 R1-Zero 的核心论断在小规模上同样成立：在一个不错的基座模型上，用简单的规则奖励做强化学习，就能走得很远。"],[671.56,676.79,146,"Now an even more telling comparison: RL versus SFT on the same data.","现在看一个更能说明问题的对比：在相同数据上，强化学习对比 SFT。"],[677.14,683.78,146,"The second bar in each group is the base model fine-tuned with SFT on those same MATH examples.","每组中的第二根柱子，是在同样的 MATH 样例上用 SFT 微调后的基座模型。"],[684.13,692.42,146,"Look at AIME two thousand twenty-four on the left. SFT on MATH actually does very poorly on AIME, just a few percent.","看左边的 AIME 2024。在 MATH 上做 SFT，在 AIME 上的表现其实非常差，只有百分之几。"],[692.77,698.18,146,"RL from the same starting point reaches about thirty-three, roughly thirty points higher.","从同一起点出发的强化学习达到了大约三十三分，高了大约三十分。"],[698.53,702.18,146,"That's what the slide calls easy-to-hard generalization.","这就是幻灯片上说的“由易到难的泛化”。"],[702.53,713.17,146,"Training only on MATH-level problems, RL produces a model that does better on much harder competition problems, while SFT on the same data doesn't transfer.","只在 MATH 难度的题目上训练，强化学习得到的模型在难得多的竞赛题上表现更好，而在同样数据上做 SFT 却无法迁移。"],[713.52,720.98,146,"It's the same story we saw in part three, SFT memorizes, RL generalizes, now in math.","这和我们在第三部分看到的是同一个故事：SFT 记忆，强化学习泛化，现在换到了数学上。"],[722.23,723.8,147,"Let's look inside the training run.","我们来看看训练过程内部。"],[724.15,731.2,147,"On the left is training: reward in blue goes up steadily from about zero point two to about zero point seven.","左边是训练曲线：蓝色的奖励从大约 0.2 稳步上升到大约 0.7。"],[731.55,738.06,147,"Response length in orange does something interesting: it drops sharply first, then gradually climbs back up.","橙色的回复长度很有意思：它先急剧下降，然后逐渐回升。"],[738.41,743.44,147,"On the right is evaluation, divided into three phases by the red lines.","右边是评测曲线，被红线分成了三个阶段。"],[743.79,750.64,147,"Accuracy rises quickly in phase one, more slowly in phase two, and then levels off in phase three.","准确率在第一阶段快速上升，第二阶段上升变慢，第三阶段趋于平稳。"],[750.99,755.87,147,"Length falls in phase one, and rises through phases two and three.","长度在第一阶段下降，在第二和第三阶段持续上升。"],[756.22,765.01,147,"The bottom line in red is the surprising part: just eight K MATH examples lift a seven B base model this far, with no other external signal.","底部红色这行是令人惊讶的地方：仅仅 8K 条 MATH 样例，就把一个 7B 基座模型提升到了这个程度，没有任何其他外部信号。"],[765.36,768.94,147,"Next, let's go through the three phases one by one.","接下来，我们逐个看看这三个阶段。"],[770.19,774.21,148,"Phase one: why does length decrease at first?","第一阶段：为什么长度一开始会下降？"],[774.56,780.66,148,"The right plot shows the clip ratio: the fraction of generations that hit the maximum length limit.","右边的图展示的是截断率：达到最大长度限制的生成所占的比例。"],[781.01,784.18,148,"At the start it's high, about twenty-five percent.","一开始它很高，大约百分之二十五。"],[784.53,790.34,148,"A base model hasn't been taught to stop; it often rambles on or repeats itself until it's cut off.","基座模型没有学过如何停下来；它常常喋喋不休或者不断重复，直到被截断。"],[790.69,795.88,148,"Those cut-off answers have no boxed answer, so they get the minus-one format penalty.","这些被截断的回答没有 boxed 答案，所以会受到负一的格式惩罚。"],[796.23,801.03,148,"So the first thing RL teaches is simply to finish properly and give a final answer.","所以强化学习教会的第一件事，就是好好收尾，给出最终答案。"],[801.38,807.57,148,"The clip ratio drops, length drops, and accuracy jumps, as you see in the box on the left.","截断率下降，长度下降，准确率跃升，正如左边框里所示。"],[807.92,813.13,148,"It's learning to stop from the predefined rule, before it learns to think longer.","它先从预定义的规则中学会停下来，然后才学会想得更久。"],[814.38,817.83,149,"Phase two: length and performance increase together.","第二阶段：长度和性能一起上升。"],[818.18,825.31,149,"On the right is the average stopped length: the length of answers that end normally, not cut off.","右边是平均停止长度：正常结束、而不是被截断的回答的长度。"],[825.66,833.24,149,"In this phase it climbs from around four hundred to around six hundred tokens, while accuracy on the left keeps rising.","在这一阶段，它从大约四百个 token 升到大约六百个，同时左边的准确率持续上升。"],[833.59,839.93,149,"So the model isn't just rambling more; its complete, well-formed answers are getting longer, and better.","所以模型并不只是更啰嗦了；它完整、规范的回答正变得更长，也更好。"],[840.28,849.46,149,"The interpretation in red: longer sequences mean more exploration, more room to try steps and check them, and that gives stronger performance.","红色的解读是：更长的序列意味着更多的探索，有更多空间去尝试和检查步骤，从而带来更强的性能。"],[849.81,852.93,149,"Exploration is the key factor for better RL.","探索是强化学习做得更好的关键因素。"],[853.28,857.2,149,"That connects directly to the exploration theme from part three.","这和第三部分的探索主题直接相连。"],[858.45,862.43,150,"Phase three: length and performance saturate together.","第三阶段：长度和性能一起饱和。"],[862.78,867.81,150,"The stopped length levels off at around six hundred, and accuracy plateaus.","停止长度稳定在大约六百，准确率也进入平台期。"],[868.16,872.92,150,"Meanwhile, look at the red clip-ratio curve on the left: it climbs again.","与此同时，看左边红色的截断率曲线：它又开始上升了。"],[873.27,880.79,150,"More answers are hitting the length limit, and many of those are likely meaningless repetition rather than useful thinking.","更多的回答撞上了长度上限，其中很多可能是无意义的重复，而不是有用的思考。"],[881.14,887.46,150,"The interpretation: when the model stops exploring a larger generation space, performance saturates.","解读是：当模型不再探索更大的生成空间时，性能就饱和了。"],[887.81,893.26,150,"What could push further? Maybe a higher sampling temperature, or a longer length limit.","什么能进一步推动它？也许是更高的采样温度，或者更长的长度上限。"],[893.61,899.53,150,"But the slide also suggests that stopping meaningless repetition might matter just as much.","但幻灯片也指出，阻止无意义的重复可能同样重要。"],[899.88,904.06,150,"Longer is only good if the extra tokens are useful.","只有多出来的 token 有用，更长才是好事。"],[905.31,914.29,151,"Did the famous aha moment appear in this small-scale setting too? There are some signs, around iteration forty.","著名的顿悟时刻在这种小规模设定下也出现了吗？在第四十次迭代左右，有一些迹象。"],[914.64,920.82,151,"In this example, a word problem about Denali and Nate walking dogs, the model sets up equations.","在这个例子里，是一道关于 Denali 和 Nate 遛狗的应用题，模型先列出方程。"],[921.17,923.02,151,"It finds that the solution doesn't work.","它发现解出来的结果不成立。"],[923.37,928.72,151,"And then it says, in red: Let's recheck the setup. The correct setup should be.","然后它用红色这句话说：让我们重新检查设定。正确的设定应该是……"],[929.07,930.94,151,"And it solves it again carefully.","然后它重新仔细地求解。"],[931.29,935.28,151,"That's the same kind of self-correction we saw in R1-Zero.","这和我们在 R1-Zero 中看到的自我纠正是同一类行为。"],[935.63,941.38,151,"But one example isn't proof, so the next slide measures it more systematically.","但一个例子不能证明什么，所以下一页会更系统地衡量它。"],[942.63,948.79,152,"To measure reflection systematically, they counted reflection keywords in the model's outputs.","为了系统地衡量反思，他们统计了模型输出中的反思关键词。"],[949.14,954.48,152,"Recheck, rethink, try again, wait, alternatively, retry, however.","包括 recheck、rethink、try again、wait、alternatively、retry、however。"],[954.83,956.98,152,"Honestly, the picture is noisy.","说实话，结果相当嘈杂。"],[957.33,962.33,152,"On the left, the average count goes up somewhat, but jumps around a lot.","左边，平均次数有一定上升，但波动很大。"],[962.68,970.12,152,"On the right, for AIME, it's higher, because harder problems seem to trigger more reflection, but it's still unstable.","右边是 AIME，次数更高，因为更难的题目似乎会触发更多反思，但仍然不稳定。"],[970.47,978.62,152,"The honest conclusion, in red: there's no clear emergence pattern here, unlike the clean story in the R1 paper.","红色写的是诚实的结论：这里没有清晰的涌现模式，不像 R1 论文里那样干净利落。"],[978.97,982.82,152,"A larger model, or more challenging training data, might be needed.","可能需要更大的模型，或者更有挑战性的训练数据。"],[983.17,986.1,152,"I like this slide precisely because it's honest.","我喜欢这一页，恰恰是因为它很诚实。"],[986.45,994.49,152,"Not every result reproduces cleanly at small scale, and that tells us something about where these behaviours come from.","并非每个结果都能在小规模上干净地复现，而这也告诉了我们这些行为从何而来。"],[995.74,998.46,153,"The next experiment adds a warmup.","下一个实验加入了一个热身阶段。"],[998.81,1007.78,153,"Before RL, distill some long chain-of-thought examples from QwQ-32B, a strong reasoning model, and do a short SFT stage.","在强化学习之前，先从强推理模型 QwQ-32B 那里蒸馏一些长思维链样例，做一个短暂的 SFT 阶段。"],[1008.13,1011.84,153,"Then run the same RL as SimpleRL-Zero.","然后运行和 SimpleRL-Zero 相同的强化学习。"],[1012.19,1018.42,153,"The training dynamics on the left look similar, including the dip in length early on, highlighted in red.","左边的训练动态看起来很相似，包括早期长度的下降，用红框标出。"],[1018.77,1023.98,153,"On the right, after training, accuracy is slightly higher than SimpleRL-Zero.","右边，训练之后，准确率比 SimpleRL-Zero 略高。"],[1024.33,1030.82,153,"And responses are much longer, around one thousand six hundred tokens versus around nine hundred.","而回复要长得多，大约一千六百个 token，对比大约九百个。"],[1031.17,1038.02,153,"The slide's interpretation of the early length drop: maybe QwQ's very long style isn't favoured by the reward.","幻灯片对早期长度下降的解释是：也许 QwQ 那种非常长的风格并不受奖励青睐。"],[1038.37,1044.7,153,"Or it's beyond what a seven B model can use effectively, so RL trims it back first.","或者它超出了一个 7B 模型能有效利用的范围，所以强化学习先把它修剪回来。"],[1045.95,1050.06,154,"And here's how the warmed-up version, called SimpleRL, compares.","再来看经过热身的版本，也就是 SimpleRL，表现如何。"],[1050.41,1057.85,154,"The key comparison is between the second bar, the base model plus eight K QwQ distillation, meaning SFT only.","关键的对比在第二根柱子之间，它是基座模型加 8K 条 QwQ 蒸馏数据，也就是只做了 SFT。"],[1058.2,1063.63,154,"And the yellow bar, SimpleRL, which is that same model after RL.","以及黄色的柱子 SimpleRL，也就是同一个模型再经过强化学习之后。"],[1063.98,1068.09,154,"On average, RL adds six point nine points on top of distillation.","平均来看，强化学习在蒸馏的基础上又提升了 6.9 分。"],[1068.44,1075.41,154,"SimpleRL also consistently beats Eurus-2-PRIME, and slightly exceeds SimpleRL-Zero on average.","SimpleRL 还始终优于 Eurus-2-PRIME，平均成绩也略高于 SimpleRL-Zero。"],[1075.76,1079.21,154,"So distillation and RL aren't enemies.","所以蒸馏和强化学习并不是对立的。"],[1079.56,1087.2,154,"A short imitation warmup can give RL a better starting point, and RL then takes the model beyond what imitation alone gave.","一个简短的模仿热身可以给强化学习一个更好的起点，然后强化学习再把模型带到单靠模仿达不到的高度。"],[1087.55,1091.02,154,"That's exactly the logic of R1's cold-start stage.","这正是 R1 冷启动阶段背后的逻辑。"],[1092.27,1099.0,155,"Let's collect the hypotheses that come out of these experiments, because they're useful rules of thumb if you ever run RL yourself.","我们来汇总从这些实验中得出的假设，因为如果你自己做强化学习，它们是很有用的经验法则。"],[1099.35,1104.04,155,"First, the base model has to reach a certain accuracy for RL to work at all.","第一，基座模型必须达到一定的准确率，强化学习才能起作用。"],[1104.39,1111.06,155,"If it never gets anything right, every reward is zero, which is the all-wrong-group problem from part three.","如果它一道题都做不对，所有奖励都是零，这就是第三部分讲过的“全组皆错”问题。"],[1111.41,1113.57,155,"So a weak model needs easy data.","所以弱模型需要简单的数据。"],[1113.92,1121.48,155,"Second, a large model might be needed for genuine reflection to emerge; different models need different amounts of search.","第二，可能需要大模型才能涌现真正的反思；不同的模型需要不同程度的搜索。"],[1121.83,1127.71,155,"Third, we probably need more dynamic control of sampling temperature and length during training.","第三，在训练中我们可能需要更动态地控制采样温度和长度。"],[1128.06,1136.78,155,"In B-STaR, an earlier work from the same group, the temperature is raised when the diversity of samples drops, to keep the model exploring.","在同一团队更早的工作 B-STaR 中，当样本多样性下降时就提高温度，让模型保持探索。"],[1138.03,1145.07,156,"To sum up SimpleRL: it replicated the core of DeepSeek-R1 on small models with limited data.","总结一下 SimpleRL：它用有限的数据，在小模型上复现了 DeepSeek-R1 的核心。"],[1145.42,1151.85,156,"The design is simple, with no reward model and, in the Zero version, no SFT.","设计很简单，没有奖励模型，在 Zero 版本中也没有 SFT。"],[1152.2,1159.47,156,"A seven B model developed longer chains of thought and some signs of self-reflection from just eight K MATH examples.","一个 7B 模型仅凭 8K 条 MATH 样例，就发展出了更长的思维链和一些自我反思的迹象。"],[1159.82,1166.96,156,"And it rivalled methods that used more than fifty times more data and much more complex pipelines.","而且它可以媲美那些用了五十多倍数据、流程也复杂得多的方法。"],[1167.31,1171.31,156,"The QR code takes you to the project if you want to try it.","如果你想试一试，扫描这个二维码就能找到这个项目。"],[1171.66,1178.99,156,"This is the kind of experiment a student team can realistically run, which makes it a good final project idea.","这是学生团队可以实际做出来的实验，所以是一个很好的期末项目选题。"]]},{"n":9,"title":"Self-Verification, Olympiad Gold and ARC-AGI","blurb":"DeepSeekMath-V2's generator, verifier and meta-verifier, gold-level olympiad results, the AIMO competitions, and ARC-AGI's tests of learning new skills.","file":"lecture06_part9.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part9.jpg","duration":606.3,"first":157,"last":167,"slides":[{"n":157,"title":"5.5 Self-Verification: DeepSeekMath-V2","t":0.8},{"n":158,"title":"DeepSeekMath-V2: Towards Self-Verifiable Mathematical Reasoning","t":24.12},{"n":159,"title":"Why Self-Verification? Beyond Final-Answer Rewards","t":54.04},{"n":160,"title":"DeepSeekMath-V2: Generator, Verifier and Meta-Verifier","t":120.02},{"n":161,"title":"DeepSeekMath-V2: Gold-Level Results on IMO, CMO and Putnam","t":184.08},{"n":162,"title":"20× Smaller Models Achieve IMO Gold-Medal Performance","t":230.28},{"n":163,"title":"AIMO 2: Our Team's Result","t":286.13},{"n":164,"title":"ARC-AGI: Can AI Learn a New Skill from a Few Examples?","t":337.06},{"n":165,"title":"ARC-AGI-2 (2025): Harder Puzzles, and How Fast They Fell","t":404.3},{"n":166,"title":"ARC-AGI-3 (2026): Interactive Games with No Instructions","t":481.38},{"n":167,"title":"AIMO 3: AI Mathematical Olympiad Progress Prize 3","t":562.37}],"sents":[[0.8,6.62,157,"SimpleRL confirms that final-answer rewards work, even at small scale.","SimpleRL 证实了，即使在小规模上，基于最终答案的奖励也是有效的。"],[6.97,12.13,157,"But they have a blind spot: a correct final answer is not a correct proof.","但它们有一个盲点：最终答案正确，不等于证明正确。"],[12.48,17.78,157,"And many problems, like olympiad proofs, have no single answer to match at all.","而且很多问题，比如奥赛证明题，根本就没有一个可以比对的唯一答案。"],[18.13,22.72,157,"This subsection asks how we can reward rigorous reasoning itself.","这一小节探讨的是：我们如何奖励严谨的推理本身。"],[23.97,31.68,158,"This is DeepSeekMath-V2: Towards Self-Verifiable Mathematical Reasoning, from DeepSeek-AI.","这是来自 DeepSeek-AI 的 DeepSeekMath-V2：迈向可自我验证的数学推理。"],[32.03,39.47,158,"You'll recognize the first author, Zhihong Shao, from the GRPO slides; he also led the original DeepSeekMath.","你应该认得第一作者邵智宏，他在 GRPO 那几页出现过；他也主导了最初的 DeepSeekMath。"],[39.82,48.85,158,"The title is the idea: instead of checking only the final answer, train the model to verify its own reasoning, and use that verification as a reward.","标题本身就是核心思想：不只检查最终答案，而是训练模型验证自己的推理，并把这种验证当作奖励。"],[49.2,52.64,158,"Let's see why that's needed, and how it works.","我们来看看为什么需要这样做，以及它是怎么实现的。"],[53.89,57.27,159,"On the left, the limits of RLVR for math.","左边是 RLVR 在数学上的局限。"],[57.62,65.29,159,"A right answer can hide wrong steps; a model can guess, or make two errors that cancel, and still get rewarded.","正确的答案可能掩盖错误的步骤；模型可能是猜的，或者犯了两个相互抵消的错误，却仍然拿到奖励。"],[65.64,67.99,159,"Proofs have no final answer to match.","证明题没有可以比对的最终答案。"],[68.34,74.39,159,"And there's no rule-based checker for proofs written in natural language, unlike the Lean proofs we saw earlier.","而且对于用自然语言写的证明，没有基于规则的检查器，这和我们之前看到的 Lean 证明不同。"],[74.74,78.09,159,"On the right is DeepSeekMath-V2's recipe.","右边是 DeepSeekMath-V2 的配方。"],[78.44,85.93,159,"Train a verifier that grades a proof: list its issues, and score it zero, a half or one.","训练一个给证明打分的验证器：列出其中的问题，并给出零分、半分或一分。"],[86.28,90.42,159,"Train a meta-verifier that checks the issues the verifier reports are real.","训练一个元验证器，检查验证器报告的问题是否真实存在。"],[90.77,95.47,159,"Train the generator with RL against the verifier, so it learns to check itself.","用强化学习、以验证器为对手训练生成器，让它学会自我检查。"],[95.82,101.94,159,"And scale up verification by automatically labelling hard proofs and retraining the verifier.","再通过自动标注困难的证明并重新训练验证器，来扩大验证的规模。"],[102.29,107.35,159,"The line at the bottom is my favourite on this slide, because it ties today together.","底部这一行是我在这页最喜欢的，因为它把今天的内容串了起来。"],[107.7,118.62,159,"RLHF learned a reward from people; RLVR replaced it with rules; and self-verification learns a reward again, but one that can itself be checked.","RLHF 从人那里学习奖励；RLVR 用规则取而代之；而自我验证又重新学习奖励，但这个奖励本身是可以被检查的。"],[119.87,122.16,160,"Here are the three roles in more detail.","下面更详细地看看这三个角色。"],[122.51,130.28,160,"The generator produces several candidate proofs, and it learns to check and refine its own proof before finalizing it.","生成器产生多个候选证明，并学会在定稿之前检查和完善自己的证明。"],[130.63,139.48,160,"The verifier is a proof grader: it reads a proof, lists its issues with textual feedback, and gives a score of zero, a half or one.","验证器是一个证明评分器：它阅读证明，用文字反馈列出问题，并给出零分、半分或一分。"],[139.83,142.85,160,"The meta-verifier is the grader of the grader.","元验证器是“评分者的评分者”。"],[143.2,149.08,160,"It checks whether the issues the verifier reported actually exist, which keeps the verifier honest.","它检查验证器报告的问题是否真的存在，从而让验证器保持诚实。"],[149.43,154.48,160,"Now look at the rewards at the bottom. The generator's reward is the verifier's score.","现在看底部的奖励。生成器的奖励就是验证器的打分。"],[154.83,164.25,160,"The verifier's own reward is a product of three terms: correct format, the right score, and the meta-verifier confirming its issues are real.","验证器自己的奖励是三项的乘积：格式正确、分数正确，以及元验证器确认它指出的问题属实。"],[164.6,169.15,160,"Because it's a product, the verifier gets nothing unless all three hold.","因为是乘积，所以除非三项都满足，否则验证器什么都得不到。"],[169.5,175.99,160,"That stops it from hacking its own reward by, for example, inventing problems in a correct proof.","这就防止它投机取巧地刷自己的奖励，比如在一个正确的证明里捏造问题。"],[176.34,182.68,160,"Remember the judge biases from part two? This is a systematic way to keep a learned judge faithful.","还记得第二部分讲的裁判偏差吗？这是一种让学习型裁判保持忠实的系统性方法。"],[183.93,186.5,161,"And it works remarkably well.","而且它的效果非常好。"],[186.85,196.96,161,"On IMO two thousand twenty-five, the model fully solved problems one to five, for eighty-three point three percent of the points, which is gold-medal level.","在 IMO 2025 上，模型完整解出了第一到第五题，拿到百分之八十三点三的分数，达到金牌水平。"],[197.31,203.13,161,"On the Chinese Mathematical Olympiad two thousand twenty-four, seventy-three point eight percent.","在 2024 年中国数学奥林匹克上，得分是百分之七十三点八。"],[203.48,213.01,161,"And on the Putnam two thousand twenty-four, the hardest undergraduate competition in North America, ninety-eight point three percent, with almost every problem fully solved.","在 2024 年普特南竞赛，也就是北美最难的本科生数学竞赛上，得分是百分之九十八点三，几乎每道题都完整解出。"],[213.36,222.17,161,"The note at the bottom is the key context: other systems had reached IMO gold, from Google's Gemini and OpenAI, but those were closed.","底部的说明是关键背景：其他系统也达到过 IMO 金牌水平，来自 Google 的 Gemini 和 OpenAI，但它们都是闭源的。"],[222.52,228.88,161,"DeepSeekMath-V2 was the first open-source model to do it, so anyone can study how it works.","DeepSeekMath-V2 是第一个做到这一点的开源模型，所以任何人都可以研究它是如何工作的。"],[230.13,237.39,162,"And it keeps moving fast. This is NVIDIA's Nemotron-Cascade 2, from March two thousand twenty-six.","而且进展还在飞速推进。这是 NVIDIA 在二〇二六年三月发布的 Nemotron-Cascade 2。"],[237.74,243.84,162,"It's an open mixture-of-experts model with thirty billion total parameters and only three billion active per token.","它是一个开源的混合专家模型，总参数三百亿，每个 token 只激活三十亿参数。"],[244.19,255.55,162,"According to its abstract, it's the second open-weight model, after DeepSeek-V3.2-Speciale, to reach gold-medal level at IMO two thousand twenty-five.","根据摘要，它是继 DeepSeek-V3.2-Speciale 之后，第二个在 IMO 2025 上达到金牌水平的开源权重模型。"],[255.9,260.27,162,"It did the same at the IOI and the ICPC World Finals.","它在 IOI 和 ICPC 全球总决赛上也达到了同样的水平。"],[260.62,267.41,162,"That's the point of the title: roughly twenty times fewer parameters than the earlier gold-level open model.","这就是标题的意思：参数量比之前的金牌级开源模型少了大约二十倍。"],[267.76,272.99,162,"The recipe is careful SFT followed by cascaded RL across many domains.","它的配方是先做精心的 SFT，再跨多个领域进行级联强化学习。"],[273.34,278.07,162,"Plus on-policy distillation from the strongest teacher for each domain.","再加上从每个领域最强的教师模型进行同策略蒸馏。"],[278.42,284.73,162,"So the RL techniques we've discussed today are now giving small models olympiad-level reasoning.","所以，我们今天讨论的强化学习技术，正在让小模型具备奥赛级别的推理能力。"],[285.98,288.14,163,"A small bit of our own news.","分享一点我们自己的消息。"],[288.49,295.2,163,"This is the final leaderboard of AIMO 2, the second AI Mathematical Olympiad Progress Prize on Kaggle.","这是 AIMO 2 的最终排行榜，也就是 Kaggle 上第二届 AI 数学奥林匹克进步奖。"],[295.55,301.23,163,"Teams have to solve olympiad-level problems with open models under limited compute.","参赛队伍必须在有限算力下，用开源模型解决奥赛级别的题目。"],[301.58,310.28,163,"Our team, CUHKSZ-Huawei, which you can see in row fourteen, solved twenty-eight of the fifty problems.","我们的队伍 CUHKSZ-Huawei 在第十四行，解出了五十道题中的二十八道。"],[310.63,318.22,163,"Several teams are tied at twenty-eight, so we were ranked between ninth and fourteenth, out of about two thousand teams.","有好几支队伍并列二十八题，所以我们的排名在第九到第十四之间，参赛队伍约两千支。"],[318.57,320.6,163,"That's equivalent to a gold medal.","这相当于一枚金牌。"],[320.95,325.47,163,"The winner, NemoSkills from NVIDIA, solved thirty-four.","冠军是 NVIDIA 的 NemoSkills，解出了三十四道。"],[325.82,333.08,163,"I show this partly because competitions like this are a great way for students to get hands-on with reasoning models.","我展示这个，部分原因是这类比赛是学生亲手实践推理模型的好方式。"],[333.43,335.66,163,"And we'll come back to that in a moment.","我们稍后还会回到这一点。"],[336.91,343.05,164,"Before we leave the topic of measuring reasoning, let's look at a very different kind of test: ARC-AGI.","在结束推理评测这个话题之前，我们来看一种非常不同的测试：ARC-AGI。"],[343.4,346.77,164,"Olympiad math tests reasoning within known rules.","奥赛数学测试的是在已知规则内的推理。"],[347.12,352.06,164,"ARC asks whether a model can learn a completely new skill from just a few examples.","ARC 问的是：模型能否仅凭几个例子学会一项全新的技能。"],[352.41,360.1,164,"Look at the grid on the left. Two demos show input grids turning into output grids, and you have to infer the hidden rule.","看左边的网格。两个示例展示了输入网格如何变成输出网格，你需要推断出隐藏的规则。"],[360.45,364.76,164,"Here, it's illustrative: fill each red cell's row with pink.","这里只是一个示意：把每个红色格子所在的行涂成粉色。"],[365.11,370.58,164,"Then apply it to the test input. Most people get this in seconds.","然后把它应用到测试输入上。大多数人几秒钟就能做出来。"],[370.93,373.32,164,"There have been three generations.","ARC 已经有三代了。"],[373.67,381.43,164,"ARC-AGI-1 from two thousand nineteen, with static grid puzzles about objects, counting and symmetry.","二〇一九年的 ARC-AGI-1，是关于物体、计数和对称的静态网格谜题。"],[381.78,386.33,164,"ARC-AGI-2 from two thousand twenty-five, with harder puzzles.","二〇二五年的 ARC-AGI-2，谜题更难。"],[386.68,394.24,164,"And ARC-AGI-3 from two thousand twenty-six, which isn't a puzzle at all but interactive games.","还有二〇二六年的 ARC-AGI-3，它根本不是谜题，而是交互式游戏。"],[394.59,402.9,164,"The idea, from Francois Chollet, is that intelligence is skill-acquisition efficiency, not memorized knowledge.","这个思想来自 François Chollet：智能是获取技能的效率，而不是记住的知识。"],[404.15,409.56,165,"ARC-AGI-2 was designed to be much harder than the first version.","ARC-AGI-2 被设计得比第一版难得多。"],[409.91,418.78,165,"Every task was solved by at least two people out of four hundred plus testers within two attempts, so it's fair for humans.","每道题都被四百多名测试者中的至少两人在两次尝试内解出，所以对人类来说是公平的。"],[419.13,427.65,165,"But the tasks need symbolic interpretation, composition of several rules, and rules that change with context.","但这些题需要符号理解、多条规则的组合，以及随上下文变化的规则。"],[428.0,435.01,165,"And tasks solvable by brute force were removed. The Grand Prize bar is eighty-five percent.","能用暴力搜索解决的题目都被剔除了。大奖的门槛是百分之八十五。"],[435.36,437.83,165,"Now look at the bars on the right.","现在看右边的柱状图。"],[438.18,444.47,165,"The Kaggle winner in November two thousand twenty-five got twenty-four percent, at twenty cents per task.","二〇二五年十一月的 Kaggle 冠军得到了百分之二十四，每道题成本二十美分。"],[444.82,454.34,165,"In early two thousand twenty-six, GPT-5.2 Pro reached fifty-four percent, at nearly sixteen dollars per task.","二〇二六年初，GPT-5.2 Pro 达到了百分之五十四，每道题成本将近十六美元。"],[454.69,464.52,165,"And by July two thousand twenty-six, frontier models at maximum reasoning effort were above ninety percent, over the eighty-five percent bar.","到二〇二六年七月，前沿模型在最大推理强度下超过了百分之九十，越过了百分之八十五的门槛。"],[464.87,467.02,165,"The human panel is at one hundred.","人类测试组是百分之一百。"],[467.37,475.18,165,"So, from twenty-four to over ninety percent in about eight months, driven by reasoning models and test-time compute.","所以，在大约八个月里，从百分之二十四涨到了九十以上，驱动力是推理模型和测试时算力。"],[475.53,479.98,165,"The open question, as the red line says, is cost per task.","正如红色这行所说，悬而未决的问题是每道题的成本。"],[481.23,487.68,166,"And then ARC-AGI-3, launched in two thousand twenty-six, changes the game, literally.","然后是二〇二六年推出的 ARC-AGI-3，它真的是改变了游戏，字面意义上的。"],[488.03,492.45,166,"It's one hundred thirty-five turn-based game environments with no instructions.","它由一百三十五个回合制游戏环境组成，没有任何说明。"],[492.8,498.05,166,"The agent has to explore by pressing keys, and form hypotheses about the rules and the goal.","智能体必须通过按键来探索，并对规则和目标形成假设。"],[498.4,505.69,166,"Then it has to plan and act to reach the goal in as few moves as possible, level after level.","然后它要规划并行动，用尽可能少的步数达成目标，一关接一关。"],[506.04,510.17,166,"Scoring compares the AI's number of actions with a human's.","计分方式是把 AI 的行动次数和人类的进行比较。"],[510.52,516.47,166,"Each level scores human actions divided by AI actions, squared, capped at one.","每一关的得分是人类行动数除以 AI 行动数，再平方，上限为一。"],[516.82,520.43,166,"Thinking is free, but wasted moves cost you.","思考是免费的，但浪费的步数要付出代价。"],[520.78,527.7,166,"Look at the results. At launch in March two thousand twenty-six, the best frontier models scored well under one percent.","看结果。二〇二六年三月推出时，最好的前沿模型得分远低于百分之一。"],[528.05,532.93,166,"By mid two thousand twenty-six, the best verified score was about thirty percent.","到二〇二六年年中，最好的经过验证的分数大约是百分之三十。"],[533.28,540.31,166,"And a third-party report from October claims around sixty-three, so treat that one with some caution.","而十月份的一份第三方报告声称达到了约六十三，所以对这个数字要谨慎看待。"],[540.66,542.4,166,"Humans are at one hundred.","人类是一百。"],[542.75,545.4,166,"The red line is the lesson for our next part.","红色这行是我们下一部分的启示。"],[545.75,552.94,166,"A model that scored ninety-seven percent on a familiar game with a hand-built harness got zero on an unfamiliar one.","一个在熟悉的游戏上、借助手工搭建的框架拿到百分之九十七的模型，在一个陌生游戏上得了零分。"],[553.29,560.97,166,"Acting in a new environment is a different skill from reasoning on a page, and it's exactly what agentic RL has to teach.","在新环境中行动，和在纸面上推理是不同的能力，而这正是智能体强化学习要教会的。"],[562.22,570.61,167,"Coming back to math competitions to close part five: this is AIMO 3, the third AI Mathematical Olympiad Progress Prize on Kaggle.","回到数学竞赛来结束第五部分：这是 AIMO 3，Kaggle 上第三届 AI 数学奥林匹克进步奖。"],[570.96,574.62,167,"It has harder problems and a bigger prize pool than before.","它的题目比以前更难，奖金池也更大。"],[574.97,581.69,167,"The note on the slide makes an interesting point: AIMO 3 has become an educational practice for smaller models.","幻灯片上的说明提出了一个有意思的观点：AIMO 3 已经成了小模型的一种教学实践。"],[582.04,592.11,167,"Because the frontier models are now so strong, the competition is really about how much reasoning you can squeeze out of small open models under tight compute.","由于前沿模型现在已经非常强，这个比赛真正比的是：在紧张的算力下，你能从小型开源模型中榨出多少推理能力。"],[592.46,600.62,167,"That's exactly the setting where everything in parts three and five, GRPO, data selection, test-time scaling, really matters.","正是在这种设定下，第三和第五部分讲的一切，GRPO、数据选择、测试时扩展，才真正重要。"],[600.97,604.45,167,"If you're looking for a hands-on project, this is a great one.","如果你在找一个动手实践的项目，这是一个很好的选择。"]]},{"n":10,"title":"RL beyond Math and Toward Agentic RL","blurb":"Applying RL to medicine and video with HuatuoGPT-o1, Video-R1 and OnePO, then the shift to agentic RL, why it is hard, and the lecture's takeaways.","file":"lecture06_part10.mp4","poster":"lecture06_part10.jpg","duration":942.6,"first":168,"last":185,"slides":[{"n":168,"title":"6 Our Work: RL beyond Math","t":0.8},{"n":169,"title":"Our Work: HuatuoGPT-o1 — Search for Complex CoT, then RL","t":30.34},{"n":170,"title":"HuatuoGPT-o1: Verifiable Problems in the Medical Domain","t":97.86},{"n":171,"title":"Our Work: Video-R1 — Rewarding Temporal Reasoning (T-GRPO)","t":158.82},{"n":172,"title":"Domain Adaptation Without SFT: HuatuoGPT-3","t":214.47},{"n":173,"title":"OnePO: Teacher Outputs as Transient Guidance","t":289.5},{"n":174,"title":"7 Toward Agentic RL","t":362.35},{"n":175,"title":"From “Reasoning” Thinking to “Agentic” Thinking","t":384.48},{"n":176,"title":"Language Generalizes through Reasoning in Agents","t":437.01},{"n":177,"title":"The Agentic RL Era: Why Is Training So Hard?","t":490.29},{"n":178,"title":"The First Half vs. the Second Half of AI","t":566.76},{"n":179,"title":"Discussion: Two Bets on Coding Agents","t":614.69},{"n":180,"title":"Outlook: Why You Should Work on RL","t":686.58},{"n":181,"title":"Takeaways: One Tool, Changing Rewards","t":760.26},{"n":182,"title":"Acknowledgement","t":831.44},{"n":183,"title":"References (1/2)","t":856.94},{"n":184,"title":"References (2/2)","t":875.13},{"n":185,"title":"Thank You! Questions?","t":888.3}],"sents":[[0.8,10.66,168,"So far, almost every success has been in math and code, where answers can be checked automatically, and even proofs can now be verified.","到目前为止，几乎所有的成功都集中在数学和代码上，在这些领域答案可以自动检查，现在连证明也能验证了。"],[11.01,16.45,168,"But what about domains with no unit tests, like medicine or video understanding?","但那些没有单元测试的领域呢，比如医学或视频理解？"],[16.8,19.72,168,"Part six covers our own work on two questions.","第六部分介绍我们自己在两个问题上的工作。"],[20.07,28.94,168,"How to build verifiable rewards in those domains, and how to adapt a model to a new domain with RL alone, without SFT.","一是如何在这些领域构建可验证的奖励，二是如何不用 SFT、仅靠强化学习让模型适应新领域。"],[30.19,37.12,169,"The first piece is HuatuoGPT-o1, our medical reasoning model, built in two stages.","第一项工作是 HuatuoGPT-o1，我们的医学推理模型，分两个阶段构建。"],[37.47,40.99,169,"Stage one, on the left, is learning complex reasoning.","左边的第一阶段是学习复杂推理。"],[41.34,45.02,169,"We take a verifiable medical problem, with a ground-truth answer.","我们取一个带有标准答案的可验证医学问题。"],[45.37,50.34,169,"The model proposes a reasoning chain and an answer, and a verifier checks it.","模型给出一条推理链和一个答案，然后由验证器检查。"],[50.69,59.17,169,"If it's wrong, we sample a search strategy: backtracking, exploring new paths, verification, or correction, and try again.","如果错了，就采样一种搜索策略：回溯、探索新路径、验证或纠正，然后再试一次。"],[59.52,64.36,169,"We continue until the verifier says it's right, or we give up and restart.","一直重复，直到验证器判定正确，或者放弃并重新开始。"],[64.71,71.79,169,"The successful search trajectory is then rewritten into one smooth, complex chain of thought.","然后把成功的搜索轨迹改写成一条流畅的复杂思维链。"],[72.14,77.37,169,"It has thinking like, wait, actually, this may not help us. We fine-tune on those.","其中包含这样的思考：“等等，其实这可能帮不了我们。”我们用这些数据做微调。"],[77.72,82.5,169,"Stage two, on the right, enhances complex reasoning with RL.","右边的第二阶段，用强化学习增强复杂推理。"],[82.85,90.64,169,"The model answers verifiable medical problems, the verifier compares with the ground truth, and that reward drives PPO.","模型回答可验证的医学问题，验证器把答案和标准答案比对，这个奖励再驱动 PPO。"],[90.99,96.46,169,"So the trick is to make medicine look like math: create problems where the answer can be checked.","所以诀窍是让医学看起来像数学：构造出答案可以被检查的问题。"],[97.71,101.99,170,"How do we get verifiable problems in medicine? Look at the left side.","我们怎样在医学中获得可验证的问题？看左边。"],[102.34,109.89,170,"We start from closed-set exam questions, from the MedQA and MedMCQA training sets, and select the hard ones.","我们从封闭式的考试题出发，来自 MedQA 和 MedMCQA 的训练集，然后挑出其中较难的题。"],[110.24,115.4,170,"Then we transform each into an open-ended problem with a single ground-truth answer.","再把每道题转化成一个只有唯一标准答案的开放式问题。"],[115.75,125.02,170,"Take the example below: a thirty-year-old woman who recently travelled to India presents with fever, chills, jaundice and anaemia.","看下面的例子：一位三十岁的女性最近去过印度，出现发热、寒战、黄疸和贫血。"],[125.37,129.43,170,"And the question asks for the most severe complication.","题目问的是最严重的并发症是什么。"],[129.78,135.36,170,"In the exam it's multiple choice, with the answer C, cerebral edema.","在考试中这是一道选择题，答案是 C，脑水肿。"],[135.71,142.4,170,"We remove the options, so the model can't just guess a letter, and keep cerebral edema as the ground truth.","我们去掉选项，这样模型就不能靠猜字母蒙对，并把脑水肿保留为标准答案。"],[142.75,151.83,170,"On the right, the medical verifier, itself an LLM, checks whether the model's final answer matches the ground truth.","右边的医学验证器本身也是一个 LLM，它检查模型的最终答案是否与标准答案一致。"],[152.18,157.42,170,"It's not a perfect rule, but it's much more reliable than judging a whole free-text explanation.","它不是完美的规则，但比评判一整段自由文本的解释要可靠得多。"],[158.67,163.66,171,"The second piece is Video-R1, for reasoning about videos.","第二项工作是 Video-R1，用于视频推理。"],[164.01,169.88,171,"A known problem with video models is that they often answer from a single frame and ignore time.","视频模型的一个已知问题是：它们常常只根据单帧作答，忽略了时间信息。"],[170.23,173.22,171,"They'd give the same answer if you shuffled the frames.","即使把帧的顺序打乱，它们也会给出同样的答案。"],[173.57,177.47,171,"Our fix is T-GRPO, temporal GRPO.","我们的解决方案是 T-GRPO，也就是时序 GRPO。"],[177.82,184.25,171,"For each question, the policy answers twice: once with the frames in the right temporal order, the green group.","对每个问题，策略模型回答两次：一次用按正确时间顺序排列的帧，也就是绿色这一组。"],[184.6,188.21,171,"And once with randomly shuffled frames, the blue group.","另一次用随机打乱的帧，也就是蓝色这一组。"],[188.56,191.27,171,"Both groups get the usual rewards.","两组都会得到常规的奖励。"],[191.62,198.03,171,"On top of that there's a temporal reward: the model earns a bonus when it does better on the ordered frames than on the shuffled ones.","在此之上还有一个时序奖励：当模型在有序帧上比在乱序帧上表现更好时，就获得额外奖励。"],[198.38,203.76,171,"So the reward directly encourages the model to actually use temporal information.","所以这个奖励直接鼓励模型真正去利用时间信息。"],[204.11,213.07,171,"That's a nice example of reward design: when there's no unit test, you create a contrast that only a model doing the right thing can win.","这是奖励设计的一个好例子：没有单元测试时，就构造一种对比，只有做对事情的模型才能胜出。"],[214.32,224.45,172,"The third piece is our newest work, HuatuoGPT-3, which asks whether you can adapt a base model to a new domain using RL alone.","第三项是我们最新的工作 HuatuoGPT-3，它探讨能否仅用强化学习让基座模型适应一个新领域。"],[224.8,226.38,172,"Look at the three pipelines.","看这三条流程。"],[226.73,232.38,172,"Classic domain adaptation goes base, continued pre-training, domain SFT, RL.","经典的领域适配流程是：基座、继续预训练、领域 SFT、强化学习。"],[232.73,238.68,172,"That's long, needs domain data at every stage, and SFT imitation narrows exploration.","流程很长，每个阶段都需要领域数据，而且 SFT 的模仿会收窄探索。"],[239.03,250.02,172,"Pure R1-Zero-style RL has been shown for general math and code reasoning, but not for adapting to a new domain, where the model faces a cold start.","纯 R1-Zero 式的强化学习已经在通用数学和代码推理上得到了验证，但没有用于适配新领域，在新领域中模型会面临冷启动。"],[250.37,258.44,172,"OnePO, our method, is one stage of RL with a retiring teacher: the teacher warms up the policy, then steps aside.","我们的方法 OnePO 是带“退休教师”的单阶段强化学习：教师先给策略热身，然后退场。"],[258.79,269.0,172,"On the right, with the same twenty K training samples, HealthBench scores are fifty-nine point eight for pure RL, and sixty-four point five for SFT plus RL.","右边，在相同的两万条训练样本下，HealthBench 分数：纯强化学习 59.8，SFT 加强化学习 64.5。"],[269.35,277.55,172,"And sixty-seven point two for OnePO: two point seven points above SFT plus RL, and seven point four above pure RL.","OnePO 是 67.2：比 SFT 加强化学习高 2.7 分，比纯强化学习高 7.4 分。"],[277.9,288.1,172,"The released HuatuoGPT-3-27B reaches seventy point one on HealthBench, and seventy-one point four on HealthBench Professional.","发布的 HuatuoGPT-3-27B 在 HealthBench 上达到 70.1，在 HealthBench Professional 上达到 71.4。"],[289.35,291.36,173,"How does the retiring teacher work?","“退休教师”是怎么运作的？"],[291.71,299.67,173,"First, why naive mixed-policy RL, mixing teacher outputs into the RL groups, falls short. Two problems.","首先，为什么简单的混合策略强化学习，也就是把教师输出混进强化学习的组里，效果不够好。有两个问题。"],[300.02,307.81,173,"Gradient starvation: the teacher's most informative tokens have low probability under the policy, so they're learned far too slowly.","梯度饥饿：教师最有信息量的 token 在策略下概率很低，所以学得太慢了。"],[308.16,316.5,173,"And teacher-distribution anchoring: if you keep using stale teacher outputs, the policy gets pinned to the teacher and can't improve beyond it.","以及教师分布锚定：如果一直使用过时的教师输出，策略就会被钉在教师身上，无法超越它。"],[316.85,319.57,173,"OnePO's fixes match those two problems.","OnePO 的解决方案正好对应这两个问题。"],[319.92,327.61,173,"Adaptive objective evolution re-weights the objective to learn faster from informative, low-probability teacher tokens.","自适应目标演化会重新加权目标函数，让模型更快地从信息量大、概率低的教师 token 中学习。"],[327.96,333.59,173,"And teacher retirement discards a teacher output as soon as the policy can beat it on reward.","而教师退休机制会在策略的奖励能超过某个教师输出时，立即把它丢弃。"],[333.94,335.82,173,"Look at the rollout groups at the bottom.","看底部的 rollout 组。"],[336.17,339.86,173,"Early on, one teacher sample gives a warm start.","早期，一个教师样本提供热启动。"],[340.21,344.8,173,"In the middle, the policy catches up, and the teacher's weight shrinks.","中期，策略逐渐追上，教师的权重随之缩小。"],[345.15,349.68,173,"Late in training, the teacher is gone, and it's pure on-policy RL.","训练后期，教师退场，变成纯粹的同策略强化学习。"],[350.03,360.95,173,"The data: about twenty thousand medical tasks, half multiple-choice with exact-match rewards, half open-ended scored by a rubric grader model.","数据方面：大约两万个医学任务，一半是采用精确匹配奖励的选择题，一半是由评分细则打分模型评判的开放式问题。"],[362.2,368.47,174,"To close part six: with the right reward design, RL works beyond math, in medicine and video too.","第六部分小结：只要奖励设计得当，强化学习在数学之外同样有效，医学和视频领域也不例外。"],[368.82,372.69,174,"Now the last part. Reasoning is only the first step.","现在进入最后一部分。推理只是第一步。"],[373.04,383.08,174,"In agentic RL, the reward comes from tools, environments, and eventually the physical world, and the model has to act, not just think.","在智能体强化学习中，奖励来自工具、环境，最终来自物理世界，模型必须行动，而不仅仅是思考。"],[384.33,392.33,175,"Here's a nice framing of this transition from Junyang Lin of the Qwen team, in a post called From Reasoning Thinking to Agentic Thinking.","这里有一个对这种转变很好的阐述，来自 Qwen 团队的林俊旸，文章标题是《从“推理式”思考到“智能体式”思考》。"],[392.68,399.79,175,"His argument goes like this. o1 showed that thinking can be a first-class capability you train for.","他的论点是这样的：o1 证明了思考可以成为一种需要专门训练的一等能力。"],[400.14,405.45,175,"R1 showed that this kind of post-training can be reproduced outside the original labs.","R1 证明了这类后训练可以在原始实验室之外被复现。"],[405.8,416.9,175,"So the first half of two thousand twenty-five was mostly about reasoning thinking: how to spend more inference compute, and train it with stronger rewards.","所以二〇二五年上半年主要关注的是推理式思考：如何投入更多推理算力，以及如何用更强的奖励来训练。"],[417.25,425.76,175,"The next question, he argues, is agentic thinking: thinking in order to act, while interacting with an environment.","他认为，下一个问题是智能体式思考：为了行动而思考，同时与环境交互。"],[426.11,430.7,175,"And continuously updating plans based on feedback from the world.","并根据来自世界的反馈不断更新计划。"],[431.05,435.61,175,"That's exactly the shift in reward source we've been tracking all lecture.","这正是我们整堂课一直在追踪的奖励来源的转变。"],[436.86,442.76,176,"Here's a concrete picture of what agentic thinking looks like: reasoning as augmented action.","这是智能体式思考的一个具体图景：把推理当作一种增强的行动。"],[443.11,446.79,176,"The agent observes: you're cooking, and the salt is out.","智能体观察到：你在做菜，盐用完了。"],[447.14,455.1,176,"Then it reasons: the dish should be savoury, so I'll use soy sauce instead, and it's in the cabinet to my right.","然后它推理：这道菜应该是咸鲜味的，所以我改用酱油，酱油在我右手边的柜子里。"],[455.45,463.48,176,"Then it acts: turn right. It observes again: a cabinet and a table. And acts: open the cabinet.","然后它行动：向右转。它再次观察：一个柜子和一张桌子。然后行动：打开柜子。"],[463.83,470.28,176,"The reasoning step isn't an answer to anyone; it's an internal action that makes the next physical action better.","推理这一步并不是给谁的回答；它是一种内部行动，让下一个物理行动做得更好。"],[470.63,474.08,176,"And this is how language generalizes in agents.","语言正是这样在智能体中实现泛化的。"],[474.43,481.53,176,"Knowledge like, soy sauce can replace salt, lets the agent handle a situation it was never trained on.","像“酱油可以代替盐”这样的知识，让智能体能够应对从未训练过的情境。"],[481.88,488.89,176,"You'll see this pattern, interleaving thought, action and observation, in detail in the next lecture on agents.","这种思考、行动、观察交替进行的模式，你会在下一讲关于智能体的内容中详细看到。"],[490.14,493.32,177,"So why is agentic RL so hard to train?","那么，为什么智能体强化学习这么难训练？"],[493.67,499.43,177,"Look at the diagram on top: a trainer, a rollout engine, and environments with tools.","看上面的示意图：一个训练器、一个 rollout 引擎，以及带工具的环境。"],[499.78,506.11,177,"They exchange weights, trajectories, tool calls and observations. And there are six problems.","它们之间交换权重、轨迹、工具调用和观测。这里面有六个问题。"],[506.46,514.57,177,"One, rollouts dominate compute: trajectories can have hundreds of tool calls and over one hundred K tokens.","第一，rollout 占据了大部分算力：轨迹可能包含数百次工具调用和超过十万个 token。"],[514.92,517.56,177,"Generating them eats most of the GPU time.","生成这些轨迹耗费了大部分 GPU 时间。"],[517.91,527.73,177,"Two, long tails: lengths vary wildly, so a synchronous batch waits for its slowest rollout, the problem we saw with async RL.","第二，长尾问题：轨迹长度差异极大，同步批次要等最慢的 rollout，这就是我们在异步强化学习中见过的问题。"],[528.08,533.97,177,"Three, tools are slow and can fail, and asynchronous rollouts make the data off-policy.","第三，工具很慢还可能失败，而异步 rollout 会让数据变成离策略的。"],[534.32,540.91,177,"Four, infrastructure: thousands of isolated sandboxes, and safe execution of model-written code.","第四，基础设施：成千上万个隔离的沙箱，以及安全执行模型写出的代码。"],[541.26,549.96,177,"Five, train-inference mismatch: the training and inference engines compute slightly different token probabilities, which can destabilize RL.","第五，训练与推理不一致：训练引擎和推理引擎算出的 token 概率略有差异，这可能让强化学习变得不稳定。"],[550.31,559.46,177,"Six, credit assignment: one sparse reward at the end of a very long episode, plus new ways to hack the reward through tools.","第六，信用分配：在一段很长的交互结束时只有一个稀疏奖励，还多了通过工具投机奖励的新途径。"],[559.81,565.36,177,"Notice how much of this is systems, not algorithms. That's where the frontier is.","注意，这里面有多少是系统问题，而不是算法问题。前沿正在这里。"],[566.61,572.68,178,"Here's a perspective from Shunyu Yao's essay, The Second Half, that helps explain why.","姚顺雨的文章《下半场》提供了一个视角，有助于解释其中的原因。"],[573.03,580.43,178,"In the first half of AI, progress came from new methods: Transformers, pre-training, RLHF.","在 AI 的上半场，进步来自新方法：Transformer、预训练、RLHF。"],[580.78,583.92,178,"If you invented a better algorithm, you won.","谁发明了更好的算法，谁就赢了。"],[584.27,594.22,178,"In the second half, the bottleneck shifts to defining the tasks: environments, tools, protocols like MCP, skills, and evaluations.","到了下半场，瓶颈转向了定义任务：环境、工具、MCP 这样的协议、技能，以及评测。"],[594.57,597.77,178,"What should we optimize, and how do we measure it?","我们应该优化什么？又该如何衡量？"],[598.12,604.71,178,"Because once RL with a strong prior just works, the recipe is no longer the hard part.","因为一旦有了强先验的强化学习能直接奏效，配方就不再是难点了。"],[605.06,613.29,178,"The hard part is pointing it at the right real-world problems, with rewards that capture what we actually want.","难点在于把它对准正确的现实问题，并用能真正体现我们需求的奖励来引导它。"],[614.54,623.19,179,"Let's end with a discussion, and I want to be clear upfront, as the slide says: these are industry rumours, not confirmed by either lab.","最后我们来做个讨论。我要先说清楚，正如幻灯片所写：这些是业内传闻，两家实验室都没有证实。"],[623.54,626.71,179,"I'm sharing them to provoke thinking, not as facts.","分享它们是为了引发思考，而不是当作事实。"],[627.06,633.49,179,"Bet A, RL first: scale RL in real coding environments, with tests passing as the reward.","赌注 A，强化学习优先：在真实的编程环境中扩展强化学习，以测试通过作为奖励。"],[633.84,640.35,179,"The upside is that the model can find strategies no human showed it, and it scales with compute.","好处是模型能找到人类从未展示过的策略，而且能随算力扩展。"],[640.7,644.69,179,"The downside is reward hacking and huge environment infrastructure.","坏处是奖励投机，以及庞大的环境基础设施。"],[645.04,656.11,179,"Bet B, human priors first: inject expertise through SFT on long, high-quality agent trajectories written or curated by experts, then do RL.","赌注 B，人类先验优先：先用专家编写或筛选的高质量长智能体轨迹做 SFT 注入专业知识，然后再做强化学习。"],[656.46,664.64,179,"The upside is well-behaved agents with good taste. The downside is being bounded by those expert trajectories.","好处是智能体行为规范、品味好。坏处是会受限于那些专家轨迹。"],[664.99,667.84,179,"In reality, both labs surely use both.","实际上，两家实验室肯定都是两者兼用。"],[668.19,672.52,179,"So the real question for you is where the capability comes from.","所以留给你们真正的问题是：能力究竟从何而来。"],[672.87,678.96,179,"Should the prior come from humans or from exploration, and which scales better as tasks get longer?","先验应该来自人类还是来自探索？随着任务变长，哪一种扩展得更好？"],[679.31,685.18,179,"Notice it's the same tension we've seen all lecture: imitation versus incentive.","注意，这和我们整堂课看到的是同一种张力：模仿与激励。"],[686.43,690.35,180,"So why should you work on RL? Look at the timeline at the top.","那么，你为什么应该研究强化学习？看顶部的时间线。"],[690.7,697.32,180,"Pre-training scaled data and models. Distillation let everyone imitate strong teachers.","预训练扩展了数据和模型。蒸馏让每个人都能模仿强大的教师模型。"],[697.67,706.0,180,"Now we're scaling RL, from verifiable tasks to agentic ones, and after that comes embodied RL in the physical world.","现在我们在扩展强化学习，从可验证任务走向智能体任务，再往后是物理世界中的具身强化学习。"],[706.35,708.08,180,"The three boxes give my view.","这三个框代表了我的看法。"],[708.43,715.56,180,"Distillation has peaked: it was cheap and effective after R1, but a student is bounded by its teacher.","蒸馏已经见顶：R1 之后它便宜又有效，但学生会受限于老师。"],[715.91,719.71,180,"The best teachers are closed, and the easy gains are used up.","最好的老师是闭源的，而容易拿到的提升也已经用完了。"],[720.06,729.07,180,"RL drives the next phase: verifiable rewards scale with compute, and agentic RL turns tools and environments into training signal.","强化学习推动下一阶段：可验证奖励能随算力扩展，智能体强化学习则把工具和环境变成训练信号。"],[729.42,734.96,180,"And embodied RL is wide open: robots get reward from the physical world.","而具身强化学习还是一片蓝海：机器人从物理世界中获得奖励。"],[735.31,739.08,180,"Sim-to-real, safe exploration and data efficiency are all unsolved.","仿真到现实的迁移、安全探索和数据效率，都还没有解决。"],[739.43,741.38,180,"The bottom line is practical advice.","底部这一行是实用的建议。"],[741.73,749.9,180,"Learn the RL fundamentals: policy gradients, PPO and GRPO. Learn reward design: verifiers and rubrics.","学习强化学习的基础：策略梯度、PPO 和 GRPO。学习奖励设计：验证器和评分细则。"],[750.25,758.86,180,"And learn RL infrastructure: rollouts and environments. Those three skills will stay valuable for a long time.","再学习强化学习基础设施：rollout 和环境。这三项技能在很长时间内都会很有价值。"],[760.11,764.5,181,"Let's wrap up with one table, which is really the whole lecture.","我们用一张表来收尾，这张表其实就是整堂课的内容。"],[764.85,771.37,181,"SFT learns from human demonstrations, unlocks instruction following, and is bounded by its data.","SFT 从人类示范中学习，解锁了指令遵循能力，但受限于它的数据。"],[771.72,779.83,181,"RLHF and DPO learn from human preferences, and give us models that are helpful, honest and harmless.","RLHF 和 DPO 从人类偏好中学习，带给我们有用、诚实、无害的模型。"],[780.18,784.67,181,"But they suffer from biased reward models and reward hacking.","但它们受困于有偏差的奖励模型和奖励投机。"],[785.02,796.97,181,"RLVR learns from verifiers like answer checkers and tests, and unlocks long chains of thought and self-reflection, but only for checkable tasks.","RLVR 从答案检查器、测试这样的验证器中学习，解锁了长思维链和自我反思，但只适用于可检查的任务。"],[797.32,807.16,181,"Self-verification learns a verifier, checked by a meta-verifier, and unlocks rigorous proofs, as long as the verifier stays ahead of the generator.","自我验证学习一个验证器，并由元验证器来检查它，解锁了严谨的证明，前提是验证器要始终领先于生成器。"],[807.51,813.93,181,"And agentic RL learns from tools and environments, and unlocks acting in the world.","而智能体强化学习从工具和环境中学习，解锁了在世界中行动的能力。"],[814.28,818.01,181,"It's limited mainly by infrastructure and credit assignment.","它主要受限于基础设施和信用分配。"],[818.36,821.71,181,"And the sentence at the bottom is the one to take home.","底部这句话是大家要带回家的。"],[822.06,830.04,181,"From alignment to reasoning to agentic RL, the algorithm barely changes. What changes is the source of the reward.","从对齐到推理，再到智能体强化学习，算法几乎没变。变的是奖励的来源。"],[831.29,837.6,182,"Before we finish, thanks to the courses and people whose materials helped shape this lecture.","在结束之前，感谢那些课程和老师，他们的材料帮助塑造了这一讲。"],[837.95,843.63,182,"That includes Stanford's CS224N, and Danqi Chen's course at Princeton.","其中包括斯坦福的 CS224N，以及普林斯顿陈丹琦老师的课程。"],[843.98,855.54,182,"And Junxian He's slides on large reasoning models, plus the Awesome-o1 collection, which is a great reading list if you want to go deeper.","还有何俊贤老师关于大型推理模型的课件，以及 Awesome-o1 合集，如果你想深入学习，这是一份很棒的阅读清单。"],[856.79,859.13,183,"Here's the first page of references.","这是参考文献的第一页。"],[859.48,871.74,183,"You don't need to read them all, but if a topic today caught your interest, InstructGPT, DPO, DeepSeek-R1 or GRPO, these are the papers to start with.","你不需要全部读完，但如果今天哪个话题引起了你的兴趣，比如 InstructGPT、DPO、DeepSeek-R1 或 GRPO，可以从这些论文开始。"],[872.09,873.73,183,"The slides will be online.","幻灯片会放到网上。"],[874.98,880.02,184,"And the second page of references, covering the rest of the papers cited today.","这是参考文献的第二页，涵盖了今天引用的其余论文。"],[880.37,886.9,184,"Again, use them as a starting point for further reading, or for your final project literature review.","同样，你可以把它们作为进一步阅读的起点，或者用于期末项目的文献综述。"],[888.15,889.52,185,"That's it for today.","今天的内容就到这里。"],[889.87,897.89,185,"Let's recap in one breath: we started with why SFT isn't enough, and built up RLHF and DPO for alignment.","我们一口气回顾一下：我们从为什么 SFT 不够讲起，接着构建了用于对齐的 RLHF 和 DPO。"],[898.24,908.55,185,"We opened up the RL algorithms from PPO to GRPO, and watched verifiable rewards give rise to reasoning models like o1 and DeepSeek-R1.","我们剖析了从 PPO 到 GRPO 的强化学习算法，看到了可验证奖励如何催生出 o1 和 DeepSeek-R1 这样的推理模型。"],[908.9,914.21,185,"And we ended with agentic RL, where the reward comes from the world.","最后讲到了智能体强化学习，在那里奖励来自世界本身。"],[914.56,921.55,185,"Next time, in Lecture seven, we pick up exactly where we stopped: LLM agents and harness engineering.","下一次，在第七讲，我们会从这里接着讲：LLM 智能体与框架工程。"],[921.9,927.9,185,"We'll look at how agents are built around a model, with tools, memory and the harness that runs them.","我们会看看智能体是如何围绕一个模型搭建起来的，包括工具、记忆，以及运行它们的框架。"],[928.25,934.48,185,"And why, as ARC-AGI-3 showed, the harness can matter as much as the model.","以及为什么正如 ARC-AGI-3 所展示的那样，框架可能和模型本身一样重要。"],[934.83,940.74,185,"If you have questions, keep them in mind and bring them along. Thanks, everyone, and see you next time!","如果你有问题，请记下来带到课上。谢谢大家，我们下次见！"]]}]};
